{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening","id":971461,"title":"Emphasizing ambiguity and horror: Gecko's currently unnamed Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T12:31:32-07:00","id":971461,"title":"Emphasizing ambiguity and horror: Gecko's currently unnamed Awakening","content":"I've been wondering if there was a way to accomplish my goals for Mage: The Transgression on a smaller scale, by slightly hacking and nudging Awakening. The primary goal isn't just to make it more fun or flavorful or mad science-y, but to really make it feel like a personal horror game about broken monsters. The most important thing is, what would be the best way to run or hack Mage in order to emphasize the ambiguity and horror of the setting? To really make the players question everything, and to create the genuine possibility that a lot of the principles of the setting are either false or much more complicated.<br /> <br /> Here are my goals/ideas so far: <br /> <br /> \u2022 The main thing I want to do is present being Awakening as a cursed, monstrous condition rather than a blessing or a &quot;higher state&quot; of evolution, make it so that &quot;Awakened&quot; and &quot;Sleepers&quot; are just terms Mages use to feel better about themselves, and close to or more than half of Mages wish secretly or openly that they were normal humans again. <br /> \u2022 Paradox and Obsessions are both much more dangerous and punishing. <br /> \u2022 Archmastery is equivalent to becoming a True Fae- the Mage becomes an utterly inhuman entity. <br /> \u2022 Much of the setting's assumptions are ambiguous or wrong, and the possibility exists that much of what Mages believe is true is true because their disruptive presence in reality forces it to be true. <br /> \u2022 Moral ambiguities of the main conflict are emphasized. The Seers have a genuinely good case for why they're right. <br /> \u2022 As Mages gain power and lose Wisdom, they must take Bans and Banes related to how they can perform magic, like other supernatural creatures. <br /> \u2022 Crossover possibilities are enhanced, with Mage supremacy being actively fought with nerfs. <br /> \u2022 The subjective nature of the Supernal is emphasized, as well as the possibility that it's essentially a shared delusion that Mages can force into reality. Players only have to pick one of their Path's Arcana, and choose any other as their second ruling Arcana. Experiences of the Supernal realms are vastly different and subjective. <br /> \u2022 Some Mages have no Path. They are stereotyped as being more likely to become Scelesti or Banishers, but the truth of this assumption is questionable. <br /> \u2022 A significant and ever-increasing number of Mages Awaken as Gifted Scientists from the Mage Chronicler's Guide. <br /> \u2022 Presumably other stuff I'll think of later. <br /> <br /> Feedback and suggestions are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T23:34:54-07:00","id":971791,"title":"","content":"Here're some more:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Many Mages deliberately try to avoid gaining power, because gaining power inevitably removes the Mage more and more from humanity. Obsessions get stronger, Bans and Banes develop, and ultimately the Mage risks becoming an utterly inhuman Archmaster. <br /> \u2022 Mages are stuck between the risk of higher power and the painful compulsion to seek it- their Obsessions constantly force them to delve into paranormal phenomena and seek knowledge, no matter how much they try to resist. <br /> \u2022 The Nimbus grows more powerful as a Mage gains in power as a representation of their growing distance from humanity, acting similarly to the Wake from Leviathan. <br /> \u2022 It's quite hard to effect powerful supernatural creatures, and some are immune to direct uses of magic entirely. Creativity and problem-solving are key. <br /> \u2022 More pessimistic Mages prefer the terms &quot;Hollow&quot; or &quot;Open&quot; to &quot;Awakened&quot;, because they more accurately describe what happens. A Mage blows a hole in his soul and desperately fills it with chunks of occult symbols, grabbing onto a watchtower to survive having their mind cast into primordial chaos. The &quot;hollow&quot; nature of Mages is why they're so sensitive to the occult and potent with it: they have &quot;open space&quot; with which to connect directly with the supernatural. Obsessions play into this, too: every Mage feels a deep and aching pain, as if they are missing something precious, and Obsessions are an attempt to fill that hole. <br /> \u2022 The factions now have more of a resemblance to the Covenants in Vampire- they primarily exist to help Mages justify and survive their cursed state. <br /> \u2022 The Silver Ladder is sort of equivalent to the Invictus, using elaborate hierarchies and rituals to manage their condition. They try to frame the Awakened state as a honorable burden, something given only to the worthy. Members of this group are most likely to be Lemurians- those who are trying to bring back a lost magical golden age. <br /> \u2022 The Mysterium seek knowledge with a fervor that surpasses that of other Mages. Some seek it for its own sake, while others look for the secrets of the world in the hope of regulating or removing their condition. They study the past to learn from it. Most historically significant Mages, after all, are primarily famous as cautionary tales. <br /> \u2022 The Guardians of the Veil know just how dangerous the supernatural is, especially the volatile powers of their own kind. They dedicate themselves completely to protecting the Whole not just from direct menaces but from knowledge that might lead them down the same self-destructive path the Hollow tread. <br /> \u2022 The Adamantine Arrow are not simply about warfare or strength. They focus on control and refinement as a means of honing mind and body to withstand the ravages of the Awakened condition. Many are in some way ascetic, seeking enough control to keep the fires raging inside them under control. <br /> \u2022 The Free Council are no longer the primary technomages at all. Every order has a fair proportion of scientifically-focused mages and Gifted Scientists. The Council's connection to mortal occult traditions is much more important to them, because their focus is connection: remaining in contact with the mortal world and humanity so as to avoid drifting away from it. <br /> \u2022 Hm, maybe The Hollow Chronicle is a good name for it. <br /> \u2022 No player is allowed to make a character inspired by Dr. Who or Benedict Cumberbatch's Sherlock. Any character who qualifies as a sarcastic british man is to be subject to close ST scrutiny, and is only allowed a maximum of three quips per game. <br /> <br /> ...you know, I just realized that Mage rubs me the wrong way not because I have a problem with power fantasies but because I've always identified with monsters so much, and seeing something so prominent in my favorite game about monsters that's so...un-monstrous is jarring. Mages just seem like...the cool kids, the effortlessly popular ones who sail through life while the rest of us are scraping around in the dirt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T23:51:15-07:00","id":971797,"title":"","content":"Who knows, this could work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-18-2016, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:35:05-07:00","id":971806,"title":"","content":"Question? Have you actually read the book? Or just trying to port over the rules to Mage the Ascension or your fan based game? Do you have Imperial Mysteries? Do you have any clue how archmastery works? Do you understand IM is just a baseline? Given Archmages will have a complete rewrite in the end? Just use the conversion guide book and roll would be my advice if you can't answer my former questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-18-2016, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:42:14-07:00","id":971810,"title":"","content":"My aim is pretty clear: I'm trying to emphasize the personal horror elements as much as possible to make Mages feel genuinely monstrous and cursed, not kewl magic superheroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:53:18-07:00","id":971814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971810#post971810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My aim is pretty clear: I'm trying to emphasize the personal horror elements as much as possible to make Mages feel genuinely monstrous and cursed, not kewl magic superheroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Explain. What are you actually asking for? Given ALL Maw mages are monsters by default. Superheroes? Show me. They can be powerful but not from 21Jumpstreet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:17:27-07:00","id":971823,"title":"","content":"Have you thought about just making your own game from scratch? Seems like less of a headache then trying to bend entire other system to fit into the tiny box that you so desperately feel it needs to fit into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T02:07:46-07:00","id":971840,"title":"","content":"My 20 cents: i think that a Banisher Chronichle could satisfy you much more, with less work.<br /> Keep Integrity over Wisdom: each spell is a potentiatl breaking point, so as mage sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T02:16:27-07:00","id":971844,"title":"","content":"Do you, like, have players or a group that you're preparing this to run for, or is this some kind of strange exercise that exists in a vacuum? It's okay to just not like Mage. You don't have to formulate another game just as a counterpoint to the game that was published. You can play the other games without mages ever showing up or existing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T03:02:50-07:00","id":971850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971844#post971844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You don't have to formulate another game just as a counterpoint to the game that was published.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently she does. See also: 'The Lightning Chronicle'.<br /> You should also be prepared for all future mentions of Mage to be referring to her homebrew setting without her actually saying so until called on it. That bit was in her signature for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 09-30-2016, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T03:04:43-07:00","id":971851,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda surprised you've left out the Abyss. That's the realm of ambiguity and horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 More pessimistic Mages prefer the terms &quot;Hollow&quot; or &quot;Open&quot; to &quot;Awakened&quot;, because they more accurately describe what happens. A Mage blows a hole in his soul and desperately fills it with chunks of occult symbols, grabbing onto a watchtower to survive having their mind cast into primordial chaos. The &quot;hollow&quot; nature of Mages is why they're so sensitive to the occult and potent with it: they have &quot;open space&quot; with which to connect directly with the supernatural. Obsessions play into this, too: every Mage feels a deep and aching pain, as if they are missing something precious, and Obsessions are an attempt to fill that hole. </div> </div> </div>That's quite interesting. I really like 'Open' it has a scientology vibe to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 The factions now have more of a resemblance to the Covenants in Vampire- they primarily exist to help Mages justify and survive their cursed state. </div> </div> </div>I think these are really interesting ideas. I particularly like the SL version. I wonder if there couldn't be a bit of countering the Abyss in there. I mean, if the Abyss is about contradiction and paradox then it could make sense to make your organisation as unambiguous as possible. That does seem to be an undercurrent in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T03:40:50-07:00","id":971857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971810#post971810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My aim is pretty clear: I'm trying to emphasize the personal horror elements as much as possible to make Mages feel genuinely monstrous and cursed, not kewl magic superheroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be silly! Mage isn't about Kewl Magic Superheroes!<br /> It's about Kewl Magic Supervillains.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I think the best way to add more horror to Mage is to emphasise the horror Mages wreak instead of that which they themselves suffer. Even the nicest Mage can and likely will invite horror through their actions, whether through Paradox or other means. You shouldn't punish the acquisition of power, but instead encourage its abuse. Then show them the suffering they have brought and the karma they have earned.<br /> Mages aren't monsters because of what they are, but because of what they do.<br /> ------<br /> I do have suggestions for if you want to continue with your current plans though.<br /> Consider the possibility that there is no Supernal, and that the Abyss is the source of all Magic.<br /> Also consider using the Banisher rules, or some variation of them, for most if not all Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T04:18:09-07:00","id":971871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wondering if there was a way to accomplish my goals for Mage: The Transgression on a smaller scale, by slightly hacking and nudging Awakening. The primary goal isn't just to make it more fun or flavorful or mad science-y, but to really make it feel like a personal horror game about broken monsters. The most important thing is, what would be the best way to run or hack Mage in order to emphasize the ambiguity and horror of the setting? To really make the players question everything, and to create the genuine possibility that a lot of the principles of the setting are either false or much more complicated.<br /> <br /> Here are my goals/ideas so far:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The main thing I want to do is present being Awakening as a cursed, monstrous condition rather than a blessing or a &quot;higher state&quot; of evolution, make it so that &quot;Awakened&quot; and &quot;Sleepers&quot; are just terms Mages use to feel better about themselves, and close to or more than half of Mages wish secretly or openly that they were normal humans again.<br /> \u2022 Paradox and Obsessions are both much more dangerous and punishing.<br /> \u2022 Archmastery is equivalent to becoming a True Fae- the Mage becomes an utterly inhuman entity.<br /> \u2022 Much of the setting's assumptions are ambiguous or wrong, and the possibility exists that much of what Mages believe is true is true because their disruptive presence in reality forces it to be true.<br /> \u2022 Moral ambiguities of the main conflict are emphasized. The Seers have a genuinely good case for why they're right.<br /> \u2022 As Mages gain power and lose Wisdom, they must take Bans and Banes related to how they can perform magic, like other supernatural creatures.<br /> \u2022 Crossover possibilities are enhanced, with Mage supremacy being actively fought with nerfs.<br /> \u2022 The subjective nature of the Supernal is emphasized, as well as the possibility that it's essentially a shared delusion that Mages can force into reality. Players only have to pick one of their Path's Arcana, and choose any other as their second ruling Arcana. Experiences of the Supernal realms are vastly different and subjective.<br /> \u2022 Some Mages have no Path. They are stereotyped as being more likely to become Scelesti or Banishers, but the truth of this assumption is questionable.<br /> \u2022 A significant and ever-increasing number of Mages Awaken as Gifted Scientists from the Mage Chronicler's Guide.<br /> \u2022 Presumably other stuff I'll think of later.<br /> <br /> Feedback and suggestions are welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to quote (i hope) Exalted here but &quot;The surest test of a man's character is to give him power over another&quot;. You have the horror element right in mage it is about thinking your a super cool magical hero until your first Paradox happens, and you watch as the Abyss takes the time to personally bend you over, tentacle screw you, then high five the next spawn of madness as they take their turn violating your body, soul, and magic. What's worse is even though you know your letting horrors that would munch on sanity, and wisdom like potato chips have their way with you, your addicted to the power you get from that. You know that as your wisdom keeps sliding down like a prostitutes clothes, you can't help but leaving yourself open and bare to these horrors from beyond because of the power you can get doing so! And you know that when your done with your slide into nothingness not only will you be used up, beaten up, broken, and unfixable but other mages will terminate you like the rabid dog you became. Yet you can't stop! You have things you want to do people you want to protect, and that is how you justify letting that happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T07:19:47-07:00","id":971916,"title":"","content":"I think a great deal of what you're trying to accomplish here is already accomplished by the setting as-written. More specific responses to come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T07:52:34-07:00","id":971927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wondering if there was a way to accomplish my goals for Mage: The Transgression on a smaller scale, by slightly hacking and nudging Awakening. The primary goal isn't just to make it more fun or flavorful or mad science-y, but to really make it feel like a personal horror game about broken monsters. The most important thing is, what would be the best way to run or hack Mage in order to emphasize the ambiguity and horror of the setting? To really make the players question everything, and to create the genuine possibility that a lot of the principles of the setting are either false or much more complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>So right away, you're asking about how to make Mage more of a personal horror game (which it is) by introducing themes that are already present. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 The main thing I want to do is present being Awakening as a cursed, monstrous condition rather than a blessing or a &quot;higher state&quot; of evolution, make it so that &quot;Awakened&quot; and &quot;Sleepers&quot; are just terms Mages use to feel better about themselves, and close to or more than half of Mages wish secretly or openly that they were normal humans again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, being Awakened <i>is</i> a monstrous Condition, and &quot;Awakened&quot; and &quot;Sleepers&quot; <i>are</i> just terms that Mages made up. And I would argue that most Mages <i>do</i> wish to be human, so much so that they are almost all in pretty deep denial about the fact that they're monsters. If you want to play Mages who are fully aware of their monstrosity, you could just play as Banishers. But, if you really want the Awakened to lament their Awakened natures, that's an easy thing to accomplish. Just put that in your setting document and bam, done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Paradox and Obsessions are both much more dangerous and punishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsessions aren't punishing as part of a general 2e design philosophy of mechanically encouraging player behavior with carrots, not sticks. By the fluff, Obsessions are something Mages are constantly plagued by and can only resist with great effort and discipline. Mechanically, you award Beats for pursuing your Obsessions so that players are encouraged to pursue them. If you want to add a stick, I suppose you could make players have to spend willpower or succeed a Resolve + Composure roll or something to resist an opportunity to pursue an Obsession. As for Paradox, Paradox is pretty dangerous already. It's more dangerous to reality than it is to the Mage herself, and that's part of the horror of Mage. Every Paradox is your fault, for knowingly using more magic than you could safely handle. Now you have a choice, take responsibility for that mistake and suffer resistant damage and potentially a Condition, or force that responsibility on the world around you, keeping your own body and soul safe but damaging reality itself in the process and risking your spell twisting into something truly dangerous in ways you didn't intend it to be. If you insist on making it harsher though, just adjust the Paradox dice by Gnosis progression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Archmastery is equivalent to becoming a True Fae- the Mage becomes an utterly inhuman entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Much of the setting's assumptions are ambiguous or wrong, and the possibility exists that much of what Mages believe is true is true because their disruptive presence in reality forces it to be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Moral ambiguities of the main conflict are emphasized. The Seers have a genuinely good case for why they're right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 As Mages gain power and lose Wisdom, they must take Bans and Banes related to how they can perform magic, like other supernatural creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Innured spells are pretty much Mage's version of Banes from Vampire. You could expand them slightly so that instead of (or in addition to) making the spell always a Paradox risk, the Mage gains some kind of ban-like weakness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Crossover possibilities are enhanced, with Mage supremacy being actively fought with nerfs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to touch this one, personally. Crossover &quot;balance&quot; is really not my jam, but have fun with that if you decide to go that route.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 The subjective nature of the Supernal is emphasized, as well as the possibility that it's essentially a shared delusion that Mages can force into reality. Players only have to pick one of their Path's Arcana, and choose any other as their second ruling Arcana. Experiences of the Supernal realms are vastly different and subjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is already the case that the Supernal might be a shared delusion that Mages force on to reality, and if you compare the descriptions of the Watchtowers from various Dark Eras, you'll see that it is expeienced differently by different mages, albeit on more of a cultural scale than a personal scale. As for your house rule about Paths, looks like you've already got that figured out, so just roll with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Some Mages have no Path. They are stereotyped as being more likely to become Scelesti or Banishers, but the truth of this assumption is questionable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure this is already the case, though it's quite rare. If you want it to be more common thought, it can be. Again, that change is as simple as noting it down in your setting document.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 A significant and ever-increasing number of Mages Awaken as Gifted Scientists from the Mage Chronicler's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't help you there, haven't read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-18-2016, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:15:24-07:00","id":971931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Many Mages deliberately try to avoid gaining power, because gaining power inevitably removes the Mage more and more from humanity. Obsessions get stronger, Bans and Banes develop, and ultimately the Mage risks becoming an utterly inhuman Archmaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, most Mages are too driven by Obsession and desire for knowledge/power to have this outlook. It sounds again like this desire could be served by playing Banishers, but if you want this to be how Mages see it, just put that in your setting doc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Mages are stuck between the risk of higher power and the painful compulsion to seek it- their Obsessions constantly force them to delve into paranormal phenomena and seek knowledge, no matter how much they try to resist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already very, very much the case. Like, it's the main premise of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 The Nimbus grows more powerful as a Mage gains in power as a representation of their growing distance from humanity, acting similarly to the Wake from Leviathan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already the case. Have you not read the Nimbus rules?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 It's quite hard to effect powerful supernatural creatures, and some are immune to direct uses of magic entirely. Creativity and problem-solving are key.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty easy to accomplish, just add Supernatural Tolerance to Withstand. (Maybe other Mages don't gain this benefit so you can still have Mage-on-Mage magic fights). Mages are going to have a very difficult time affecting all but the weakest of supers under this house rule, but that sounds like exactly what you want so that shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 More pessimistic Mages prefer the terms &quot;Hollow&quot; or &quot;Open&quot; to &quot;Awakened&quot;, because they more accurately describe what happens. A Mage blows a hole in his soul and desperately fills it with chunks of occult symbols, grabbing onto a watchtower to survive having their mind cast into primordial chaos. The &quot;hollow&quot; nature of Mages is why they're so sensitive to the occult and potent with it: they have &quot;open space&quot; with which to connect directly with the supernatural. Obsessions play into this, too: every Mage feels a deep and aching pain, as if they are missing something precious, and Obsessions are an attempt to fill that hole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! Put it in the setting doc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 The factions now have more of a resemblance to the Covenants in Vampire- they primarily exist to help Mages justify and survive their cursed state. <br /> \u2022 The Silver Ladder is sort of equivalent to the Invictus, using elaborate hierarchies and rituals to manage their condition. They try to frame the Awakened state as a honorable burden, something given only to the worthy. Members of this group are most likely to be Lemurians- those who are trying to bring back a lost magical golden age. <br /> \u2022 The Mysterium seek knowledge with a fervor that surpasses that of other Mages. Some seek it for its own sake, while others look for the secrets of the world in the hope of regulating or removing their condition. They study the past to learn from it. Most historically significant Mages, after all, are primarily famous as cautionary tales. <br /> \u2022 The Guardians of the Veil know just how dangerous the supernatural is, especially the volatile powers of their own kind. They dedicate themselves completely to protecting the Whole not just from direct menaces but from knowledge that might lead them down the same self-destructive path the Hollow tread. <br /> \u2022 The Adamantine Arrow are not simply about warfare or strength. They focus on control and refinement as a means of honing mind and body to withstand the ravages of the Awakened condition. Many are in some way ascetic, seeking enough control to keep the fires raging inside them under control. <br /> \u2022 The Free Council are no longer the primary technomages at all. Every order has a fair proportion of scientifically-focused mages and Gifted Scientists. The Council's connection to mortal occult traditions is much more important to them, because their focus is connection: remaining in contact with the mortal world and humanity so as to avoid drifting away from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're just describing the Orders pretty much exactly as they're presented in 2e, except the part about the Mysterium looking for a cure. Most Mages by default aren't self-aware enough to want to be cured.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Hm, maybe The Hollow Chronicle is a good name for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>K.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 No player is allowed to make a character inspired by Dr. Who or Benedict Cumberbatch's Sherlock. Any character who qualifies as a sarcastic british man is to be subject to close ST scrutiny, and is only allowed a maximum of three quips per game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooookayy, I'm just going to... Walk away now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-18-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:45:06-07:00","id":971945,"title":"","content":"I'm aware that a lot of what I'm describing is already present in the text, what I'm working on is emphasizing it. That's why I'm considering doing this instead of a full remake (the other reason is laziness).<br /> <br /> Yes, making a totally new game would probably be best, but no one would play it, and it's a shitload of work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-01-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:13:12-07:00","id":971957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971945#post971945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware that a lot of what I'm describing is already present in the text, what I'm working on is emphasizing it. That's why I'm considering doing this instead of a full remake (the other reason is laziness).</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, I think what you're perceiving as misplaced emphasis is merely the result of the text being written from a Mage's perspective. Mages are presented as these awesome higher beings that everyone should want to be because that's how Mages want to see themselves. All you have to do is take a step back and look at it from a more objective standpoint and you see that they're terrifying, dangerous monsters. The Banishers are presented as insane for their self-loathing, but the thing is they're <i>right</i>. With their human Integrity, they have a clearer view of what Supernal magic really is than any Mage; they are the ones with the objective view, and what they see traumatizes the hell out of them, it scars their very souls. Mages are horrifying, and that horror is only made all the more frightening by the fact that they are so utterly oblivious to it.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I don't know why this is such a sticking point for so many people when it comes to Mage specifically. Every line presents its monsters as awesome. Vampire tells you &quot;hey, you may be Damned, but at least you'll be young and beautiful for ever. Besides, you can't go to Hell if you never die!&quot; Werewolf tells you &quot;We're the righteous inheritors of a sacred duty to protect the world by maintaing the border between spirit and flesh.&quot; The books making it look awesome to be a monster is nothing new. The horror has always come in the form of that fridge logic &quot;Wait... What are we <i>doing</i>?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:08:37-07:00","id":971984,"title":"","content":"Though I agree with you in general I don't think you can actually claim that Banishers have an objective opinion about magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:37:01-07:00","id":972000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971984#post971984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I agree with you in general I don't think you can actually claim that Banishers have an objective opinion about magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, everyone has biases. But Banishers are essentially mages with a human perspective. It may not be objective, but it is biased in ways that reveal truths about magic that Awakened are not comfortable with. Their perspective is the more useful from which to judge Mages' monstrosity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:43:00-07:00","id":972005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971945#post971945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...damn it, I was needlessly confrontational and combative again. Great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll bite. You wrote this out, which means you realized it before actually making this post. <br /> That means you could have corrected the post in question silently. Instead, you just let it stand and made an addendum to call special attention to it. <br /> Why? This is just a really weird thing to pointedly call attention to instead of fixing it, which one would expect if you <i>actually</i> had a problem with your own tone/attitude/approach.<br /> <br /> On-topic: You don't need a new game, you need a setting doc. Everything you want is already present and the mechanics reflect it to an extent already. Minor mechanical changes and a setting doc should resolve the issues you have with the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:17:54-07:00","id":972026,"title":"","content":"I said it earlier: try a banisher only story , or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:35:34-07:00","id":972035,"title":"","content":"&quot;Pretty easy to accomplish, just add Supernatural Tolerance to Withstand.&quot;<br /> <br /> This should have been he default rule and I'm not sure why it wasn't right in the core book?<br /> <br /> Anyways I kind of like the Banishers perpective, it adds an interesting twist.<br /> <br /> I think the horror is more obvious in the other lines then mage.<br /> <br /> Vampire your a blood sucking being that hunts humans and some of whom use blood magic. No other explaination needed.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, your an inhuman shape shifter who can be driven into a rage so severe you hulk out and go on a killing/destruction spree, plus you hunt sentient beings.<br /> <br /> Promeathan your artificially made oddity that poisons the enviroment and drives people to behavior irrationally.<br /> <br /> Mummy is a dead body that pretends its alive every once in awhile, who likes to collect stuff and who spends most of its time in Duat a hellish place, that might be a lower depths plane.<br /> <br /> Demon, your a fallen cyberangel you takes peoples lives for your own by pacts.<br /> <br /> Sin Eater's have a creepy voyeristic ghost fucker inside and when they die someone else takes their place.<br /> <br /> Changelings are kindnapped, tortured, and transformed, only to escape and live in fear of those who would drag it back, all while dealing with an inhuman copy cat who stole your life, and while dealing with semireal delusions every day for the rest of your life. Horror is obvious there too.<br /> <br /> Mage on the other hand, the horror isn't obvious, its extremely subtle, its the horror of how power corrupts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:36:56-07:00","id":972037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972035#post972035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty easy to accomplish, just add Supernatural Tolerance to Withstand.<br /> <br /> This should have been he default rule and I'm not sure why it wasn't right in the core book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if you actually <i>try</i> it, you'll find it means magic only works on Sleepers. Ever.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:55:33-07:00","id":972049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972035#post972035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Pretty easy to accomplish, just add Supernatural Tolerance to Withstand.&quot;<br /> <br /> This should have been he default rule and I'm not sure why it wasn't right in the core book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave has said it was at one point during playtesting, and what they found was that it made affecting supernaturals (including other Mages and ephemeral entities) with magic nearly impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972035#post972035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways I kind of like the Banishers perpective, it adds an interesting twist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Banishers. I've said before that I see Kreia from KotOR 2 as a Banisher, and she is one of my favorite villains from anything ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972035#post972035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the horror is more obvious in the other lines then mage.<br /> <br /> Vampire your a blood sucking being that hunts humans and some of whom use blood magic. No other explaination needed.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, your an inhuman shape shifter who can be driven into a rage so severe you hulk out and go on a killing/destruction spree, plus you hunt sentient beings.<br /> <br /> Promeathan your artificially made oddity that poisons the enviroment and drives people to behavior irrationally.<br /> <br /> Mummy is a dead body that pretends its alive every once in awhile, who likes to collect stuff and who spends most of its time in Duat a hellish place, that might be a lower depths plane.<br /> <br /> Demon, your a fallen cyberangel you takes peoples lives for your own by pacts.<br /> <br /> Sin Eater's have a creepy voyeristic ghost fucker inside and when they die someone else takes their place.<br /> <br /> Changelings are kindnapped, tortured, and transformed, only to escape and live in fear of those who would drag it back, all while dealing with an inhuman copy cat who stole your life, and while dealing with semireal delusions every day for the rest of your life. Horror is obvious there too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all in how you present it. I could just as easily say that in Mage you're a mortal handed the power of a god that literally unmakes reality when you mess up, with no instruction manual and an insatiable drive to test the limits of your power.<br /> <br /> On a different note, it has just occurred to me that The Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya is a Mage story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972035#post972035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage on the other hand, the horror isn't obvious, its extremely subtle, its the horror of how power corrupts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's as obvious or as subtle as you want to make it. Same could be said of the other lines, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-18-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T13:35:54-07:00","id":972099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's all in how you present it. I could just as easily say that in Mage you're a mortal handed the power of a god that literally unmakes reality when you mess up, with no instruction manual and an insatiable drive to test the limits of your power.On a different note, it has just occurred to me that The Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya is a Mage story. </div> </div> </div>Most magi are given pretty extrensive training. And at least initially they're not that powerful.<br /> <br /> Also, in Haruhi's case who do you think is the Mage? There's a divide between the person with the power and the person with the actual control. Assuming that it's not intended to be a narrative double bluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T13:49:50-07:00","id":972105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972099#post972099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most magi are given pretty extrensive training. And at least initially they're not that powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication of the power stat being Gnosis is that you have the power from the beginning, it's just a matter of knowing how to tap into it. And Mages training Mages rings of the blind leading the blind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972099#post972099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in Haruhi's case who do you think is the Mage? There's a divide between the person with the power and the person with the actual control. Assuming that it's not intended to be a narrative double bluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haruhi. It's not a perfect analogy, but yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:20:58-07:00","id":972125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Mages training Mages rings of the blind leading the blind. </div> </div> </div>Mage society clearly does change over time, however slowly, they do still learn from previous mistakes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Haruhi. It's not a perfect analogy, but yeah. </div> </div> </div>I was going to say Kyon is a pretty good analogy. He even gets asked if he'd like all the weirdness to go, and he says no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:28:57-07:00","id":972285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972049#post972049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave has said it was at one point during playtesting, and what they found was that it made affecting supernaturals (including other Mages and ephemeral entities) with magic nearly impossible.<br /> <br /> <br /> I love Banishers. I've said before that I see Kreia from KotOR 2 as a Banisher, and she is one of my favorite villains from anything ever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's all in how you present it. I could just as easily say that in Mage you're a mortal handed the power of a god that literally unmakes reality when you mess up, with no instruction manual and an insatiable drive to test the limits of your power.<br /> <br /> On a different note, it has just occurred to me that The Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya is a Mage story.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's as obvious or as subtle as you want to make it. Same could be said of the other lines, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div> By subtle I mean less obvious to most people compared to people. <br /> <br /> I mean no other game line keeps getting people asking where's the horror like Mage does, I really had to think about it personally, because its not obvious at all, and the fact that Mage is the only CoD gameline that gets this question consistantly from people backs me up on that.<br /> <br /> No one asks where's the horror in Changeling, Werewolf, Vampire, Mummy, Demon, Giest, Hunter, or Promeathan. Heck people figured it out really easily for Deviant already and its not even out yet.<br /> <br /> Mage the other hands gets this question all the time. The horror is there, but its alot subtler then other gamelines.<br /> <br /> Now in an individual game you can easily play up the horror of Mage, set up situations with aton of collatoral damage, have alot of abyssal creatures, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:35:34-07:00","id":972286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972285#post972285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By subtle I mean less obvious to most people compared to people.<br /> <br /> I mean no other game line keeps getting people asking where's the horror like Mage does, I really had to think about it personally, because its not obvious at all, and the fact that Mage is the only CoD gameline that gets this question consistantly from people backs me up on that.<br /> <br /> No one asks where's the horror in Changeling, Werewolf, Vampire, Mummy, Demon, Giest, Hunter, or Promeathan. Heck people figured it out really easily for Deviant already and its not even out yet.<br /> <br /> Mage the other hands gets this question all the time. The horror is there, but its alot subtler then other gamelines.<br /> <br /> Now in an individual game you can easily play up the horror of Mage, set up situations with aton of collatoral damage, have alot of abyssal creatures, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling got it a <i>lot</i> before Second Edition. Geist still gets it every now and then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:43:02-07:00","id":972739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971957#post971957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, I think what you're perceiving as misplaced emphasis is merely the result of the text being written from a Mage's perspective. Mages are presented as these awesome higher beings that everyone should want to be because that's how Mages want to see themselves. All you have to do is take a step back and look at it from a more objective standpoint and you see that they're terrifying, dangerous monsters. The Banishers are presented as insane for their self-loathing, but the thing is they're <i>right</i>. With their human Integrity, they have a clearer view of what Supernal magic really is than any Mage; they are the ones with the objective view, and what they see traumatizes the hell out of them, it scars their very souls. Mages are horrifying, and that horror is only made all the more frightening by the fact that they are so utterly oblivious to it.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I don't know why this is such a sticking point for so many people when it comes to Mage specifically. Every line presents its monsters as awesome. Vampire tells you &quot;hey, you may be Damned, but at least you'll be young and beautiful for ever. Besides, you can't go to Hell if you never die!&quot; Werewolf tells you &quot;We're the righteous inheritors of a sacred duty to protect the world by maintaing the border between spirit and flesh.&quot; The books making it look awesome to be a monster is nothing new. The horror has always come in the form of that fridge logic &quot;Wait... What are we <i>doing</i>?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you know, that's kind of a good point. Vampire 2e, which I love, is written from a very pro-vampire perspective. I just feel like the audience is already accustomed to see the &quot;curse&quot; aspect of vampirism, whereas having magic powers and being Literally Neo isn't something people automatically perceive as monstrous, so it takes some more work to make it so. <br /> <br /> Also, a lot of the lines aren't nearly that positive. Changeling, Mummy, and Demon hit the notes of &quot;this really kind of sucks but I guess you can make the best of it&quot; that I'm looking for, and Promethean is honestly too negative about being a Created for me.<br /> <br /> I can see Geist, but how the hell could someone not see the horror in Changeling?<br /> <br /> And this isn't a new game, it's a hack. I still genuinely think that Mage: The Transgression would be a much better fit for ChroD, but even if I actually write it out that won't magically insert it into canon. I've decided it's easier to just look for a compromise that would let me enjoy and use the existing Mage material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-19-2016, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:55:19-07:00","id":972749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972739#post972739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this isn't a new game, it's a hack. I still genuinely think that Mage: The Transgression would be a much better fit for ChroD...</div> </div> </div> </div>A sentiment shared by vanishingly few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:05:21-07:00","id":972754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972739#post972739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this isn't a new game, it's a hack. I still genuinely think that Mage: The Transgression would be a much better fit for ChroD, but even if I actually write it out that won't magically insert it into canon. I've decided it's easier to just look for a compromise that would let me enjoy and use the existing Mage material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kinda curious, but what <i>do</i> you like about Mage as written? I've seen you talk about all the things you want to change, but what do you like as is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:20:53-07:00","id":972768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972754#post972754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda curious, but what <i>do</i> you like about Mage as written? I've seen you talk about all the things you want to change, but what do you like as is?</div> </div> </div> </div>The color, style and point size of the font is my guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T20:35:18-07:00","id":972905,"title":"","content":"So: does anyone have any suggestions on how to run/play/write up a setting document/whatever to emphasize the horror and the broken-ness of Mages as much as possible? In thinking Promethean is actually a good inspiration: Promethean is about having a fire burning inside you, and I can't think of any better way to describe how I want to present the condition of being a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T20:43:35-07:00","id":972911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972905#post972905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So: does anyone have any suggestions on how to run/play/write up a setting document/whatever to emphasize the horror and the broken-ness of Mages as much as possible? In thinking Promethean is actually a good inspiration: Promethean is about having a fire burning inside you, and I can't think of any better way to describe how I want to present the condition of being a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you could start your own game from the ground up. It would probably be easier then trying to twist someone else's work into a shape you find more desirable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T21:08:19-07:00","id":972924,"title":"","content":"A setting document is purely a page or several detailing how you want to run/play the game you envision as an ST. For example, say I'm running a Mage game wherein I want the players to awaken during the game and not already be mages. To emphasise this, I might say that merits can't be swapped into gnosis and that order/consilia status can't be purchased during creation. Or, in another game, I might want to heavily emphasise that being a Mage is bollocks and that the abyss is always working to counter a Mage's work, so in my setting document I house rule that paradox is always a minimum of one dice and can't be reduced to chance die. <br /> <br /> That being said, you should also make it clear in your setting document that you have a strong dislike for pretty much every core conceit of Mage and would much rather be playing a hybrid of Genius that emphasises how much being a Mage sucked. If I was uninformed and sat down at your table to play Mage, I'd likely leave the table once I realised your vision of Mage was nothing like the game I intended to join. If I was in the mood to play a game involving having everything I do end up with me sucking and weird science, I'd have looked for a Promethean game :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T21:09:10-07:00","id":972925,"title":"","content":"It seems like there's a disagreement between people who think Mage isn't in-your-face horror enough and people who feel it's subtly very horrific indeed. For my own part, I'm pretty happy with Mage's horror level right where it is - whatever anyone else deems it to be. I like that the mage's temptation to push his limits is mirrored in how the mechanics tempt the player, but I also like that the choice to play someone who is overcome by hubris or someone who is merely tempted but steadfastly resists is ultimately firmly in the player's hands rather than being imposed from on high. I mean, if I wanted to play Fucked-Up Guy: The Cursening, I could be playing something else. But I am not playing something else. HMM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T21:30:43-07:00","id":972929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972905#post972905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So: does anyone have any suggestions on how to run/play/write up a setting document/whatever to emphasize the horror and the broken-ness of Mages as much as possible? In thinking Promethean is actually a good inspiration: Promethean is about having a fire burning inside you, and I can't think of any better way to describe how I want to present the condition of being a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Increase the effect of Paradox. I'd look of Dark Heresy Parales of the warp, include effects like summoning creatures of the Abyss that attack, and ravage the world and mages.<br /> 2. remove the ability to target more than one person with an attack spell, instead if you want to hit multiple people with a damaging spell you need to make it an AOE, and play up collateral damage. Give them the feeling that every time they drop a spell it could turn into Hiroshima and they will have to live with the consequences.<br /> 3. Make them face the consequences from lives destroyed, homes burned down, and the guilt from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T01:07:43-07:00","id":972986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972905#post972905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So: does anyone have any suggestions on how to run/play/write up a setting document/whatever to emphasize the horror and the broken-ness of Mages as much as possible? In thinking Promethean is actually a good inspiration: Promethean is about having a fire burning inside you, and I can't think of any better way to describe how I want to present the condition of being a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would just use the book without changing anything because that's already represented really well by Obsession.<br /> <br /> It's really bizarre that you keep complaining that Mage doesn't suit you and then you ask us how to stick stuff into Mage and then it turns out that stuff is already in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-20-2016, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T03:22:12-07:00","id":973015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972986#post972986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would just use the book without changing anything because that's already represented really well by Obsession.<br /> <br /> It's really bizarre that you keep complaining that Mage doesn't suit you and then you ask us how to stick stuff into Mage and then it turns out that stuff is already in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he wants to make it more obvious rather than subtle. <br /> <br /> Ohh hey, have the first thing they do be hunt down a wisdom 0 mage with starting stats! Have that fallen mage seem like a walking nuke with random &quot;lightning&quot; arcing from him that hits with random arcana 5 effects on anything it touches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T03:38:28-07:00","id":973022,"title":"","content":"It isn't subtle though, it's right there in the text. It looks like willful ignorance to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T04:18:16-07:00","id":973028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973022#post973022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't subtle though, it's right there in the text. It looks like willful ignorance to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is subtle though. It slowly builds up, rather than be in your face, that you are in fact a monster. Slowly so that Ammon who started off thinking that Mind magic was a blasphemy eventually learns it and uses it because as his wisdom slips away he stops caring that manipulating others minds or controlling them sounds like the Devil's path. He justifies it as what needs to be done, what he has to do to explore magics connection to the divine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T04:25:28-07:00","id":973032,"title":"","content":"I think Mrmdubois meant in the context of the Mage book, not within the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:19:25-07:00","id":973056,"title":"","content":"That's exactly what I meant. It seems like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> keeps making the complaint that this or that isn't in Mage or heavily emphasized, but most of it actually is and if you want emphasis that's the ST's job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T08:27:01-07:00","id":973151,"title":"","content":"Okay, I dislike house rules. Especially when people use masses of house rules to shoehorn a system rather than using something more fitting.<br /> <br /> But pretty much every sub-forum here is full of house rules. Most seem to have at least one system re-write somewhere. This sub-forum even has another re-write on the first page that people are actually being helpful with.<br /> <br /> \u200bYes, Mage has a lot of what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> wants by default. The title says &quot;emphasizing&quot; so I assume he wants more. There is nothing wrong with wanting more or a different emphasis.<br /> <br /> Can people please either be helpful or just ignore the thread? The thread does not affect you in any way, shape, or form unless you actually plan on running his modified system.<br /> <br /> I'd rather be part of a community that ignores things they dislike but isn't hurting anyone than a community that dogpiles and attacks people over inconsequential things.<br /> <br /> Someone said earlier that he brings it into other threads. Can't we just worry about that when it happens instead of being dicks to someone who wants help in a thread that isn't hurting anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:16:05-07:00","id":973169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wondering if there was a way to accomplish my goals for Mage: The Transgression on a smaller scale, by slightly hacking and nudging Awakening. The primary goal isn't just to make it more fun or flavorful or mad science-y, but to really make it feel like a personal horror game about broken monsters. The most important thing is, what would be the best way to run or hack Mage in order to emphasize the ambiguity and horror of the setting? To really make the players question everything, and to create the genuine possibility that a lot of the principles of the setting are either false or much more complicated.<br /> <br /> Here are my goals/ideas so far:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The main thing I want to do is present being Awakening as a cursed, monstrous condition rather than a blessing or a &quot;higher state&quot; of evolution, make it so that &quot;Awakened&quot; and &quot;Sleepers&quot; are just terms Mages use to feel better about themselves, and close to or more than half of Mages wish secretly or openly that they were normal humans again.<br /> \u2022 Paradox and Obsessions are both much more dangerous and punishing.<br /> \u2022 Archmastery is equivalent to becoming a True Fae- the Mage becomes an utterly inhuman entity.<br /> \u2022 Much of the setting's assumptions are ambiguous or wrong, and the possibility exists that much of what Mages believe is true is true because their disruptive presence in reality forces it to be true.<br /> \u2022 Moral ambiguities of the main conflict are emphasized. The Seers have a genuinely good case for why they're right.<br /> \u2022 As Mages gain power and lose Wisdom, they must take Bans and Banes related to how they can perform magic, like other supernatural creatures.<br /> \u2022 Crossover possibilities are enhanced, with Mage supremacy being actively fought with nerfs.<br /> \u2022 The subjective nature of the Supernal is emphasized, as well as the possibility that it's essentially a shared delusion that Mages can force into reality. Players only have to pick one of their Path's Arcana, and choose any other as their second ruling Arcana. Experiences of the Supernal realms are vastly different and subjective.<br /> \u2022 Some Mages have no Path. They are stereotyped as being more likely to become Scelesti or Banishers, but the truth of this assumption is questionable.<br /> \u2022 A significant and ever-increasing number of Mages Awaken as Gifted Scientists from the Mage Chronicler's Guide.<br /> \u2022 Presumably other stuff I'll think of later.<br /> <br /> Feedback and suggestions are welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amazing!<br /> <br /> Try click the link to my Frailty Chronicle house rules? All supernaturals, including Mages, transform into increasing monstrous beings by committing Atrocities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:40:13-07:00","id":973180,"title":"","content":"So a comment from me, not trying to downvote but just trying to show a few things can be acomplished using what's already in the books.<br /> <br /> Archmage's - IMHO they are already pretty inhuman. After reading IM my image of a archmage is a guy who believes in having a morality licence to do whatever he wants and so absolutely obsessed about something that they'll do ANYTHING do acomplish that goal. That's pretty scary for me.<br /> <br /> Obsessions aren't meant to be dangerous because players would never pursue them. I always had this problem in RPGs that players were always doing the most &quot;optimal&quot; choice and that frequently meant not engaging with the game. Obessions are meant to be something the players work for, it's up to the ST to make them have consequences. Try to encourage players to take obsessions that would lead towards &quot;bad&quot; decisions.<br /> <br /> For me it seems like you want something more obvious than the type of horror that Mage: the Awakening tries to do. From what I read in your posts seems like Ascension would be a better fit for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 09-20-2016, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:40:54-07:00","id":973182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973151#post973151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone said earlier that he brings it into other threads. Can't we just worry about that when it happens instead of being dicks to someone who wants help in a thread that isn't hurting anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very fine idea. <br /> I'm curious to see how eager you are to follow it after seeing months of the same old story repeating again and again and again.<br /> These forums exist in the context of larger conversations, and those conversations require the goodwill of all participants. I think even the naysayers here are <i>trying</i> to be helpful, but what you're seeing is the result of that effort when the goodwill backing it has been almost utterly exhausted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:05:59-07:00","id":973199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973182#post973182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think even the naysayers here are <i>trying</i> to be helpful, but what you're seeing is the result of that effort when the goodwill backing it has been almost utterly exhausted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they should take a breather and come back when they're more relaxed.<br /> <br /> Now, to be productive: Has anyone considering importing the Atrocity Dice mechanic from Requiem's Chronicler's Guide (I think?) and using it as a Paradox/Wisdom substitute? Would need some tweaking (new name, first and foremost), but it would add that &quot;you're a monster, and there's no turning back&quot; element into Awakening. Maybe every spell adds 1 point of !Atrocity, and that gets used as the Paradox pool, while Permanent !Atrocity add as a Paradox pool to all spells?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:53:09-07:00","id":973234,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your suggestions. <br /> <br /> I'm kind of having a major problem, though, in that I'm being told two contradictory things:<br /> <br /> One group of people is telling me that I don't need to change much or anything, because what I want is already present in the setting and mechanics and Mage is already a game about being a monster. <br /> <br /> The other group is telling me that making Mage into a personal horror game about being a monster requires radically changing it in a way counter to its original intention. <br /> <br /> If the first one is true, I admit I've had a hard time seeing in it Mage RAW and would like to work out ways to emphasize it more. If the second is true, then I still want to go ahead with this, because I think Mage should be a personal horror game about being a monster, and if it isn't that or wasn't supposed to be that, that's all the more reason to work on it.<br /> <br /> I would suggest that the people who don't want a game about power being dangerous and inherently corrupting and inhuman are the ones looking for something contrary to the setting. Again, I don't have anything against this, but I'm working from the assumption (and preference) that ChroD is a personal horror game, not an urban fantasy one.<br /> <br /> Dave's current project, Deviant, actually provides a perfect outline of how I see supernatural power working in a horror setting: the more power a Deviant has, the more Scars they have. This holds true for all the games other than Mage. Demons and Mummies are the most powerful supernaturals after Mages, and they're probably the least human and saddled with some of the biggest drawbacks. Vampires have comparatively limited power next to mages, yet they're stuck with a host of downsides and monstrous tendencies. I've said it before: I want to make Mages either less powerful or less human, because my vision of ChroD is that you can only pick one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-20-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:00:11-07:00","id":973236,"title":"","content":"That's to be expected, multiple interpretations of a single text is a pattern throughout history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:11:23-07:00","id":973245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973234#post973234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your suggestions.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of having a major problem, though, in that I'm being told two contradictory things:<br /> <br /> One group of people is telling me that I don't need to change much or anything, because what I want is already present in the setting and mechanics and Mage is already a game about being a monster.<br /> <br /> The other group is telling me that making Mage into a personal horror game about being a monster requires radically changing it in a way counter to its original intention.<br /> <br /> If the first one is true, I admit I've had a hard time seeing in it Mage RAW and would like to work out ways to emphasize it more. If the second is true, then I still want to go ahead with this, because I think Mage should be a personal horror game about being a monster, and if it isn't that or wasn't supposed to be that, that's all the more reason to work on it.<br /> <br /> I would suggest that the people who don't want a game about power being dangerous and inherently corrupting and inhuman are the ones looking for something contrary to the setting. Again, I don't have anything against this, but I'm working from the assumption (and preference) that ChroD is a personal horror game, not an urban fantasy one.<br /> <br /> Dave's current project, Deviant, actually provides a perfect outline of how I see supernatural power working in a horror setting: the more power a Deviant has, the more Scars they have. This holds true for all the games other than Mage. Demons and Mummies are the most powerful supernaturals after Mages, and they're probably the least human and saddled with some of the biggest drawbacks. Vampires have comparatively limited power next to mages, yet they're stuck with a host of downsides and monstrous tendencies. I've said it before: I want to make Mages either less powerful or less human, because my vision of ChroD is that you can only pick one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody's saying that second thing. Except you. Your assertion that power must come with drawbacks in order to be horror is enlightening and explains a lot of your issues with Mage, but it's not how the setting is written, especially when you remember that Mages aren't monsters because of what they are but because of what they do. Mages go from being able to light fires with their minds to being able to create and destroy lives, minds, and mess with time. They go from human+ to alien gods married with ambition and a desire to understand how their powers work, and if that's not terrifying to you then I don't know what else to tell you.<br /> <br /> That Mages are beholden to nobody but themselves is <i>part</i> of the horror, not unrelated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:41:57-07:00","id":973259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973245#post973245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody's saying that second thing. Except you. Your assertion that power must come with drawbacks in order to be horror is enlightening and explains a lot of your issues with Mage, but it's not how the setting is written, especially when you remember that Mages aren't monsters because of what they are but because of what they do. Mages go from being able to light fires with their minds to being able to create and destroy lives, minds, and mess with time. They go from human+ to alien gods married with ambition and a desire to understand how their powers work, and if that's not terrifying to you then I don't know what else to tell you.<br /> <br /> That Mages are beholden to nobody but themselves is <i>part</i> of the horror, not unrelated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. The horror of Mage isn't that the mechanics force them to go on killing sprees with magic or die, or to rip the souls out of everyone they meet or risk losing their powers. The horror of Mage isn't that the mechanics force them without question to do horrible things. The horror from Mage comes from the fact that even though they have power that they can do whatever they want to with it, they <i>choose</i> to do some pretty terrible things with it. They aren't forced to do it, <i>they do it because they want to.</i> <br /> <br /> I honestly find that more horrific than a vampires need to drink blood or anything of the like. Vampires are forced to harm people for survival, when a Mage chooses to harm someone it's not because they have to to live, or that they're irresistibly compelled to (though while not irresistible, they might still be compelled to). No, if a Mage chooses to harm you, it is because they've decided <i>with their very soul</i> that whatever harm it is that they are inflicting upon you is a reasonable price to pay to attain whatever it is they think they're getting from it. Simply put I personally find that much more horrific than draining a bit of blood from someone to live another night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:50:08-07:00","id":973268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973245#post973245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody's saying that second thing. Except you. Your assertion that power must come with drawbacks in order to be horror is enlightening and explains a lot of your issues with Mage, but it's not how the setting is written, especially when you remember that Mages aren't monsters because of what they are but because of what they do. Mages go from being able to light fires with their minds to being able to create and destroy lives, minds, and mess with time. They go from human+ to alien gods married with ambition and a desire to understand how their powers work, and if that's not terrifying to you then I don't know what else to tell you.<br /> <br /> That Mages are beholden to nobody but themselves is <i>part</i> of the horror, not unrelated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree there, best thing to do would be use the perils of the warp from Dark Heresy for external Paradox results, and remember that dedicated tools and Mana still leave a chance die. Take away the chance die option. Always make it so one die is there. And have the spell go sideways somehow. Collateral damage all the way.<br /> <br /> If they internalize it still hit them with more than damage but megalomania, and other psychological problems. Also give them a big Yantra bonus for sacrifices of lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:06:17-07:00","id":973278,"title":"","content":"&quot;That being said, you should also make it clear in your setting document that you have a strong dislike for pretty much every core conceit of Mage and would much rather be playing a hybrid of Genius that emphasises how much being a Mage sucked. If I was uninformed and sat down at your table to play Mage, I'd likely leave the table once I realised your vision of Mage was nothing like the game I intended to join. If I was in the mood to play a game involving having everything I do end up with me sucking and weird science, I'd have looked for a Promethean game :P&quot;<br /> <br /> There's someone who's saying that what I want goes against the core concept of the game and what appeals to them in it. So it isn't that &quot;nobody but me&quot; is saying that. Just clearing that up. What I'm saying is that some people are telling me that what I want is already there and some people are telling me that what I want is against the soul of the game. I have been told both of those things, neither is a strawman. I am saying that I respect both perspectives but am having trouble reconciling them. In the same posts where you said no one was saying the second thing...you said the second thing, by telling me that what I wanted was against how the game was written. <br /> <br /> And I've never been a fan of the &quot;they're scary because they could do terrible things with their powers&quot; as a justification for something existing in ChroD. ChroD isn't just horror, it's horror where the players take on the role of horror archetypes. Mages in Awakening do not resemble any horror archetype, as sorcerers and wizards in horror fiction more closely resemble minor template sorcerers or Geniuses than Awakened. To be more specific, I prefer for it to be that power itself is monstrous, not just what people do with it. This isn't because of personal belief or anything related to the real world, it's because &quot;power is monstrous&quot; is one of the central principles that horror operates on. I don't think I'm amiss in pointing out the ways in which Awakening breaks from both its source material and its wider setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-20-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:13:02-07:00","id":973282,"title":"","content":"Lot of threadcrapping here. Anyways, to be helpful:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 The main thing I want to do is present being Awakening as a cursed, monstrous condition rather than a blessing or a &quot;higher state&quot; of evolution, make it so that &quot;Awakened&quot; and &quot;Sleepers&quot; are just terms Mages use to feel better about themselves, and close to or more than half of Mages wish secretly or openly that they were normal humans again.<br /> \u2022 Paradox and Obsessions are both much more dangerous and punishing.<br /> \u2022 Archmastery is equivalent to becoming a True Fae- the Mage becomes an utterly inhuman entity.<br /> \u2022 Much of the setting's assumptions are ambiguous or wrong, and the possibility exists that much of what Mages believe is true is true because their disruptive presence in reality forces it to be true.<br /> \u2022 Moral ambiguities of the main conflict are emphasized. The Seers have a genuinely good case for why they're right.<br /> \u2022 As Mages gain power and lose Wisdom, they must take Bans and Banes related to how they can perform magic, like other supernatural creatures.<br /> \u2022 Crossover possibilities are enhanced, with Mage supremacy being actively fought with nerfs.<br /> \u2022 The subjective nature of the Supernal is emphasized, as well as the possibility that it's essentially a shared delusion that Mages can force into reality. Players only have to pick one of their Path's Arcana, and choose any other as their second ruling Arcana. Experiences of the Supernal realms are vastly different and subjective.<br /> \u2022 Some Mages have no Path. They are stereotyped as being more likely to become Scelesti or Banishers, but the truth of this assumption is questionable.<br /> \u2022 A significant and ever-increasing number of Mages Awaken as Gifted Scientists from the Mage Chronicler's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>So, point one is you want there to be reasons for a Mage to not want to be a Mage, right?</li> <li>Paradox is already pretty dangerous, though usually for other people (that's part of the theme). To make it more dangerous, just have the Paradoxes more likely to affect the Mage. As for Obsessions, give Mages a persistent Addicted Condition. They <i>are</i> supposed to be &quot;Addicted to Mysteries&quot; after all.</li> <li>Archmasters already have pretty opaque and divergent goals. Just make it clear how much so, and how their magic/Obsessions drives them further.</li> <li>How to represent that though? This issue is a bit vague to handle in one bullet point.</li> <li>What do you see as the Seers' main point, in which they might be right?</li> <li>Maybe spin it as: As their power (Gnosis) grows and their self-awareness (Wisdom) drops, they become more set in their ways and psychologically dependent upon certain actions or modes of thought (needing to use their Yantras, instead of them being optional for a bonus, or compulsively indulging in &quot;Evil Sorcerer&quot; behavior).</li> <li>Meh. Maybe other Supernaturals add to Paradox just like Sleepers do? Or Clashes against Supernaturals provoke ongoing spells to warp like unsafely Relinquished ones can? Mages can still do amazing things... they just become more likely to blow up in their face.</li> <li>First part needs something cast doubt. That's just flavor to be added in your setting. Second part is rules. Those look fine, I guess (and map to how Supernal Entities' Arcana work, I think).</li> <li>Flavor it sounds like you already decided on.</li> <li>Meh. Why, though?</li> </ul><br /> Additionally, maybe you could play up the influence of Mage Sight and Symbols. I remember there was text in 1E Changeling regarding them seeing everything as &quot;embodied&quot; or some such at low Clarity. Like a lighter flame isn't just a small flame, but a small fire being they could talk to (or something like that). Perhaps Mages are similarly affected, in that they start to see <i>everything</i> in the context of Symbols - they don't become inhuman via compulsion so much as their think alters to see things like murder, joy, or other people as mere collections of abstract Symbols (which is arguably already in text). Full-time Active Mage Sight, basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:18:20-07:00","id":973285,"title":"","content":"That sounds good. As for the last point, it's because:<br /> <br /> A. &quot;Mad scientist&quot; is one of my two favorite horror archetypes (the other being &quot;Frankensteinian galvanic chimera&quot;, the ChroD depiction of which is sadly also dragged down by HFY and mortality porn and is something else I'm working on).<br /> <br /> B. Mad scientists are vastly more common in horror media than &quot;mad wizards&quot;, especially wizards of the type seen in Awakening. Mad scientists have been the stars of more horror movies than werewolves and mummies combined. Put simply, they're so massively important to horror as a genre that they deserve proportionate representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:35:18-07:00","id":973299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973278#post973278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I've never been a fan of the &quot;they're scary because they could do terrible things with their powers&quot; as a justification for something existing in ChroD. ChroD isn't just horror, it's horror where the players take on the role of horror archetypes. Mages in Awakening do not resemble any horror archetype, as sorcerers and wizards in horror fiction more closely resemble minor template sorcerers or Geniuses than Awakened. To be more specific, I prefer for it to be that power itself is monstrous, not just what people do with it. This isn't because of personal belief or anything related to the real world, it's because &quot;power is monstrous&quot; is one of the central principles that horror operates on.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're free to believe whatever you want about what CofD is supposed to be, but in this case you have nothing to cite to back up your assertion (that players must take on the role of horror archetypes), and it remains a personal belief. It's a game about playing monsters. Mages are monsters because of what they do, not what they are. Can you play a Mage who defends the innocent, subtly helps those around them, and generally uses their powers selflessly and without going too far? Of course, just like you could play a vampire who only feeds off of animals or the willing and who keeps themselves away from situations where they might frenzy, or a Harmony 5 Werewolf who manages to perfectly balance their lives as an apex predator and loving human, or a Promethean who manages their relationships to humans with remote correspondence and only choosing friends who can probably handle Disquiet and never staying in one place long enough to cause Wastelands.<br /> <br /> But the point of these games is to play non-aspiration characters - <i>monsters</i> - who do terrible stuff. Not because they want to, but because they're either left with no choice or because it's the easy way out. It's <i>hard</i> for a Mage to be a &quot;good guy&quot; because the temptation to push themselves too far and cause Paradox, or to enact vigilante justice, or scry on their neighbors &quot;Just to make sure nobody's a serial killer or something, I'm just being practical&quot;. All of those actions are monstrous, and Mages can only do them <i>because they are mages</i>. Vampires aren't monsters because they <i>have</i> to drink blood to survive, it's because they typically choose humans as their prey. Pretty much the only group that <i>must behave</i> like monsters are Beasts, and thus they don't get a trait to reflect how monstrous they're behaving.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:49:41-07:00","id":973309,"title":"","content":"CofD has never been the place to go for archetypal horror. Vampires are really the only template that bears more than a passing resemblance to the horror archetype it ostensibly represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:52:38-07:00","id":973313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973285#post973285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (the other being &quot;Frankensteinian galvanic chimera&quot;, the ChroD depiction of which is sadly also dragged down by HFY and mortality porn</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Can we not with this? It's disrespectful towards Matt.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:03:38-07:00","id":973325,"title":"","content":"Sure, my bad. But I still maintain that there's a lot more done with horror archetypes than what some people think. Why are Prometheans vulnerable to fire? Because &quot;fire bad!&quot; is something that's famously associated with the Creature. The way Sekhem works in Mummy is made to allow players to play unstoppable tomb robber-shredding ancient monstrosities and do stuff straight out of The Mummy. The reason it has Death Curse mechanics is right out of mummy folklore. Changeling draws extensively from both mythology and modern UFO media. Deviants are hunted by conspiracies because conspiracies are most often the antagonists in the inspirational media. <br /> <br /> Demon is most often called out as a deviation from the archetype it's based on, but it really isn't- it represents more modern monster archetypes, such as the reality-warping mysterious stranger (Agent Smith, the G-Man, Bill Cipher) and the killer robot/malevolent AI (the Terminator, the WAU, Agent Smith again).<br /> <br /> So yes, ChroD primarily uses recognizable horror archetypes as a basis. Even weirder things Hosts are based on horror archetypes: body snatchers, parasites, and the old standby of &quot;a guy but he's actually full of spiders/worms/rats&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:05:33-07:00","id":973330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973299#post973299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are monsters because of what they do, not what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't make <b>Mages</b> monsters, since some Mages can (easily) choose to behave non-monstrously. Here, Monster is determined by actions, which can fit some Mages, but not others. heck, it can fit some people.<br /> <br /> It's like saying Mages are Monsters because they <i>can</i> kill people. So what? People can kill people. We don't say all people are Monsters. You can say Mages are &quot;tempted&quot; to commit Monstrous actions, but how? If anything, Wisdom <i>dis</i>incentivizes it. A Mage <i>can</i> Reach for more power, but a generic human <i>can</i> also use human shields, care nothing for collateral damage, or employ torture. A Vampire or Werewolf at least has a trigger that could cause them to do things they <i>don't want</i> to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973299#post973299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires aren't monsters because they <i>have</i> to drink blood to survive, it's because they typically choose humans as their prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor quibble: eventually, they <i>do</i> have to prey upon people. And even later, other vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:26:31-07:00","id":973349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973330#post973330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which doesn't make <b>Mages</b> monsters, since some Mages can (easily) choose to behave non-monstrously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we're talking about vampires here, have a thing Rose mentioned two years ago:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/152378-how-bloodlines-work?p=165276#post165276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are magic. It's not a term we use often, because when people hear &quot;magic&quot; they think &quot;Mage.&quot; But vampires operate on magical logic. <b>They leverage sympathy, they have a malignant aura, and they spread curses.</b> The fundamental aesthetics of <i>Requiem</i> vampires are all supernatural. Not spellcasting, no, but distinctly magical.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Minor quibble: eventually, they <i>do</i> have to prey upon people. And even later, other vampires. </div> </div> </div>Nope. 2e shuffled the hard limit to an expensive surcharge and provided non-consumptive means of getting Vitae. You can theoretically have elders who haven't put fangs to humanlike skin in decades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:43:18-07:00","id":973358,"title":"","content":"Back to Mages, I want to keep the fact that being a Mage is something you choose to become, but add more consequences: make magic bleeding into your mind and the world around you more of a threat. Playing up the &quot;you did this yourself&quot; aspect by making the condition of being Awakened equivalent to: you deliberately turned yourself into a walking hole in reality because you wanted power/knowledge/to take over the world&quot;. I reeeeeeeeally want to make Mages feel less like &quot;Humans 2.0&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:45:14-07:00","id":973359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973349#post973349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. 2e shuffled the hard limit to an expensive surcharge and provided non-consumptive means of getting Vitae. You can theoretically have elders who haven't put fangs to humanlike skin in decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, right. The 1 Willpower per Vitae taken tax? I forgot about that.<br /> <br /> Still, they are going to need some kind of Willpower source to fuel that kind of unlifestyle. Major commitment to their Mask and Dirge, might do it, since they aren't getting Willpower from sleep (I think).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:51:50-07:00","id":973364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973359#post973359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, right. The 1 Willpower per Vitae taken tax? I forgot about that.<br /> <br /> Still, they are going to need some kind of Willpower source to fuel that kind of unlifestyle. Major commitment to their Mask and Dirge, might do it, since they aren't getting Willpower from sleep (I think).</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. There's also the torpor option: if they can't keep up with their nightly needs they can just sleep for a few decades to get their Blood Potency back to 2 or 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:56:31-07:00","id":973368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973358#post973358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to Mages, I want to keep the fact that being a Mage is something you choose to become, but add more consequences: make magic bleeding into your mind and the world around you more of a threat. Playing up the &quot;you did this yourself&quot; aspect by making the condition of being Awakened equivalent to: you deliberately turned yourself into a walking hole in reality because you wanted power/knowledge/to take over the world&quot;. I reeeeeeeeally want to make Mages feel less like &quot;Humans 2.0&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me ask you this.<br /> <br /> How do you view the mages reacting when they reach a spell, Paradox happens and razor sharp glass fills the body of the young couple and there child because all glass in Potency yards of you shattered. When you while trying to save the life of Sister Ophelia and the girls at St. Teresa's school you blasted a vampire with everything you had, and you turn back and watch as the creature from the Abyss eats them like potato chips? When you drive Old Bootsy, the bum in the alley you get information from, to insanity because of a ghostly wailing sound that won't go away because of your paradox.<br /> <br /> Mages are Nuclear bombs. They are Andy from Red vs. Blue. Nukes who want nothing more than to explode. And when they go nova (wisdom 0) is when they are even more dangerous.<br /> <br /> Just like Psychers from Dark Heresy. They are one pushed power away from inviting a greater demon into reality to murder, rape, and skin everyone (and you pray it's in that order).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 09-20-2016, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:03:13-07:00","id":973374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973358#post973358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to Mages, I want to keep the fact that being a Mage is something you choose to become, but add more consequences: make magic bleeding into your mind and the world around you more of a threat. Playing up the &quot;you did this yourself&quot; aspect by making the condition of being Awakened equivalent to: you deliberately turned yourself into a walking hole in reality because you wanted power/knowledge/to take over the world&quot;. I reeeeeeeeally want to make Mages feel less like &quot;Humans 2.0&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That could work with 0 or very little modification of the setting. <br /> But again I think you're looking for something very different than the game is about. Mage IMHO (and also other CofD games) was very much about &quot;human evil&quot;, as others already pointed out. So you might have time modyfying the setting, though I'll hope you'll be satisfied in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:59:17-07:00","id":973501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973358#post973358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to Mages, I want to keep the fact that being a Mage is something you choose to become, but add more consequences: make magic bleeding into your mind and the world around you more of a threat. Playing up the &quot;you did this yourself&quot; aspect by making the condition of being Awakened equivalent to: you deliberately turned yourself into a walking hole in reality because you wanted power/knowledge/to take over the world&quot;. I reeeeeeeeally want to make Mages feel less like &quot;Humans 2.0&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really <i>choose</i> to become a Mage. You can choose whether or not you use magic, but a Mage who doesn't cast is still a Mage. <br /> <br /> Magic bleeding into the world around you is done through your nimbus running rampant through your sympathetic links. Theoretically it could get really bad, but that's one of the reasons why Shadow Names and the separation between your mundane and magical identity is a thing. Mages and their society attempts to put a buffer between themselves and the world around them, so as to avoid their magic needlessly spilling out though the people and places they care about. Usually that means that any time their magic <i>does</i> seep through and mess with the lives of their friends and family, it is due to a personal failure. Had they been cautious enough, safe enough, they could have prevented it from happening.<br /> <br /> I feel that that packs more impact than some mechanic that just fucks you over regardless in some vain attempt at 'Oh, look how evil and monstrous you are not being able to stop that thing you had absolutely no control over! How bad it is to be you~&quot;. Also, frequency plays a decent role in impact too. If it's something that happens all the time it sort of loses its flair. At that point Mages would logically just cut all ties to people around them and avoid the issue completely. With it being less frequent and even preventable, it allows them to stay close to their loved one long enough for that eventual slip up that ruins everything. So it becomes is really big high moment rather than some constant low key annoyance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:23:46-07:00","id":973609,"title":"","content":"Another aspect that I can think of came to me while watching Stranger Things on netflix. The more you use your power, the more you become used to it. The more it can do for you, the more that power starts to wield you instead of you wielding it. The other kids look at 011 like she is a bad-ass friend. One of them sees her as a monster. Others see her as a tool to use and more than a few seek to do so. A lot of people see her as a monster though for how casually she kills people with a nod, and her general detachment from people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:41:21-07:00","id":973618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971945#post971945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware that a lot of what I'm describing is already present in the text, what I'm working on is emphasizing it. That's why I'm considering doing this instead of a full remake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like your problem steams from practicality rather than theory. You need to figure out ways to emphasize those elements within a story and setting, rather than focus exclusively in mechanics. Hundreds of play-testers already tuned the mechanics for those needs as much as feasible.<br /> <br /> To give an example: if you want Obsession to involve risks, you have to actually come up with complications derived from their pursuit - such as being obsessed with an Iris that ultimately makes your worst fear (the horrible death of your spouse) come to fruition if you somehow manage to open it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T20:51:12-07:00","id":973623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=972925#post972925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like there's a disagreement between people who think Mage isn't in-your-face horror enough and people who feel it's subtly very horrific indeed. For my own part, I'm pretty happy with Mage's horror level right where it is - whatever anyone else deems it to be. I like that the mage's temptation to push his limits is mirrored in how the mechanics tempt the player, but I also like that the choice to play someone who is overcome by hubris or someone who is merely tempted but steadfastly resists is ultimately firmly in the player's hands rather than being imposed from on high. I mean, if I wanted to play Fucked-Up Guy: The Cursening, I could be playing something else. But I am not playing something else. HMM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage's horror, IMHO, steams from the fact that you just can't unsee the world as it fundamentally is: You can't go have a night out without noticing the vampire mind-raping someone for a fix of their blood, the silent screams of the spirits forcefully bound in that Uratha's fetish, the way that this fairest is playing chicken with people's fate threads, to say nothing of innumerable and not so readily explainable phenomena and creatures that form the basis for 89% of every obsession you might develop along the way.<br /> <br /> As Nietzsche put it: &quot;When you gaze upon the abyss...&quot;<br /> <br /> But if the ST isn't proactive in filling his setting with such unsettling mysteries... Such Themes and Mood go the way of the dodo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:06:11-07:00","id":973662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973309#post973309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CofD has never been the place to go for archetypal horror. Vampires are really the only template that bears more than a passing resemblance to the horror archetype it ostensibly represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting view point. Can I buy your thoughts for a penny? It's a shinny penny!<br /> <br /> Ok so I get the standard werewolves are all about the uncontrollable monster during the full moon. I can still see that in forsaken, but does the added spiritual component delude that origin too much?<br /> <br /> I know in Mage it's more Hubrus and what have I DONE! and crazy magic running out of control. very Mad sciencsty.<br /> <br /> Promethean still feels pretty much the same old Frankenstein Monster Story, with a modern update. The disquiet and all plays that up.<br /> <br /> Changeling can still dive into its Germanic roots for bastard fae characters. Baby/ Child Stealing changeling fae, fetches right out the gate. but that one rhythm in the nursery poetry<br /> <br /> In vampire, I still feel the old a monster I am least a monster I become vibe. but you're definitely not playing the hunter/mortal Van Halsing. Does the line's focus on the political game push those ideas away from the limelight? It still has the very invasive forced overtones of the embrace, and slow loss of self to immoral hunger<br /> <br /> The Hunter Line has the Atypical Horror movie as its selling point.<br /> <br /> You can play the splats as you see fit. I still believe a pretty good ST can pull the game back into the Atypical horror theme. Course Player buy in is still required. There's lots of extra weirdness in the game lines. But does the weirdness make it unpalatable to the audience?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":". 09-21-2016, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:21:06-07:00","id":973675,"title":"","content":"I'd generally say that the player characters being the monsters, and thus making them into protagonists changes the theme and mood of each of the lines quite a bit from their thematic roots. As Charlaquin says, Vampire still shares a lot of headspace with its inspirations, a blood sucking parasitical entity cursed to roam the night for eternity. But, as mentioned, the other games change up the protagonists of their setting quite a bit. Werewolf, rather than being about a curse that activates during a period of time each month wherein you become a bestial killer is about animistic wolfmen who police the border between humanity and a spiritual world. Mage, rather than being about people having congress with demons for arcane power is about Gnostic humans who've seen past the veil of illusion laid over the world and reformed their souls to access an arcane realm above ours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T01:32:59-07:00","id":973718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973358#post973358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to Mages, I want to keep the fact that being a Mage is something you choose to become, but add more consequences: make magic bleeding into your mind and the world around you more of a threat. Playing up the &amp;quot;you did this yourself&amp;quot; aspect by making the condition of being Awakened equivalent to: you deliberately turned yourself into a walking hole in reality because you wanted power/knowledge/to take over the world&amp;quot;. I reeeeeeeeally want to make Mages feel less like &amp;quot;Humans 2.0&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you want to play up the Nimbus, particularly the Long Term Nimbus. Well that was easy,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T02:19:06-07:00","id":973726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973718#post973718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you want to play up the Nimbus, particularly the Long Term Nimbus. Well that was easy,</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any specific suggestion, besides &quot;make stuff up on the fly&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T02:56:47-07:00","id":973734,"title":"","content":"Why would you want to tie an endless possibility engine down to specifics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T03:30:02-07:00","id":973742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973662#post973662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so I get the standard werewolves are all about the uncontrollable monster during the full moon. I can still see that in forsaken, but does the added spiritual component delude that origin too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, if anything, the whole spiritual aspects add even more horror. What could possibly be more horrible than facing the spiritual manifestation of your own unsated bloodlust, for instance? How do you figure what is enough killing from excess? How do you reach a compromise with your savage self? What happens when such a thing outright wears your skin, likely throwing you into a possibly perpetual state of Kuruth until you're drunk with all the innocent spilled blood? What happens if you outright destroy this part of your self?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:30:04-07:00","id":973751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971927#post971927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Already the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Seers have a good argument for being right, then why does the book explicitly say that all Seers know they're wrong?<br /> <br /> &quot;No mage serves the Throne out of altruism. Even the deluded or willfully ignorant find themselves quickly disabused of notions of fighting the good fight.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:42:25-07:00","id":973776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973751#post973751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Seers have a good argument for being right, then why does the book explicitly say that all Seers know they're wrong?<br /> <br /> &quot;No mage serves the Throne out of altruism. Even the deluded or willfully ignorant find themselves quickly disabused of notions of fighting the good fight.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Perspective Bias. Same reason that the pure are deemed wrong. It's because the skewed perspective. We see everything from the perspective of those fighting the Exarchs, but we know nothing of things from the other perspective. All the splat books are full of propiganda for one point of view. The one we assume would be the more correct. This isn't always correct though. There was a recent Youtube video that called out Startreks Federation as being a Facist empire. The thing is we never see it because we are viewing things though the perspective of the elect of that society. So everything mostly looks all sunshine and rainbows, with occasional storms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:04:53-07:00","id":973788,"title":"","content":"Perspective bias can go do one, or stick to Ascension where it belongs.<br /> <br /> In the gameline we actually <i>have</i> we explain why the Pentacle believe the things they do while in the next para cheerfully point out why those things make them fail.<br /> <br /> Seers have to accept that by any routine standard of morality they're doing evil by serving the Exarchs. They do it anyway, in the same spirit as someone working for a company they know is up to no good, or the way we all know our society is built on the backs of the developing world's slave labour but doing something about it is too hard.<br /> <br /> A Seer could serve because he wants to be on the winning side, or believes himself an exception, or feels like the world pushed him around so now it's his turn to get some, or is afraid of the Exarchs. Unless he's completely delusional, the things his Ministry (and once a prelate, his dreams) tell him to do in their service are obviously Not Good. But magic is payment, and that's the price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:06:46-07:00","id":973789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973734#post973734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you want to tie an endless possibility engine down to specifics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, my imagination isn't endless. And I'm not asking for specifics, but some guidelines, at least, as the corebook is particularly vague on that point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:23:26-07:00","id":973802,"title":"","content":"Sorry. To elaborate;<br /> <br /> Seers was my first Mage book as a writer. The team still included many cwod veterans, who had had years of people arguing about the Technocracy in Ascension and whether they were justified. The Guide to the Technocracy was written as satire, and taken at face value. In the nWoD, when the time came to write the Pure and Seer books, we were determined to <i>not have that happen</i>. My induction into freelancing was discussions about how we could communicate what the Seers believed while being absolutely clear that they were villains.<br /> <br /> It is an experience that has served me well over the years, which is why - coming around to the thrust of this thread - Mage now has sections in the Orders about their hubris, sample Awakenings where you see how obsessed mages have to be to Awaken, and the intro of the book clearly states the horror themes of the game in defiance of certain posters ignoring it. Mage is about obsession, and how chasing it harms the people around you. Its protagonists in the Pentacle are dangerous assholes. The Seers are worse.<br /> <br /> Come into the game half-reading it because you read Genius and internalised its creator's tantrum about the sons of ether, and thinking it's cheerleading for mages the way Ascension does, and you get... Threads like this, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:38:42-07:00","id":973813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973789#post973789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, my imagination isn't endless. And I'm not asking for specifics, but some guidelines, at least, as the corebook is particularly vague on that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pg. 88 It should be shaped by Path, legacy, and personal symbolism like dedicated tools and shadow name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:08:01-07:00","id":973835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973813#post973813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pg. 88 It should be shaped by Path, legacy, and personal symbolism like dedicated tools and shadow name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, particularly vague.<br /> <br /> Let's pull a specific example. You got Lisa Bauer, a Thyrsus attempting to heal the world. She sees the One as All, and the All as One. Every organism is connected, so the world can only be &quot;fixed&quot; with a bit of surgery, helping people connect with each other and with whatever surrounds them. She created her own Space/Spirit Legacy to help her accomplish just that. She uses no Shadow Name, and has Dedicated her bag of oils and powders, which she uses to anoint the targets of her magic. She's also a dutiful daughter, loving sister, and a nurse at the local hospital.<br /> <br /> What's appropriate as a Long-Term Nimbus for Lisa? Besides &quot;it feels right&quot;, how do you justify your decision?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:29:44-07:00","id":973839,"title":"","content":"Spirits of sickness and healing are likely to be attracted or attached to her Sympathetic connections, oils and powders start taking on strange properties, unlikely hybrid organisms crop up, etc. The best way to have the LTN act though is for the actions of the character to indirectly influence how it manifests which requires game time (And can explain why at low Gnosis it's subtle, but the higher your Gnosis rises the more pronounced the effects are). You might get to best bang for your buck by having the Nimbus confront the Mage with positive confirmation bias. They see things that seem to prove them right and this confirms their course of action and outlook to themselves. It's a fairly organic way to run it and represents their magic leaking out of them, and occasionally you can drive that point home by taking a Nimbus inspired set of circumstances to a horrifying logical conclusion, in her case possibly an organic, grey goo that devours people and spirits alike.<br /> <br /> Edit: Need an obvious connection between the two? Slap her Signature Nimbus on the effect. Though honestly that might be too on the nose. YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-21-2016, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:57:02-07:00","id":973851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973751#post973751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Seers have a good argument for being right, then why does the book explicitly say that all Seers know they're wrong?<br /> <br /> &quot;No mage serves the Throne out of altruism. Even the deluded or willfully ignorant find themselves quickly disabused of notions of fighting the good fight.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The allure of the Seers, particularly for newly Awakened mages who don't yet have a full picture of their new, vastly expanded world, is easy to understand.<br /> <br /> As Dave indicated, just like in the real world, one need not serve because of altruism or some higher purpose. The Seers being &quot;right&quot; has absolutely nothing to do with it.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs have already won much of the fight for reality, the Seers are their winning team, service grants <u>fantastic</u> mundane and magical rewards, and it only requires occasional bad acts while the rest of the time you're free to pursue your own Obsessions. It's a simple cost / benefit analysis.<br /> <br /> When inquiring why any mage would join the Seers, contemplate why any regular person would work for tobacco companies or why so many attorneys would represent known criminals and mobsters. The vast majority of these people sleep well at knight, comfortable that they and their families are safe and secure in a cruel world. Given how the CofD is worse than the real world, the benefits of such service are even more understandable.<br /> <br /> Besides, most of the evil acts and oppression demanded by the Exarchs are directed at Sleepers. It's not like the ants really matter. If they did, they would have Awakened (a view also shared by many Pentacle mages, particularly in the Mysterium) ... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:04:19-07:00","id":973856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973802#post973802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry. To elaborate;<br /> <br /> Seers was my first Mage book as a writer. The team still included many cwod veterans, who had had years of people arguing about the Technocracy in Ascension and whether they were justified. The Guide to the Technocracy was written as satire, and taken at face value. In the nWoD, when the time came to write the Pure and Seer books, we were determined to <i>not have that happen</i>. My induction into freelancing was discussions about how we could communicate what the Seers believed while being absolutely clear that they were villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>So one of the best and more mature book that grabbed a one-dimensional bruahaha villan and make it something interesting was a complete accident when in reality the authors wanted to just keep on the one dimensional route?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:29:14-07:00","id":973868,"title":"","content":"The Guide to the Technocracy has a stat for how brainwashed your character is. It's about people who've been fooled - a low level Technocrat might think they're in the right, but the conventions are run from the Horizon by ex Order of Reason guys who know that they're mages and know what they're doing.<br /> <br /> The Traditions do not, in fact, have a grudge against indoor plumbing. \ud83d\ude01<br /> <br /> RAI, a technocracy game is meant to be like nMummy: Figuring out you're being used and deciding what to do from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:37:00-07:00","id":973872,"title":"","content":"I'd argue the Seers are a more mature antagonist anyway. Or a more pessimistic one: people don't need to be manipulated by archmages like Tychoides to do evil. They just need to be given a good steak","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:47:18-07:00","id":973876,"title":"","content":"I, for one, welcome our Awakened overlords.<br /> <br /> More seriously, Branford, weren't you objecting to the comparison of the Seers to lawyers who take on clients they know are bad recently? Or was that someone else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:01:04-07:00","id":973880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973835#post973835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, particularly vague.<br /> <br /> Let's pull a specific example. You got Lisa Bauer, a Thyrsus attempting to heal the world. She sees the One as All, and the All as One. Every organism is connected, so the world can only be &quot;fixed&quot; with a bit of surgery, helping people connect with each other and with whatever surrounds them. She created her own Space/Spirit Legacy to help her accomplish just that. She uses no Shadow Name, and has Dedicated her bag of oils and powders, which she uses to anoint the targets of her magic. She's also a dutiful daughter, loving sister, and a nurse at the local hospital.<br /> <br /> What's appropriate as a Long-Term Nimbus for Lisa? Besides &quot;it feels right&quot;, how do you justify your decision?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, just focusing on One as All, and the All as One (with input from a Space/Spirit Legacy), what about linking the health and even mood and features of people affected by her LTN? People start seeming to be the same, one gets sick/hurt, they all do, etc.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:08:33-07:00","id":973884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973872#post973872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue the Seers are a more mature antagonist anyway. Or a more pessimistic one: people don't need to be manipulated by archmages like Tychoides to do evil. They just need to be given a good steak</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the promise of being someone important. You know, like an actor or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:40:30-07:00","id":973899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973876#post973876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, for one, welcome our Awakened overlords.<br /> <br /> More seriously, Branford, weren't you objecting to the comparison of the Seers to lawyers who take on clients they know are bad recently? Or was that someone else?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did indeed object to broad comparisons of the legal profession itself as stereotypically greedy or evil. However, just like all humans, I would be the first to admit that individual lawyers may have selfish or amoral motives, and the profession certainly provides an ready outlet for the small minority of these individuals. The discussion of criminal defense attorneys, the clear majority of whom are both very liberal, meagerly compensated and represent the poor and needy, is particularly problematic, and what raised my ire in the earlier thread.<br /> <br /> I also sadly recognize that given the American constitutional and cultural peculiarities of the legal profession, and the perception of attorneys in mass media, even if generally wrong, still sometimes makes lawyers a good example to convey simple propositions. Those making such comparisons should just be careful to clearly define their points and not use stereotypes as fact (just like when discussing any other large and diverse group).<br /> <br /> In any event. I happen to very much like the Seers as Mage antagonists.<br /> <br /> They are both unremittingly evil and oppressive, yet entirely relatable and understandable, and thus function as mature and fun villains.<br /> <br /> Despite lofty rhetoric, it's also easy to see how on an individual level, many arrogant and hubristic Pentacle mages are little to no better that their Seer brethren. For what it's worth, the Seers at least acknowledge their evil. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:50:52-07:00","id":973955,"title":"","content":"Are Technocrats evil ???<br /> <br /> Well from my view point, and how I've run them they are the Villain with a point. <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/VillainHasAPoint\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...llainHasAPoint</a><br /> <br /> There was one Technocrat book that started with. You're Welcome. and then took credit for the welcomed changes from the high magic ages. When I read that I was kind of struck with the idea, wait how? what?<br /> <br /> The idea of an entirely brainwashed conspiracy was a little too much buy in for me. And you could still see the flickers of the Order of Reason ideals in the machine. They were dying but those ideals were there. The spark of rationality is there, glowing but a small ember in a dark place. What did the order of reason fight for? Physics, Science, Man's institutes. The common man against the Wizard's tower, against fae, and against monster lords. In the darkages you would be playing these guys as underdog protagonists.<br /> <br /> Did they kill free magic? Oh God Yes. But have you seen humanity? I barely trust us with nukes. Humanity needs at the same time not a lot and plenty of pushing to use destructive force. BUT and this is the one thing I can see and reason behind the techs. It's Humanity's choice. No Goblin. No Dragon. No Wizard. No Unicorn. No Gods. No Supermen. No Heroes. No Monsters. Just Human. The reason I can see the techs as at some level agreeable, is that they're humanity's Triumphs and Failings. Technology is the great equalizer.<br /> <br /> If anything you can draw a direct parallel to the Imperium of Man from 40k. Violently against the Other in space. They are Oppressive yes. but when the other is any number of horrible tortures worse than death. They're the Villain with a point. At the low points, the non enlightened are just people with a day job. You and me at the temp office, pushing papers. Not bad guys just people making ends meet. Do they care about Hal8000 in the upper server room zapping traditions in the cyberworld? well they don't know, can never know and they don't care.<br /> <br /> Another parallel, The Matrix (I know you're going UGH right now, but bare with me.) Those low level non enlightened personal are all the normies in the Matrix. They're still plugged into our reality. Our being the collective reality. The reality we find rational and understand. I once stop a cabal of mages from raiding a Tech Hospital with a Receptionist named Pam. Good mother if absent a lot of the time, great paying job. I gave her a damn good mind shield pendant. They wouldn't hit her. &quot;There are no good people in the Techys&quot; You don't need brainwashing if you pay your assets well. Is this any different from you and my lives right now? We work to get feed, and enjoy the time we have.<br /> <br /> To really win the Tradition's War they're going have to dramatically change mankind's outlook. Which isn't going to happen overnight, and probably wouldn't. That's bleak but that's the truth. Mankind can not hold onto a world without tragedy, conflict and pain. We need all these things to understand the world, and survive. Even in peace time we nave tragedy conflict and pain, just closer, and more personal. Utopia is the Dream we'll never collectively catch, and the Darkages were a nightmare everyone forgets was a nightmare. So we're left in this middle ground, but that's not terrible, its actually pretty hopeful. The past was horrible but we moved beyond it, and the future can be so much brighter.<br /> <br /> And before anyone brings up Room 101. ANY mage with enough Mind has a Room 101.<br /> <br /> Now you can start to get a little more into the theme in the middle management and higher ups. But at some point they're in the know. something is -not- up. and so there's the question: Do you still believe in the fight? Do the ends justify the means argument. For all the terrible things you had to do or not do. depending on how evil you ran the techs, can you still see the Reason in the machine for continuing? Some people will say Yes. A lot will say No.<br /> <br /> The two things that make the Tech greater than themselves is the TimeTable and keeping Reality in check. The TT is the schedule they have for mankind's collective enlightenment. At first it sounds like a noble goal, but most of these end games are terrible for everyone, but they're logical scifi conclusions. All metalmen, The matrix(Oh Wait that convention defected and therefore this a good ending now) Imperium of Man, A Brave new World 1984 or whatever dytopian we've got in the works right now. The Syndicate is actually happy about the world state right now. Incidentally I always run the Syndicate as the normalizing force in the Techs and perfectly will to accept the status quo.<br /> <br /> The Syn believe, and kind of legitimately, that they've already won. The people that want something have to fight or earn it. They look at the 9-5worker who wants to drink his beer and watch his TV, and say well he's happy enough or at least content. They give the golf clap to new awaken mages. &quot;Congratulations Now figure it out.&quot; Because to them you've earned your spot utmost the enlightened, and therefore have a right to a say in the bigger picture. They have the right to rebuttal, with guns, but yeah. They maybe greedy bastards, but as long as you're willing to pay for it they're your guy. CoughPaymentIsMagicCough<br /> <br /> As far keeping reality in check. Well every Tuesday's spaghetti night ... For those who survive Cthulhu rising out of the subway tunnels. As far as the Tech V Trad conflict Those are self interested groups going after the same resources. Also mages be craycray sometimes. Tech vs others, is the Tech v non humans, which was there mainstay.<br /> <br /> One of the first imagines of the Men in Black was actually as a Paradox effect. It was deeply rooted in the conspiracy of the &quot;Man&quot; taking you down. Men in Top Hats and mirror shades, Take you away because you kept abusing your powers. And they help get the verisimilitude of the setting by scrubbing all the bullshit players pull in games. And by legitimizing these paradox agents, they adopted the Masquerade model of Conspiracies keeping the truth from the world. and because the setting is modern day, we end up in an arms race of bullsht.<br /> <br /> TLDR: The seers are better written villains because they slowly buy into the brainwashing. While the assumption that all technocratic agents are brainwashed is a little hard to shallow, when they're the Villain with a point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:43:51-07:00","id":973982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973872#post973872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue the Seers are a more mature antagonist anyway. Or a more pessimistic one: people don't need to be manipulated by archmages like Tychoides to do evil. They just need to be given a good steak</div> </div> </div> </div>Well i would argue that while more &quot;realistic&quot; they are less compelling, they just black hats.... no moral dilema to put a bullet in their heads and go for Mcdonalds afterwards except for the whole artificial morality mechanic which now can be bypassed with unuring.<br /> <br /> They are the death eater of harry potter basically minus an urgent agenda. And i mean that both on the good and the bad. They are less morally interesting than the technocracy or most left handed paths but they shine on their methodologies and tricks, like their yantras called chains (or was shackles?) to the profane urin and something incredible insidious.<br /> <br /> Just like the Death eaters with their mask, a spells that kill people and snake motiffs.<br /> <br /> Still i dont see the problem with Gecko modifying the game to his liking, his way of asking non-whistanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-21-2016, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:48:34-07:00","id":973985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973982#post973982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well i would argue that while more &quot;realistic&quot; they are less compelling, they just black hats.... no moral dilema to put a bullet in their heads and go for Mcdonalds afterwards except for the whole artificial morality mechanic which now can be bypassed with unuring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, as long as you elaborately plan out the murder, you don't even ding Wisdom at the mid-range.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:10:29-07:00","id":973992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973982#post973982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well i would argue that while more &quot;realistic&quot; they are less compelling, they just black hats.... no moral dilema to put a bullet in their heads and go for Mcdonalds afterwards except for the whole artificial morality mechanic which now can be bypassed with unuring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hesitate to say that &quot;Bullet&quot; is a weird name for a spell, but the point remains that inuring doesn't work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:16:51-07:00","id":973995,"title":"","content":"Actually, premeditated murder does ping at Medium, going by the guidelines, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:17:00-07:00","id":973996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973992#post973992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hesitate to say that &quot;Bullet&quot; is a weird name for a spell, but the point remains that inuring doesn't work that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, using an inuring spell that shoots a bullet made of compressed air through their heads or just burn them to death with an inure fireball.<br /> <br /> I even ask this on the question thread. You kill someone once, loss wisdom once...then inure the spell used and from now on you can kill anyone with that spell and no wisdom loss. Isnt that how it works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:22:36-07:00","id":973999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973996#post973996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, using an inuring spell that shoots a bullet made of compressed air through their heads or just burn them to death with an inure fireball.<br /> <br /> I even ask this on the question thread. You kill someone once, loss wisdom once...then inure the spell used and from now on you can kill anyone with that spell and no wisdom loss. Isnt that how it works?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is the intended use. the only draw back is the extra paradox dice that gets rolled. and you always have to roll that paradox. You can spend mana to make it a chance die thou. I believe the intent was that every next time you throw that spell, you're not wholly in control of it as a player. The GM is more than encouraged to signal, Hey something is really not right here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":".  clarfication 09-21-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:37:08-07:00","id":974004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973982#post973982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well i would argue that while more &quot;realistic&quot; they are less compelling, they just black hats.... no moral dilema to put a bullet in their heads and go for Mcdonalds afterwards except for the whole artificial morality mechanic which now can be bypassed with unuring.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the usual moral dilemma that comes with driving bullets through peoples heads.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:54:09-07:00","id":974013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974004#post974004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the usual moral dilemma that comes with driving bullets through peoples heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats kind of my point there isnt a moral dilema really, the seers are black hats with no redeeming quality. Killing them is like killing a the bad guys from the purge.<br /> <br /> Take something like american history X, the bad guy is the equivalent of a seer but the only reason one can really empathize with him is that as an audience we are &quot;force&quot; (in the sense that by the nature of watching a movie we are spectators and cant intervene) to watch the hows and whys of the main character. Roleplaying dont really have that, unless the dm wants to interrupt the flow of the game to tell the story of an NPCs around the campfire.<br /> <br /> The players will only see what the NPC is doing and to what end he is doing it and maybe the whys from his pov/others povs. And all of those answers are gonna put him on the same box than kobolds in their minds because again black hats.<br /> <br /> Again, i dont have a problem with that. The Seers just dont shine on their moral complexity they are just cowards, greedy or evil, and as villans those are very boring motivations (they are surprisingly good motivations for pcs though). They shine on their cool powers and methods.<br /> <br /> Personally i just either run like that and make them evil kobolds with no morally redeeming qualities to them and just wait for the PCs to off them while banking on the obstacles that they throw around to enchance a game. Or ignore the devs word and run the &quot;protecting the status quo for the &quot;greater good&quot; &quot; angle for symphatetic seers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:12:54-07:00","id":974022,"title":"","content":"I'm not really quite sure what other moral dilemma you're talking about if you aren't talking about the usual taboo about killing other people. While they're the 'bad guys', it isn't like they all go around eating babies or something. It's pretty much the same moral dilemma as killing a bunch of people working for any other shitty company really. Honestly, going around killing every Seer you come across because they're the 'bad guys' will almost certainly make you worse far worse than most of the people you end up killing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:18:12-07:00","id":974024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973995#post973995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, premeditated murder does ping at Medium, going by the guidelines, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was changed, so that planned was okay, but unplanned was not? (Note-to-self: Reread Wisdom rules without glossing over the examples)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:18:49-07:00","id":974026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973982#post973982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well i would argue that while more &quot;realistic&quot; they are less compelling, they just black hats.... no moral dilema to put a bullet in their heads and go for Mcdonalds afterwards except for the whole artificial morality mechanic which now can be bypassed with unuring.<br /> <br /> They are the death eater of harry potter basically minus an urgent agenda. And i mean that both on the good and the bad. They are less morally interesting than the technocracy or most left handed paths but they shine on their methodologies and tricks, like their yantras called chains (or was shackles?) to the profane urin and something incredible insidious.<br /> <br /> Just like the Death eaters with their mask, a spells that kill people and snake motiffs.<br /> <br /> Still i dont see the problem with Gecko modifying the game to his liking, his way of asking non-whistanding.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree.<br /> <br /> Going back to the analogy of Seers as greedy and immoral (and often somewhat cartoonish) tobacco or oil executives, would you similarly accept it poses no moral dilemma to also &quot;put a bullet in their heads&quot; in real life? It still sounds like cold-blooded murder to me, no matter how vile you find their outlook or actions. If a Pentacle mage held such a moral perspective, I would find them little better than the Seers they claim to despise.<br /> <br /> Arrogance and hubris afflict all mages, no just Seers. As I indicated earlier, at least Seers generally understand their evil while other mages spout pleasant rhetoric while living in denial of the own evil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973982#post973982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well i would argue that while more &quot;realistic&quot; they are less compelling, they just black hats.... no moral dilema to put a bullet in their heads and go for Mcdonalds afterwards except for the whole artificial morality mechanic which now can be bypassed with unuring.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSeers are still people, and what you suggest is still murder.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-21-2016, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:19:38-07:00","id":974027,"title":"","content":"I still don't get how a psychologically &quot;realistic&quot; character would have no qualms about killing another person. Especially as there might be people who care about them. CofD isn't D&amp;D - &quot;killing bad guys is good&quot; doesn't work here.<br /> <br /> A Seer might be evil but not evil enough to warrant capital penalty, you'd skill go for the kill rote ? He might have a familiy who love and maybe even he loves them, he could even a good father for his kids, still taking the lethal route ? Some of them might be actually repentant but too deep in the shit to just quit. You can give them depth without making them less evil.<br /> <br /> Besides I for once find green and cowardice a bit of a welcome freshness. The whole &quot;well intentioned extremist&quot; shtick is getting quite cliche nowadays.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:19:40-07:00","id":974028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974013#post974013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats kind of my point there isnt a moral dilema really, the seers are black hats with no redeeming quality. Killing them is like killing a the bad guys from the purge.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I can kill these guys without a qualm because they're assholes&quot; is pretty much murderous Hubris incarnate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:42:57-07:00","id":974038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974024#post974024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that was changed, so that planned was okay, but unplanned was not? (Note-to-self: Reread Wisdom rules without glossing over the examples)</div> </div> </div> </div>Planned is a sin against medium Wisdom, killing in a rage is against low Wisdom; the difference is acknowledged, just... Yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974027#post974027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't get how a psychologically &amp;quot;realistic&amp;quot; character would have no qualms about killing another person. Especially as there might be people who care about them. CofD isn't D&amp;D - &amp;quot;killing bad guys is good&amp;quot; doesn't work here.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, a thousand times over. I wrote up a long post on this but erased it. It cannot be stressed enough, though, how ingrained the urge not to kill is in humans. To this day, armies struggle to try and drill soldiers so that killing is reflexive, rather than thoughtful, because the majority of soldiers do not want to kill. Ever. They look down the sights, see a person, and aim to miss.<br /> <br /> People who can kill without issue are psychopaths. Killing is horrifying to every sane human being, and those who manage to do it either do so from a need to survive, an urge to protect, or a complete inability to see other people as humans.<br /> <br /> Even in times of war and the worst attrocities, executions are done from behind or with the face hidden.<br /> <br /> Even if you believe a Seer deserves death, carrying it out should always be anothef matter entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:45:11-07:00","id":974042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974022#post974022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really quite sure what other moral dilemma you're talking about if you aren't talking about the usual taboo about killing other people. While they're the 'bad guys', it isn't like they all go around eating babies or something. It's pretty much the same moral dilemma as killing a bunch of people working for any other shitty company really. Honestly, going around killing every Seer you come across because they're the 'bad guys' will almost certainly make you worse far worse than most of the people you end up killing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant player &quot;morality&quot;. See, the morality system force the characters to the &quot;killing is always wrong&quot; however, im talking about player interest/engament. Players meet an antagonist and if they can see &quot;good&quot; in them then they question whether to off them or not, the morality mechanic is more a speed bump on the whole issue than anything else.<br /> <br /> The seers do bad things for bad ends for all the wrong reasons so players, put them on the same mental box as kobolds. They arent morally engaging as NPCs, unless one ignore the Dev intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974028#post974028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I can kill these guys without a qualm because they're assholes&quot; is pretty much murderous Hubris incarnate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone to cuts you on traffic is an asshole. Someone that robs people is an asshole. Someone who works for human misery just for its own sake to appeal to elder gods that want to keep said human misery running and fresh is a step up from &quot;asshole&quot;. And players tend to think that way in the &quot;I kill this NPCs because they are undemable monsters&quot; mentality","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:04:52-07:00","id":974050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974042#post974042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone to cuts you on traffic is an asshole. Someone that robs people is an asshole. Someone who works for human misery just for its own sake to appeal to elder gods that want to keep said human misery running and fresh is a step up from &quot;asshole&quot;. And players tend to think that way in the &quot;I kill this NPCs because they are undemable monsters&quot; mentality</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all players think that way, particularly when playing more mature rpg's like the CofD games. Your group can certainly alter things however they wish, but the setting and rules as designed and intended assume a more realistic tone and a lot more than 1990's comic book and Dungeons &amp; Dragons hack'n'slash ethics and morality.<br /> <br /> Unless everyone agrees to setting changes, if I were the ST, I would make it explicitly clear that the characters were acting like psychopaths, often worse than Seers, and then penalize their Wisdom and impose other appropriate negative narrative reminders that the CofD is not supposed to be a Punisher comic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:05:54-07:00","id":974051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974027#post974027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Seer might be evil but not evil enough to warrant capital penalty, you'd skill go for the kill rote ? He might have a familiy who love and maybe even he loves them, he could even a good father for his kids, still taking the lethal route ? Some of them might be actually repentant but too deep in the shit to just quit. You can give them depth without making them less evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine and good in a novel but in a game, should i detract from every story to show the family, friends and pets of all the seers the player off? After the 2nd time is gonna lost is luster if there was even one the first time around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974027#post974027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides I for once find green and cowardice a bit of a welcome freshness. The whole &quot;well intentioned extremist&quot; shtick is getting quite cliche nowadays.</div> </div> </div> </div>That another matter, yes the well intentioned extremist is done a lot nowadays more than the &quot;moustache twirling&quot;. Emperor palpatine is a great villan but never for his moral complexity but because of his methods, his manipulations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974038#post974038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, a thousand times over. I wrote up a long post on this but erased it. It cannot be stressed enough, though, how ingrained the urge not to kill is in humans. To this day, armies struggle to try and drill soldiers so that killing is reflexive, rather than thoughtful, because the majority of soldiers do not want to kill. Ever. They look down the sights, see a person, and aim to miss.<br /> <br /> People who can kill without issue are psychopaths. Killing is horrifying to every sane human being, and those who manage to do it either do so from a need to survive, an urge to protect, or a complete inability to see other people as humans.<br /> <br /> Even in times of war and the worst attrocities, executions are done from behind or with the face hidden.<br /> <br /> Even if you believe a Seer deserves death, carrying it out should always be anothef matter entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet from a player perspective that is kind of unsusteinable on the long run. So players encounter a seers and, just happen one of them have a character with a high morality (not necesarily the mechanic one) and we RP the shit out of the dilema of not killing a seer. Which is good rp, i have player highly moralistic pcs before and can be good.<br /> <br /> However after the 5th time or after it comes to bite the party in the ass players tend to resort to violence. And the kind of atrocities the seers do tend to speed that process. While psycologically might be ingrained to not kill other humans there is a reason combat is a huge mechanic of most roleplaying game, few players even care about the psycologist data that human killing is an ingrained nono and more dont believe than either. And those that do would rp that anyway regardless of seers or not seers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:15:02-07:00","id":974059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974050#post974050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless everyone agrees to setting changes, if I were the ST, I would make it explicitly clear that the characters were acting like psychopaths, often worse than Seers, and then penalize their Wisdom and impose other appropriate negative narrative reminders that the CofD is not supposed to be a Punisher comic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh i barely alter anything, my houserules are just reach option at arcanum 2 for upgrading bashing damage to lethal. There is no setting changes, when the seers come at them they throw fireballs or whatever to defend themselves and the seer die. Life or death, or the seers attack indirectly until the mage find then and then they kill them or capture them followed by a sumary execution by the guardians.<br /> <br /> But say, how would mages deal with seers gunning for them? There very few and mostly unsustainable means to lock up a mage. Soul stone is kinda worse than killing them morally speaking, forcing them to multilate their souls is by the setting worse than just off them. Black mail if possible, and thats a big if, is temporal measure and one that would not fly with more &quot;honorable&quot; pcs (and there is whole order of them). You can knock them out and they would return next time and maybe next time they dice would net them a victory.<br /> <br /> Again the wisdom penalty is bypasses by inuring. As for the social problem from the &quot;stigma&quot; of killing a seers, now that is changing the setting. All the orders go out of their way to deshumanize the seers. If a cabal fights a seer cabal and kills them, the diamond cannot condemn them. Their society is largely defined by the war with the exarch and their soldiers the seers.<br /> <br /> As an aside note. Why go out of your way to punish the players for killing a being that the players and setting dont find morally compelling? If one wants to use morally compelling antagonist there are other diamond cabals, there are some banishers, or even some left handed legacy mages. But the killing the seer should have the same moral impact than shooting down a klan member running at you with a machete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":".  Better wording 09-21-2016, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:27:28-07:00","id":974064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973751#post973751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Seers have a good argument for being right, then why does the book explicitly say that all Seers know they're wrong?<br /> <br /> &quot;No mage serves the Throne out of altruism. Even the deluded or willfully ignorant find themselves quickly disabused of notions of fighting the good fight.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because heroism and self-sacrifice is a fool's errand, particularly so when such pursuits mean nothing in the face of a reality that already bent knee to the forces of tyranny. Or so Seers believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:23:57-07:00","id":974096,"title":"","content":"LRS has a point about player psychology vs. real life and anyway Mage doesn't care if you're a psychopath. If you inured a murder spell then you don't ping Wisdom for using it. Morality isn't a factor except via peer pressure and most in the Pentacle won't lose much sleep over a bunch of Seers being offed.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> You can go the humanizing route for Seers, or the &quot;kobold&quot; route, and there's also a third way: Make Seers act in the interest of the players with enough frequency that they are reluctant to kill someone they have a working relationship with. Or there's the posthumous relationship where a Seer dies with a secret the players need, and he's ghost-proofed himself. There may be other variations as well. I'd mix and match.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:33:55-07:00","id":974103,"title":"","content":"Guys, can we skip the Seer argument for the umpteenth time. Dave has made it clear how the Seers were designed from a developers standpoint. The book makes clear the in world standpoint. If someone sees that and can't make it work for them, reexplaining won't provide erudition, it just provides a wall to bounce the same complaints against endlessly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:41:16-07:00","id":974109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974059#post974059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh i barely alter anything, my houserules are just reach option at arcanum 2 for upgrading bashing damage to lethal. There is no setting changes, when the seers come at them they throw fireballs or whatever to defend themselves and the seer die. Life or death, or the seers attack indirectly until the mage find then and then they kill them or capture them followed by a sumary execution by the guardians.<br /> <br /> But say, how would mages deal with seers gunning for them? There very few and mostly unsustainable means to lock up a mage. Soul stone is kinda worse than killing them morally speaking, forcing them to multilate their souls is by the setting worse than just off them. Black mail if possible, and thats a big if, is temporal measure and one that would not fly with more &quot;honorable&quot; pcs (and there is whole order of them). You can knock them out and they would return next time and maybe next time they dice would net them a victory.<br /> <br /> Again the wisdom penalty is bypasses by inuring. As for the social problem from the &quot;stigma&quot; of killing a seers, now that is changing the setting. All the orders go out of their way to deshumanize the seers. If a cabal fights a seer cabal and kills them, the diamond cannot condemn them. Their society is largely defined by the war with the exarch and their soldiers the seers.<br /> <br /> As an aside note. Why go out of your way to punish the players for killing a being that the players and setting dont find morally compelling? If one wants to use morally compelling antagonist there are other diamond cabals, there are some banishers, or even some left handed legacy mages. But the killing the seer should have the same moral impact than shooting down a klan member running at you with a machete.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was my impression that outright direct and destructive combat between Pentacle and Seer mages is quite rare for much of the same reason its rare among Pentacle society (and the reason for Consilia), it's far too dangerous and potentially lethal. There's little upside, and the CofD is not a superhero or fantasy setting (and such combat and destruction is hard to hide from the rest of the world). I viewed the machinations of each group more akin to a Cold War scenario with battles for influence and power and actual and infrequent combat usually through proxies, cultists and dupes.<br /> <br /> By your descriptions of circumstances, perspectives and the in-character morality and ethics of your player group, it sounds like you approach your CofD chronicles far more like comic urban fantasy rather than gritty, somewhat realistic, modern horror. You should certainly play as you wish and enjoy yourselves, but I believe its not the setting as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:12:00-07:00","id":974123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974109#post974109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It was my impression that outright direct and destructive combat between Pentacle and Seer mages is quite rare for much of the same reason its rare among Pentacle society (and the reason for Consilia), it's far too dangerous and potentially lethal. There's little upside, and the CofD is not a superhero or fantasy setting (and such combat and destruction is hard to hide from the rest of the world). I viewed the machinations of each group more akin to a Cold War scenario with battles for influence and power and actual and infrequent combat usually through proxies, cultists and dupes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you are talking about political convenience and not moral. I never said the seers didnt function as antagonist but that they dont function as morally compelling ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974109#post974109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By your descriptions of circumstances, perspectives and the in-character morality and ethics of your player group, it sounds like you approach your CofD chronicles far more like comic urban fantasy rather than gritty, somewhat realistic, modern horror. You should certainly play as you wish and enjoy yourselves, but I believe its not the setting as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit<br /> <br /> Seers as intended are bastard, unredemable (as an organization) bastards with cool toys and tricks. Nothing more to them. Your example of the politics of fighting the seers? Thats also tricks, not morality.<br /> <br /> And so far you havent argue how they are morally compelling antagonist, you just throw the cliche &quot;all lives matter&quot; which thats not something intrinsic to the seers but to everyone. That dont make the seer function as morally grey antagonist because is aside from their character and more about the character of everyone but them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":".  Not gonna lower myself to branford level 09-21-2016, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:15:26-07:00","id":974126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974096#post974096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LRS has a point about player psychology vs. real life and anyway Mage doesn't care if you're a psychopath. If you inured a murder spell then you don't ping Wisdom for using it. Morality isn't a factor except via peer pressure and most in the Pentacle won't lose much sleep over a bunch of Seers being offed.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> You can go the humanizing route for Seers, or the &quot;kobold&quot; route, and there's also a third way: Make Seers act in the interest of the players with enough frequency that they are reluctant to kill someone they have a working relationship with. Or there's the posthumous relationship where a Seer dies with a secret the players need, and he's ghost-proofed himself. There may be other variations as well. I'd mix and match.</div> </div> </div> </div>thats a good advice to use them, if difficult as it depends on the context. I had use all of the ways to great effect so far.<br /> <br /> From the bastard seer who was black hat as they come. To the useful friend seer, who even managed to sway a pc to their side and even said screw the setting and put a honest to god(s) &quot;i do what i do for the greater good&quot; seer of the gate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:34:57-07:00","id":974161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974059#post974059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh i barely alter anything, my houserules are just reach option at arcanum 2 for upgrading bashing damage to lethal. There is no setting changes, when the seers come at them they throw fireballs or whatever to defend themselves and the seer die. Life or death, or the seers attack indirectly until the mage find then and then they kill them or capture them followed by a sumary execution by the guardians.<br /> <br /> But say, how would mages deal with seers gunning for them? There very few and mostly unsustainable means to lock up a mage. Soul stone is kinda worse than killing them morally speaking, forcing them to multilate their souls is by the setting worse than just off them. Black mail if possible, and thats a big if, is temporal measure and one that would not fly with more &quot;honorable&quot; pcs (and there is whole order of them). You can knock them out and they would return next time and maybe next time they dice would net them a victory.<br /> <br /> Again the wisdom penalty is bypasses by inuring. As for the social problem from the &quot;stigma&quot; of killing a seers, now that is changing the setting. All the orders go out of their way to deshumanize the seers. If a cabal fights a seer cabal and kills them, the diamond cannot condemn them. Their society is largely defined by the war with the exarch and their soldiers the seers.<br /> <br /> As an aside note. Why go out of your way to punish the players for killing a being that the players and setting dont find morally compelling? If one wants to use morally compelling antagonist there are other diamond cabals, there are some banishers, or even some left handed legacy mages. But the killing the seer should have the same moral impact than shooting down a klan member running at you with a machete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see, they could knock him out and deliver him to the proper authorities who likely have a jail cell made to hold Seers.<br /> They could maim him, and take a piece of him like a bloody hand or arm. Remind him if he tries anything the others will blast him out of existence because they all now have sympathy with him.<br /> Put him in a persistent sleep until he receives true loves kiss, or some other equally unlikely series of events. I don't know, a sincere compliment from Donald Trump? Pick your poison. It just has to be possible not likely.<br /> <br /> The point is they don't have to kill him...in fact crippling him actually is safer on your Wisdom than killing him.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:42:08-07:00","id":974168,"title":"","content":"You're missing LRS' point.<br /> <br /> You're also wrong about it dinging Wisdom as long as they kill the Seer using an Inured Spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:52:46-07:00","id":974175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974168#post974168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing LRS' point.<br /> <br /> You're also wrong about it dinging Wisdom as long as they kill the Seer using an Inured Spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming no Inured spells at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T19:23:20-07:00","id":974187,"title":"","content":"Then it dings your Wisdom the first time and never again because if that's your go-to pattern of behavior you Inure that right away. Also, since LRS was assuming inurement then you're not actually engaging in a mutual discussion by bringing assumptions that don't match its parameters.<br /> <br /> Regardless of even that, you still missed LRS' point, and that's actually the bigger issue with your post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T20:55:14-07:00","id":974214,"title":"","content":"The definition of 'morally compelling&quot; seems to shift with the wind and strikes me as falling into a larger internet fallacy derived from dreams, ghosts, and half-remembered community college English 101 courses; the fallacy bastardizes &quot;it's generally better in stories when antagonists are, for one reason or another, interesting&quot; to &quot;an antagonist or villain who is clearly doing harm is ONE-DIMENSIONAL.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a nonsense, and nobody is obligated to entertain it.<br /> <br /> People on the internet love to froth about &quot;mustache twirling,&quot; and yet some of our favorite villains in fiction do exactly that. &quot;But mustache-twirling isn't realistic!&quot; (More properly, it doesn't adhere to that person's expressed notions about strict realism - but sadists do exist!) It's true, though, that most harm in the world isn't caused by gleeful, thorough-going sadists; but then, neither is it caused by misguided idealists or super-secret good guys. It's inflicted by workaday people punching a clock at EvilCo because they're scared of the personal consequences for them if they were to ever stop. Some of them like money and power, but even those people have people they love and who love them in return.<br /> <br /> If someone's players are treating those people like kobolds, that sure seems to me like a player problem and not like an anyone else problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:14:30-07:00","id":974256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974042#post974042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant player &quot;morality&quot;. See, the morality system force the characters to the &quot;killing is always wrong&quot; however, im talking about player interest/engament. Players meet an antagonist and if they can see &quot;good&quot; in them then they question whether to off them or not, the morality mechanic is more a speed bump on the whole issue than anything else.<br /> <br /> The seers do bad things for bad ends for all the wrong reasons so players, put them on the same mental box as kobolds. They arent morally engaging as NPCs, unless one ignore the Dev intent.<br /> <br /> Someone to cuts you on traffic is an asshole. Someone that robs people is an asshole. Someone who works for human misery just for its own sake to appeal to elder gods that want to keep said human misery running and fresh is a step up from &quot;asshole&quot;. And players tend to think that way in the &quot;I kill this NPCs because they are undemable monsters&quot; mentality</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're calling Wisdom a &quot;morality&quot; system, then you're missing the point entirely. Wisdom is not morality, it's self-control. Killing someone is a wisdom violation not because it's immoral, but because it's reckless. It's an irrevocable action with far-reaching consequences. That person could have an important destiny, or could have friends and family who will be hurt by his death, or who will go out to avenge him. That's why premeditated murder is more wise than manslaughter. Contemplating at least some of the consequences of a murder shows more self-control than just wildly acting out on emotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:17:34-07:00","id":974257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974214#post974214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The definition of 'morally compelling&quot; seems to shift with the wind and strikes me as falling into a larger internet fallacy derived from dreams, ghosts, and half-remembered community college English 101 courses; the fallacy bastardizes &quot;it's generally better in stories when antagonists are, for one reason or another, interesting&quot; to &quot;an antagonist or villain who is clearly doing harm is ONE-DIMENSIONAL.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a nonsense, and nobody is obligated to entertain it.<br /> <br /> People on the internet love to froth about &quot;mustache twirling,&quot; and yet some of our favorite villains in fiction do exactly that. &quot;But mustache-twirling isn't realistic!&quot; (More properly, it doesn't adhere to that person's expressed notions about strict realism - but sadists do exist!) It's true, though, that most harm in the world isn't caused by gleeful, thorough-going sadists; but then, neither is it caused by misguided idealists or super-secret good guys. It's inflicted by workaday people punching a clock at EvilCo because they're scared of the personal consequences for them if they were to ever stop. Some of them like money and power, but even those people have people they love and who love them in return.<br /> <br /> If someone's players are treating those people like kobolds, that sure seems to me like a player problem and not like an anyone else problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you are contradicting yourself, some of our favorite villans are indeed moustache twirling villans like for example Palpatine, the emperor from Star Wars. But also killing palpatine has the same emotional dilema than killing kobolds (with exception that should be done dispassionately, because the force). Palpatine bites it, nobody in the audience cry his death and the setting is better for it.<br /> <br /> I never said that them being not morally compelling villans makes them not work as villans, and for the sake of you little internet fallacy i meant the trope of the possible &quot;misguided idealist&quot; or the &quot;decent people in bad organization for a good goal&quot;, just that they are &quot;that&quot;, moustache twirling. They are as you said moustache twirling villans and they have a certain use in a game but their appeal lays outside of their morality. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974256#post974256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're calling Wisdom a &quot;morality&quot; system, then you're missing the point entirely. Wisdom is not morality, it's self-control. Killing someone is a wisdom violation not because it's immoral, but because it's reckless. It's an irrevocable action with far-reaching consequences. That person could have an important destiny, or could have friends and family who will be hurt by his death, or who will go out to avenge him. That's why premeditated murder is more wise than manslaughter. Contemplating at least some of the consequences of a murder shows more self-control than just wildly acting out on emotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay if you wanna be retentive then fine.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>I meant player &quot;morality&quot;. See, the WISDOM system force the characters to the &quot;Various forms of killing is wrong in different WISDOM scales&quot; however, im talking about player interest/engament. Players meet an antagonist and if they can see &quot;good&quot; in them then they question whether to off them or not, the WISDOM mechanic is more a speed bump on the whole issue than anything else.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The seers do bad things for bad ends for all the wrong reasons so players, put them on the same mental box as kobolds. They arent morally engaging as NPCs, unless one ignore the Dev intent.</i><br /> <br /> There obviously a mechanic that emulates the elements of scaling morality system of the other game lines cannot be simplified with the term morality mechanic. Just like Harmony is not a morality mechanic and humanity is not a morality mechanic etc etc. Good that i change that, the entire sense of what i wrote change now that i replace Morality mechanic with WISDOM mechanic! Good that you catch that one! Even though i wasnt really talking about the WISDOM mechanic and more about how players tend to catalog adversaries and player &quot;morality&quot; which has no rules or system and nothing to do with the WISDOM mechanic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-22-2016, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:26:22-07:00","id":974259,"title":"","content":"Antagonists don't have to be either captain planet villains or well-meaning extremists. It's not the 90s any more. They can be morally in the wrong while still being human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:36:47-07:00","id":974263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974259#post974259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can be morally in the wrong while still being human.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or in the CofD, *mostly* human. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:44:57-07:00","id":974266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974259#post974259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antagonists don't have to be either captain planet villains or well-meaning extremists. It's not the 90s any more. They can be morally in the wrong while still being human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can they be human characters? Sure. Would most player care for them? Difficult at best. Most fiction focusing on villans force the spectator to follow along the villans to see their whole story. A game session cannot do that without stopping the narrative to showcase the life story of Seers number 23345. Or, in a format like PBP which is another beast.<br /> <br /> The main character are the players, otherwise is just showcasing GMPCs or NPCs, and as such unless is for a specific purpose then the players will not see the origin/process of the villan. They just see how their actions affect the &quot;world&quot;, whether is good/bad and whether they run contrary to the players goals. The first 2 are bad by the nature of what the seers do, and while the last one depends on the agenda of the seers. If used as antagonist then they are also bad. Checking those 3 boxes they go on the kobold box in players minds.<br /> <br /> Kobolds have feelings too, one could probably run the trials and kobold harship of kobold society but there are really more &quot;morally compelling&quot; villans than the kobolds to use for that. If i want a grey vs black shades of morality conflict....seers. If i want a Grey vs Grey shades of morality conflict pentacle vs pentacle. Grey vs darker grey shades of morality conflict Left handed paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-22-2016, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:59:57-07:00","id":974270,"title":"","content":"Alright, you keep using the words morally compelling, but I'm fairly sure you're using that phrase with a rather specific meaning in mind. Would you care to elaborate in what you mean by that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T00:32:26-07:00","id":974278,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Seers are a little underwhelming, and Dave B pretty much said in this thread that they hard coded them a certain way so people wouldn't try running around saying they were the real heroes of the setting. I guess the authors and fans had a dissonance in their values/beliefs, so they intentionally misread a book to flip the script as kind of a jab at the authors. Those games were before my time though so I am not sure if that is exactly how it went down. I think its a little heavy handed, but I actually want to work with the Seers as they are written.<br /> <br /> I would say in the Seers defense though, is that almost everyone can be sympathetic, even Stalin has an interesting story, and even has some admirable qualities. I wonder, if I grew up in Russia during that time, how good of a government could I have put together? Was anything I wanted from a government even possible during that time? Or would the slow decent into paranoia and decades of brutal warfare turn me into a soul-less man of steal, if I was even strong enough to survive? <br /> <br /> If you want a sympathetic villain, just think about what people's constraints are and what incentives they face. You just have to ask yourself, what would you do in their shoes? Yeah, you will come out either estimating that you are stronger than them, and feel disgusted by their weakness, or you will come out realizing that you are weaker than them and try to use that fear and guilt to improve yourself, or maybe you will find that your moral judgement was incorrect and there was no better solution. Any of these ways its a powerful experience.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I would probably be a Seer for a time. Then probably leave after something freaked me out and turn into a banisher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","user":"AForgeForThoughts","date":".  EDIT: Removed some random tired-man sentences 09-22-2016, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T01:40:26-07:00","id":974296,"title":"","content":"That reminds me, being a Banisher isn't strictly tied to having Integrity instead of Wisdom and Mages have evidence (or at least strong suspicions) that it can act like a contagion. Killing most of the Seers you run into could put you at a higher risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T02:09:58-07:00","id":974297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974296#post974296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me, being a Banisher isn't strictly tied to having Integrity instead of Wisdom and Mages have evidence (or at least strong suspicions) that it can act like a contagion. Killing most of the Seers you run into could put you at a higher risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now imagine extremist Libertine that is 'Seer-Hunter', slowly turning into proper Banisher... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T02:40:07-07:00","id":974306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974257#post974257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said that them being not morally compelling villans makes them not work as villans, and for the sake of you little internet fallacy i meant the trope of the possible &quot;misguided idealist&quot; or the &quot;decent people in bad organization for a good goal&quot;, just that they are &quot;that&quot;, moustache twirling. They are as you said moustache twirling villans and they have a certain use in a game but their appeal lays outside of their morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let me break down the pushback you're getting here.<br /> <br /> - People disagree that Seers are, by default, &quot;mustache-twirling.&quot; I think some, especially higher-level ones, undoubtedly are - we know in real life that power, money, and insulation from consequences positively correlate with sociopathic behavior - but you seem to be not responding to the point that lots of Seers are there because they're afraid or they just don't really care enough about the world outside of their bubble of safety. As people keep pointing out.<br /> <br /> - Most people don't seem to think that being a member of a straightforwardly villainous organization automatically translates to being an unrepentant sadist.<br /> <br /> - Most people don't seem to think that being a member of a straightforwardly villainous organization automatically entitles anyone to come around and shoot you.<br /> <br /> And I would add that if your players' characters are inuring themselves against Wisdom loss from murder so they can go commit more effective murder, then you've <i>had</i> the morality debate, and morality lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T02:48:58-07:00","id":974308,"title":"","content":"Anyway, I feel like the fact that we're having a discussion about how a dude's players are using the game mechanics to turn themselves into more effective remorseless killers is its own commentary on the question of where the horror is in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T03:36:01-07:00","id":974323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974257#post974257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay if you wanna be retentive then fine.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>I meant player &quot;morality&quot;. See, the WISDOM system force the characters to the &quot;Various forms of killing is wrong in different WISDOM scales&quot; however, im talking about player interest/engament. Players meet an antagonist and if they can see &quot;good&quot; in them then they question whether to off them or not, the WISDOM mechanic is more a speed bump on the whole issue than anything else.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely disagree. I think the Wisdom system is 100% in-character and doing its job. In this case, the Wisdom system is making the players think again about what they're about to do and ask if it's really the right choice, even if for the wrong reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T07:25:13-07:00","id":975503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974270#post974270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, you keep using the words morally compelling, but I'm fairly sure you're using that phrase with a rather specific meaning in mind. Would you care to elaborate in what you mean by that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like i did right here you mean?<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974257#post974257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said that them being not morally compelling villans makes them not work as villans, and for the sake of you little internet fallacy i meant the trope of the possible &quot;misguided idealist&quot; or the &quot;decent people in bad organization for a good goal&quot;, just that they are &quot;that&quot;, moustache twirling. They are as you said moustache twirling villans and they have a certain use in a game but their appeal lays outside of their morality.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974306#post974306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- People disagree that Seers are, by default, &quot;mustache-twirling.&quot; I think some, especially higher-level ones, undoubtedly are - we know in real life that power, money, and insulation from consequences positively correlate with sociopathic behavior - but you seem to be not responding to the point that lots of Seers are there because they're afraid or they just don't really care enough about the world outside of their bubble of safety. As people keep pointing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those people are <u>kinda</u> wrong even the dev have said they are bastard coated bastards. And yes, there are seers that join out of fear however....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974306#post974306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Most people don't seem to think that being a member of a straightforwardly villainous organization automatically translates to being an unrepentant sadist.<br /> <br /> - Most people don't seem to think that being a member of a straightforwardly villainous organization automatically entitles anyone to come around and shoot you.</div> </div> </div> </div>See this is the part of people are death wrong, im not talking about your Real life morality on whether is good or bad to kill someone or whether in Real life society is right or wrong because that depends on each person and society. Hell my country is considering running over and then beating to death a robber as an acceptable solution but i am not talking about Real life or &quot;real life psychology&quot; i am talking about player (not character) psycology.<br /> <br /> See there are morally compelling bad guys characters in fiction but 90% of those are the protagonist because we can see their process and the exact circunstances and feeling of why they reach that point.<br /> <br /> A neo nazi? American history X.<br /> A drug producer? Breaking Bad.<br /> A serial killer? Dexter.<br /> Staling/hitler? Some movie about them.<br /> <br /> Even in those fiction in which the bad guys arent the protagonist like say, criminal minds, we as an audience watch the hows and whys of the serial killer. However in an RPG thats different, the &quot;camera&quot; is always on the PCs and while one can interrupt the flow to show the infancy of seer bad guy number #99888 it seems poor form to interrupt the game to start relating the backstory of a bad guy to show &quot;oh yeah he might be a good guy but he is a coward so he is not that bad&quot;.<br /> <br /> Players will see a bad guy, that oppose them for the wrong reason and are a blight for the world (they might not a sadist but the seers as an organization is a cancer), and the setting completely dehumanize them and yes the wisdom system is a speedbump to artificially tell them &quot;oh you shouldnt kill this guys because wisdom loss&quot; but in players (again, not characters) minds they already check them in the kobold box.<br /> <br /> Then the only question is how as players OOC can they bypass the artificial speedbump the game chooses to impose in them and the political obstacles.<br /> <br /> So all that issues for forcing sympathy on the seers as cowards cogs in the evil machine or just selfish which as per fiction tendencies nowadays is already more work than is worth. In the post occupy wall street movement fiction tends to deshumanize those kind of characters.<br /> <br /> When in most shows there is a storyline about a criminal who lost his family on what not because of those people and then he hunts them down, its kinda difficult to not want him to &quot;win&quot; and get his revenge with the only counter argument is the justice system which is absent on mage society. Can i show the seers coming home and having a family? Sure. Does it make a difference? Not really, the seers agenda is counter to the players and there is no compromise unless i wanna shit on the setting (that is a perfect way to do it btw i am all about ignoring the devs), the seers get the order to boycott the players plan and he has to do it, using a cheap shot like showing the seer having 4 kids and a wife in perfect house and him being a perfect dad is just that, a cheap shot, to try to force sympathy on the players (again, no the characters) while them knowing full well the seer will have to carry on his plans because of orders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=974161#post974161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's see, they could knock him out and deliver him to the proper authorities who likely have a jail cell made to hold Seers.<br /> They could maim him, and take a piece of him like a bloody hand or arm. Remind him if he tries anything the others will blast him out of existence because they all now have sympathy with him.<br /> Put him in a persistent sleep until he receives true loves kiss, or some other equally unlikely series of events. I don't know, a sincere compliment from Donald Trump? Pick your poison. It just has to be possible not likely.<br /> <br /> The point is they don't have to kill him...in fact crippling him actually is safer on your Wisdom than killing him.</div> </div> </div> </div>The proper authorities (Guardians of the veil mostly) who would interrogate the seer and follow it with a sumary execution as there is not &quot;seers jail&quot; in the setting. Yes thats totally <u>morally</u> different<u>.</u><br /> <br /> Main him? Cutting their arms is better than killing him? Thats a level of deshumanizing the seer into the kobold level on the same page as killing them with the only difference is whether you think mutilating someone is more merciful than a quick death. Same with putting him on a induced coma. So thats a no.<br /> <br /> Yes those are ways to bypass the artificial wisdom, but also they are ways in which the PCs dehumanize the seers to the point of kobolds.<br /> <br /> So yes, the seers work best as moustache twirling villans. They dont have anything redemable about themselves and they are just death eaters. Cool magics, cool tricks, cool motifs and the players, except for artificial WISDOM system, wont care about if they have a point or not or that killing them is bad morally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-24-2016, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T08:07:35-07:00","id":975519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975503#post975503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like i did right here you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because what you quoted is a bit of rambling about how 'moustache twirling villains' aren't morally compelling while saying how they could still function as villains or something of the like. That still doesn't provide me with your definition of Morally Compelling, it just tells me one thing that you don't think fits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T08:50:06-07:00","id":975538,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a>: To be honest, it sounds like what you're having is a player problem, not an antagonist problem. If your players are looking at the antagonists as Kobolds to be killed without any consideration and without any remorse, it won't matter if they're &quot;morally compelling&quot; (whatever that means to you) or not. As you've repeatedly observed, the spotlight is always on the protagonists, the antagonists don't get enough &quot;screen time&quot; for the players to see their motivations. That doesn't change because the antagonists are misguided idealists. They can have the most &quot;morally compelling&quot; back stories you can imagine, it won't matter if the players have decided to play ChroD like its D&amp;D and label the antagonists as Always Chaotic Evil monsters that it's ok to murder on sight. They're never going to see those back stories or learn those motivations if they don't seek them out themselves.<br /> <br /> That aside, I would argue that the Seers are plenty morally compelling. Perhaps moreso than misguided idealists or well-intentioned extremists, since both tropes are so played out at this point. They're a more realistic brand of evil - the &quot;just following orders&quot; sort. The people who know they're working for a corrupt organization, but do it anyway because they have a great benefits package. And besides, its not like you choosing not to work for them will make any difference on the grand scheme - the organization will keep being corrupt without you, and they'll just hire someone else to replace you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:32:39-07:00","id":975580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975519#post975519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because what you quoted is a bit of rambling about how 'moustache twirling villains' aren't morally compelling while saying how they could still function as villains or something of the like. That still doesn't provide me with your definition of Morally Compelling, it just tells me one thing that you don't think fits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly i dont know what more definition of morally compelling do you want from me than &quot;i meant the trope of the possible &quot;misguided idealist&quot; or the &quot;decent people in bad organization for a good goal&quot;. Is that not clear enough for you i dont know what to tell you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975538#post975538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a>: To be honest, it sounds like what you're having is a player problem, not an antagonist problem. If your players are looking at the antagonists as Kobolds to be killed without any consideration and without any remorse, it won't matter if they're &quot;morally compelling&quot; (whatever that means to you) or not. As you've repeatedly observed, the spotlight is always on the protagonists, the antagonists don't get enough &quot;screen time&quot; for the players to see their motivations. That doesn't change because the antagonists are misguided idealists. They can have the most &quot;morally compelling&quot; back stories you can imagine, it won't matter if the players have decided to play ChroD like its D&amp;D and label the antagonists as Always Chaotic Evil monsters that it's ok to murder on sight. They're never going to see those back stories or learn those motivations if they don't seek them out themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does all the difference, when i throw them a Diamond cabal say both cabals looking for the same resource or one cabal takes offense to the players character cabal then the approach and player mentality change radically. They will talk it out, compromise or evel kill them as last resort in a fully sanctioned duel because the other orders dont even as cogs in the machine in a ways dont work to actively hurt the world as an organization the way the seers does.<br /> <br /> Even a left hand path, depending on context player tend to relate to them on one way or another while still condemn them or kill them. From an austere or a legion member so focused on his task that lost his way.<br /> <br /> And its really not a problem with the players or the seers. The seer work as unredeamable black hats and player react to them as such, they arent on the same level as the technocracy, but also the technocracy had to carry the whole bag of antagonists on their back for a long while (with the marauder and nephandi being a small part until revised), meanwhile the seers are just a tiny part of the antagonist bag sharing it with banisher, other pentacle mages, left hand paths, the abyss and the mad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975538#post975538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That aside, I would argue that the Seers are plenty morally compelling. Perhaps moreso than misguided idealists or well-intentioned extremists, since both tropes are so played out at this point. They're a more realistic brand of evil - the &quot;just following orders&quot; sort. The people who know they're working for a corrupt organization, but do it anyway because they have a great benefits package. And besides, its not like you choosing not to work for them will make any difference on the grand scheme - the organization will keep being corrupt without you, and they'll just hire someone else to replace you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe its something cultural? I dont know, my country and by extension my culture then to deshumanize the cogs in the corrupt machine to the point when we kinda want then to die in an horrible way or cheer when they do die. I just dont see it, i could see the &quot;is more realistic&quot; argument and even then is open for everyone definition of realistic but more compelling? More interesting? more &quot;realistic&quot; doesnt always mean more interesting and, using the harry potter comparison again, Peter Pettigrew doesnt seem very interesting because of his morals. Again maybe its a difference on culture or personality but i never heard anyone physically near me thinking the seers are more interesting morally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-24-2016, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:36:24-07:00","id":975583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975580#post975580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe its something cultural? I dont know, my country and by extension my culture then to deshumanize the cogs in the corrupt machine to the point when we kinda want the to die in an horrible way or cheer when they do die. I just dont see it, i could see the &quot;is more realistic&quot; argument and even then is open for everyone definition of realistic but more compelling? More interesting? more &quot;realistic&quot; doesnt always mean more interesting and, using the harry potter comparison again, Peter Pettigrew doesnt seem very interesting because of his morals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there's a ministry dedicated to cultivating that. An endless hatred of the 'machine' that leads to distrust at anyone who might take control.<br /> <br /> Dividing people is a victory just as much as bringing them together into single-mindedness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:11:49-07:00","id":975609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975580#post975580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does all the difference, when i throw them a Diamond cabal say both cabals looking for the same resource or one cabal takes offense to the players character cabal then the approach and player mentality change radically. They will talk it out, compromise or evel kill them as last resort in a fully sanctioned duel because the other orders dont even as cogs in the machine in a ways dont work to actively hurt the world as an organization the way the seers does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they do, they have an insider's view on the Diamond Orders. What I'm getting at is, even if you make the Seers the most sympathetic musguided idealists ever written, your players will never see that because there's still no &quot;screen time&quot; dedicated to showing them that. They're still just an out-group that the players are informed are the bad-guys, so if they're the sort of players to remorselessly kill &quot;bad-guys&quot;, they won't bother trying to learn the Seers' motivations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975580#post975580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even a left hand path, depending on context player tend to relate to them on one way or another while still condemn them or kill them. From an austere or a legion member so focused on his task that lost his way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, they've got reason to look into a Left-Handed Mage's motivations. They know that a Left-Handed Mage must have started out as a normal Mage and turned down a dark path, they naturally want to know why. And once they look into the reasons, they can humanize the Left-Handed Mage which makes it harder to justify killing them. But that only happens because they bother to look into it. Each and every Seer has a reason to have joined the Order, and it's usually not &quot;because I like to do evil.&quot; Usually, it's because they want to get by. Their most common motive is one of the most universally identifiable motivations out there, but the players will never look at it that way if you don't give them a reason to care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975580#post975580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe its something cultural? I dont know, my country and by extension my culture then to deshumanize the cogs in the corrupt machine to the point when we kinda want the to die in an horrible way or cheer when they do die.</div> </div> </div> </div>So everyone who takes a job at a big corporation so they can pay the bills and feed their kids is seen as deserving to die? Damn, that's cold. I assume no one supports these corporations there, then. No one in your country works at or eats from McDonalds without becoming a social pariah?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975580#post975580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just dont see it, i could see the &quot;is more realistic&quot; argument and even then is open for everyone definition of realistic but more compelling? More interesting? more &quot;realistic&quot; doesnt always mean more interesting and, using the harry potter comparison again, Peter Pettigrew doesnt seem very interesting because of his morals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Realism is compelling. It's not always more compelling than fiction, but like I said, the &quot;following orders&quot; villain trope isn't as played-out as the well-intentioned extremist or the misguided idealist. Peter Petegrew is absolutely an interesting character. He's not a <i>likable</i> character by any means, but you don't have to like a character to find them compelling. I pity Pettegrew, he's easily the most pathetic character in the series. And that pity makes me feel more for him than I do for, say, Bellatrix, who's just kind of in it for the murdering. You know who's another compelling character in Harry Potter who fits the Seer mentality? Lucius Malfoy. He's not a Death Eater because he likes being a bad guy, he's a Death Eater because he thinks it's the winning side. He sees more benefit for himself and his family in serving Voldemort than serving the Ministry. You know who else fits the Seer mentality? Severus everyone-excuses-the-fact-that-I-was-legit-Death-Eater-because-I-creeped-on-Lilly-and-switched-sides-when-Voldemort-killed-her Snape. From beginning to end, he served the side that he saw as benefiting him the most, it just happened that he valued his obsession with Lilly more than he valued the power Voldemort offered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-24-2016, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:56:22-07:00","id":975689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975580#post975580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly i dont know what more definition of morally compelling do you want from me than &quot;i meant the trope of the possible &quot;misguided idealist&quot; or the &quot;decent people in bad organization for a good goal&quot;. Is that not clear enough for you i dont know what to tell you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are <i>examples</i> not <i>definitions</i>, and even those examples only cover an extremely narrow view. What I'm getting from you is that if you can't fit villains into this narrow definition they aren't compelling <i>to you</i>, and you are entitled to your own opinion. <i>But, </i>That doesn't mean they aren't morally compelling in general, just not in a way that you prefer. And even then you could still fit some (not all, of course) Seers into those specific tropes.<br /> <br /> A decent chunk of the lower pyramid of the Seer power structure is composed of what is essentially a bunch of average joes. They do their 9 to 5 job so they can go home at night, relax, and spend their free time basking in the rewards they've earned by working at their 'job'. They aren't 'mustache twirling villains'. Sure, they know the 'company' they work for isn't morally the best, but they don't usually have to get their hands dirty themselves except for maybe the occasional sour job and they try their best to forget about those as quickly as they can (magic helps a lot with that kinda thing). <br /> <br /> Yes, they're part of the big bad 'company', but they personally aren't really bad, they just do what their job to get by. They're no more mustache twirling villains than people who work in for tobacco companies, or people working for big oil companies, or anything of the like. And their goals aren't all going to line up perfectly either. While Seers as an organization are pretty evil, and the people working for them usually know that, the people themselves aren't nearly as unrepentantly evil. When not doing their day job they can pretty much do whatever with the wealth and luxury that being a Seer provides. If they want to do good things (that they believe won't endanger the Lie) they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T15:15:24-07:00","id":975708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975609#post975609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course they do, they have an insider's view on the Diamond Orders. What I'm getting at is, even if you make the Seers the most sympathetic musguided idealists ever written, your players will never see that because there's still no &quot;screen time&quot; dedicated to showing them that. They're still just an out-group that the players are informed are the bad-guys, so if they're the sort of players to remorselessly kill &quot;bad-guys&quot;, they won't bother trying to learn the Seers' motivations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let me put a better bad guy example. The technocracy, i have WAY more players feel them as morally compelling than the seers. The same basics, a out-of-group ....group, with corrupt organization, with counter goals in general and no screen time except what the players can see. But the difference, their endgoals where benign in a way. <br /> <br /> The players could see their point and while they didnt like the methods they emphatize with the end goal or at least though the technocrat had his heart in the right place.....the times when said technocrat wasnt a moustache twirling villan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975609#post975609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So everyone who takes a job at a big corporation so they can pay the bills and feed their kids is seen as deserving to die? Damn, that's cold. I assume no one supports these corporations there, then. No one in your country works at or eats from McDonalds without becoming a social pariah?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Mcdonalds because here is expensive and it really doesnt harm our country the way of USA but when the banks decided to withold money from everyone in a necesary (long economics reason) measure and people range from vandalising the bank themselves to attack bank workers in their homes from vandalizing to actually enter and attack them. People who they work only in a branch of the bank and had no control about it the big descision and it was accepted as &quot;good&quot; or that they &quot;deserve it&quot; with very little people protesting about it t and he police itself barely did anything about those even. So yeah, cold.<br /> <br /> Hell 2 week ago a guy got robbed, them grab a car ran over the robber and then beat it to death with his bare hands. And there is a pretty divide on him doing the &quot;right&quot; thing because &quot;criminals arent people&quot; (The society idea, not making an statement myself just clarifying so it isnt an forum rule violation) to the point our president asked the police/judge to let him go. So like i said maybe it is cultural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975609#post975609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realism is compelling. It's not always more compelling than fiction, but like I said, the &quot;following orders&quot; villain trope isn't as played-out as the well-intentioned extremist or the misguided idealist. Peter Petegrew is absolutely an interesting character. He's not a <i>likable</i> character by any means, but you don't have to like a character to find them compelling. I pity Pettegrew, he's easily the most pathetic character in the series. And that pity makes me feel more for him than I do for, say, Bellatrix, who's just kind of in it for the murdering. You know who's another compelling character in Harry Potter who fits the Seer mentality? Lucius Malfoy. He's not a Death Eater because he likes being a bad guy, he's a Death Eater because he thinks it's the winning side. He sees more benefit for himself and his family in serving Voldemort than serving the Ministry. You know who else fits the Seer mentality? Severus everyone-excuses-the-fact-that-I-was-legit-Death-Eater-because-I-creeped-on-Lilly-and-switched-sides-when-Voldemort-killed-her Snape. From beginning to end, he served the side that he saw as benefiting him the most, it just happened that he valued his obsession with Lilly more than he valued the power Voldemort offered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont find any of those character morally compelling either, like i said i like the snake motiff, masks and tricks of the death eaters but never though the entire series on whether they should get kill off or not. Not even Draco, draco-in-leather-pants be dammed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-24-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T15:38:46-07:00","id":975715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975708#post975708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, let me put a better bad guy example. The technocracy, i have WAY more players feel them as morally compelling than the seers. The same basics, a out-of-group ....group, with corrupt organization, with counter goals in general and no screen time except what the players can see. But the difference, their endgoals where benign in a way.<br /> <br /> The players could see their point and while they didnt like the methods they emphatize with the end goal or at least though the technocrat had his heart in the right place.....the times when said technocrat wasnt a moustache twirling villan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not Mcdonalds because here is expensive and it really doesnt harm our country the way of USA but when the banks decided to withold money from everyone in a necesary (long economics reason) measure and people range from vandalising the bank themselves to attack bank workers in their homes from vandalizing to actually enter and attack them. People who they work only in a branch of the bank and had no control about it the big descision and it was accepted as &quot;good&quot; or that they &quot;deserve it&quot; with very little people protesting about it t and he police itself barely did anything about those even. So yeah, cold.<br /> <br /> Hell 2 week ago a guy got robbed, them grab a car ran over the robber and then beat it to death with his bare hands. And there is a pretty divide on him doing the &quot;right&quot; thing because &quot;criminals arent people&quot; (The society idea, not making an statement myself just clarifying so it isnt an forum rule violation) to the point our president asked the police/judge to let him go. So like i said maybe it is cultural.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I dont find any of those character morally compelling either, like i said i like the snake motiff, masks and tricks of the death eaters but never though the entire series on whether they should get kill off or not. Not even Draco, draco-in-leather-pants be dammed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, from what I'm starting to get from this is that it's a personal problem. You individually don't find the style of villainy that the Seers represent compelling. It isn't that they are objectively boring or unappealing, no, it's just that you personally dislike their themes, so they don't appeal to you. At this point the only thing I can really offer up is that if it bothers you that much then change it to better suit your preferences or deal with it. You like what you like, and dislike what you dislike. Nothing anyone says here is going to change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T16:00:07-07:00","id":975722,"title":"","content":"Maybe we should be reminded that this thread was never for convincing anyone of anything, but instead to help adjust the game to be more to the taste of people like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> and we've gotten really, really off-topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T16:00:19-07:00","id":975723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975715#post975715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, from what I'm starting to get from this is that it's a personal problem. You individually don't find the style of villainy that the Seers represent compelling. It isn't that they are objectively boring or unappealing, no, it's just that you personally dislike their themes, so they don't appeal to you. At this point the only thing I can really offer up is that if it bothers you that much then change it to better suit your preferences or deal with it. You like what you like, and dislike what you dislike. Nothing anyone says here is going to change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find them compelling, just not morally. But i see to much people arguing the &quot;just 9-5 job&quot; argument and not entirely correct. A seer, a mage seers is not like a secretary in a tobacco company, they dont just do a job than it by itself is harmless which only happens to be proffiting a bad company. I doubt the seers get a mage to do secretarial work.<br /> <br /> A close example is a employee who from time to time has to dump toxic waste in a residential not for proffit just because it make the bosses happy. When you have to stop said dumping and there is no justice system then killing them becomes a non-moral issue kinda (from player perspective).The seers work as villans in their little niche a death eater/kobolds, they shine in that.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> however is right we went far FAR off topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening#post971461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here are my goals/ideas so far:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Moral ambiguities of the main conflict are emphasized. The Seers have a genuinely good case for why they're right.<br /> \u2022 Some Mages have no Path. They are stereotyped as being more likely to become Scelesti or Banishers, but the truth of this assumption is questionable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Feedback and suggestions are welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to leave for work so this 2 are the quickest i can give ideas for. When i wanna run seers as morally complex is throwing the idea that the world is good as it is and that changing it by everyone awakening is bad idea. Thats the basic i can give for now.<br /> <br /> I dont see nothing wrong with pathless mage mechanically. They can choose they own arcanums and they dont have any default tools (maybe they cant have tools at all!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-24-2016, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T16:38:39-07:00","id":975734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=975723#post975723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find them compelling, just not morally. But i see to much people arguing the &quot;just 9-5 job&quot; argument and not entirely correct. A seer, a mage seers is not like a secretary in a tobacco company, they dont just do a job than it by itself is harmless which only happens to be proffiting a bad company. I doubt the seers get a mage to do secretarial work.<br /> <br /> A close example is a employee who from time to time has to dump toxic waste in a residential not for proffit just because it make the bosses happy. When you have to stop said dumping and there is no justice system then killing them becomes a non-moral issue kinda (from player perspective).The seers work as villans in their little niche a death eater/kobolds, they shine in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you're right, it isn't really like a 9 to 5 job. You aren't going to need to work nearly as much as a Seer as you would a 9 to 5, but chances are your assignments when you get them may as well be just as, if not more pointless than in regular job. The higher ups don't tell you why they want you to do what they ask you to do or what the consequences are, they just tell you to do it. Hell, a lot of time the guy directly above you doesn't even know, as he was delegated the task from the one above him and so on. So you get an order to do something that, chances are, you're going to delegate to those beneath you (Sleepers if you're at the very bottom of the pyramid) if you don't want to do it yourself.<br /> <br /> So say you get an order to have someone wrongfully evicted from their house. That's a bit of a dick move, and you don't know why it's important, though you don't really have the stomach to do it yourself, so what do you do? You pay a Sleeper to go bribe the landlord into doing it for you. Done. It was morally wrong, sure, but you didn't make the landlord take the money, you didn't force the Sleeper working under you to take the job to go bribe the landlord, and you aren't the one who originally issued the order. You feel kinda bad for the guy getting evicted but you've never met him, you don't know his situation, and you don't much care to. You had a job to do and you got it done cleanly. The end. That doesn't make you a baby eating monster, you're just a guy doing his job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-24-2016, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:19:25-07:00","id":978211,"title":"","content":"Again, I'm getting half of the people saying that what I want is a radical departure and the other half saying it's already there. <br /> <br /> As an aside, it's kind of dispiriting to hear that from Dave about the technocracy. Thankfully, M20 committed itself fully to making the central conflict as grey as most of the players seem to prefer. And I understand that the OP devs and mods have a bit of a chip against Genius, but I really don't think you can dismiss Kyle's remarkably insightful critiques and commentary that easily. I'm trying to be open minded, and I can see what people like about Awakening. And I know what it's like to be defensive over a personal creation. But I still think that the dismissively some have for Genius, is, well...a lot like my own initial dismissal of and vitriol towards Mage. The reason for my recent spurt of posts in the thread was because I tried to re-evaluate it, and really wanted to explore its possibilities (even though its lead developer once told me that I would die and no one would remember me). <br /> <br /> Also, Dave, I'm still up to talk any time.<br /> <br /> I'd like to wag my finger at everyone and say &quot;oh, why couldn't we jus have had a productive discussion about house rules?&quot; but I admit that if I wanted that I really should have approached it better. <br /> <br /> I am still up to talk about how to ramp up and emphasize the horror and monstrosity of Mage, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-01-2016, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:55:34-07:00","id":978235,"title":"","content":"Fine, you want houserules to completely change the setting, I'll give you one. All Mages bleed mana occasionally, once they're out of mana they start bleeding their life force. They can only gain mana by solving and discovering mysteries or by draining all motes of Supernal Truth from things around them, typically by destroying them, thus creating abyssal reflections of the thing they drained. <br /> <br /> There you go, they're now Mystery vampires that have to create abyssal entities to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:57:12-07:00","id":978236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978211#post978211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't think you can dismiss Kyle's remarkably insightful</div> </div> </div> </div>I had to point out a mechanical oversight <i>to Kyle</i> that occurred because he mindlessly ported something from Awakening without considering how it interacted with the systems he was applying it to instead of its original context.<br /> <br /> The one game of Genius I have managed to run specifically ran into problems stemming from the combination of randomly-applied Faults and the use of non-narrative units of time in mechanical effects with granularity disproportionate to what should have been sensible bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> Genius was my entry point to the nWoD and comprises a substantial portion of my early discussion on the subject, much of it devoted to pointing out how utterly nonsensical and broken many of its narrative and mechanical aspects are.<br /> <br /> I wasted three years of my life on that shit and I'm sick of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as ambiguity and horror go, the primary advice I can offer amounts to &quot;Get good at devising bluebook-type weird phenomena with multiple potential causes,&quot; &quot;Re-contextualize the characters' activity,&quot; and &quot;Remember that symbols are slippery.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T00:21:10-07:00","id":978251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978211#post978211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I'm getting half of the people saying that what I want is a radical departure and the other half saying it's already there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe this is because people aren't clear on what you actually want.<br /> <br /> Can Mage give you ambiguity and horror? Well, it's a game set in a horror cosmos whose mechanics support and encourage players to tell stories about characters slowly becoming inhuman. So yes. And there's been a whole lot of discussion about identifying those elements and how to foreground them.<br /> <br /> Is Mage sufficiently like some random dude's &quot;in <i>my</i> world, elves are called dwelves&quot; fansplat? Nah, probably not.<br /> <br /> Can Mage tell stories about dangerously flawed protagonists? Yes. We literally had a guy in the thread saying his players, if given the excuse, will go around killing their enemies - thinking, feeling human beings - &quot;like kobolds.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does Mage refuse to acknowledge that its antagonists, who perpetrate real human crimes like chattel slavery, are doing evil in the world because, <i>like, you know, *toke* who's to say, man?</i> No. It is a game that has graduated college.<br /> <br /> Is Mage the game for you? Probably not! I legitimately don't think it is! Especially if all you're going to be thinking about while reading or talking about it is an imaginary vendetta with the developer.<br /> <br /> Will another thread solve the problem? I don't know, maybe the 500th time is the charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T00:41:30-07:00","id":978258,"title":"","content":"I've never really understood the argument that Mage is somehow more superheroes with trenchcoats, either for Awakening or back in my Ascension days than other lines. A fundamental aspect of the Mage settings, to me, sets a rather terrifying table as is. While the nature of Mages and the opening up of the reality of the world(s) they inhabit certainly provides the Mage the tools, in potentia anyway, to deal with the avenues now open to them. It doesn't really change that these things are horrific. A predatory Shadow world of spirits and less definable things, literal inner demons, horrific entities some which by their very nature defy explanation or definition,Symbols of tyranny,etc. Awakening is not lacking for varying levels of horror in external threats.<br /> <br /> But that's not all the horror in Mage. Dealing with other people, some of whom have made themselves something more(less?) than human, and what they can do with magic is itself horrifying. To say nothing of having those capabilities yourself. Knowing you COULD rip into someone's mind and rewire essentially who they are, to say nothing of the million and one other things that is within the grasp of a Mage. That's going to be an ever present temptation for mages, it's sets a table for Wisdom and the tensions in Mage societies. Real world people deal all the time with thoughts of fancy about what they might do to someone with even just a tiny fraction of the capabilities Mages have available to them. And that's just talking your everday mostly decent people.<br /> <br /> I think to ignore or dismiss the horror inherent to Mage requires an ignorance or intentional oversight of the the very evils of the real world and the motivations behind some of the most horrific acts in human history. Human nature can be very terrifying. That, to a certain extent to me, sets a contrast against those creatures in the WoD where some of the horror is inherent to the nature of being(vampire,werewolf,etc) before you start diving into how urges and motivations and ideologies start to rear their ugly head in the other games. Human evil, in the sense of real world evil runs throughout all the lines and Mage is no exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-29-2016, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T01:21:47-07:00","id":978266,"title":"","content":"I think there's a fair parallel to be drawn between both Mage games (and any story about wizards) with superheroes, inasmuch as superhero stories are often about people with power struggling to use it responsibly, how having power divorces you from the people and things you care about, what it's like to be a being with a unique or inhuman perspective on the world and on morality, what the world owes you vs. what you owe the world, and so forth.<br /> <br /> But I sure don't think a lot of people making the comparison mean it that way. It sure feels like a very sneering 3edgy5me kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T02:13:20-07:00","id":978277,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> Once a participant in a conversation has reached the point where all they can do is repeat themselves that participant has ceased to be a productive part of the conversation. <br /> <br /> You're just kicking the conversation back to square one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T05:23:18-07:00","id":978321,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> That describes just about everyone in this thread since the first page, barring a few people who have made good-faith attempts to actually be productive.<br /> <br /> \u200bNothing about this thread has been productive, since people have been getting their jollies by voicing their problems with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> and what he wants rather than actually staying on topic and being contributing members of the community since moment one.<br /> <br /> Both counts include me, if we're honest. Since I'm mindlessly repeating myself in a vain attempt to keep things on topic rather than having anything meaningful to contribute.<br /> <br /> I just don't particularly like how everyone is using this thread to tell somebody that they're having fun the wrong way. If you don't like how he's trying to have fun, don't post in the thread. That way everyone is happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:00:07-07:00","id":978333,"title":"","content":"No one has said they're having wrong fun, and that's not the gist of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> post either. Instead they wrote about how others have more than one way to look at and play Mage and somehow that's a problem (When it's not being sidetracked by complaints about the devs). It's not addressing any of the actual help that has been brought. Even if the help has been a little repetitive its irrelevant because gecko's post is not actually engaging the conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:20:42-07:00","id":978338,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the conversation has been something like:<br /> -&quot;I need help highlighting this aspect of the game&quot;<br /> -&quot;The mechanics already do that, nothing needs to be changed&quot;<br /> Repeated ad nauseum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:28:06-07:00","id":978341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978211#post978211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Dave, I'm still up to talk any time. Over the course of this thread, I realized I was falling back into defensive asshole mode again. I know what that place is like, it's not a good place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gecko. An apology means nothing if you don't change your behavior. We've been dealing with this for months now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:37:38-07:00","id":978346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971945#post971945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...damn it, I was needlessly confrontational and combative again. Great.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now having read back in the thread: this wasn't edited. Your post here was not edited, so you didn't realize after the fact that you were being confrontational. Why post the comment at all?<br /> <br /> (More will likely come, as I'm now reading through the thread in its entirety.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:43:41-07:00","id":978347,"title":"","content":"Can't remember if I posted this before, but one way you can dial up some problematic implications of Mage is:<br /> <br /> All magic (Mage magic, at least) comes from the Abyss. Remember how in Seer/Diamond lore, how the Abyss was formed (or brought into relevance) by the Fall? Invert that. The Abyss wasn't created, the <i>Supernal</i> was. In the Time Before, there was only the World That Is, and the Abyss of all that Is Not. Atlantis/Lemuria/the Exarchs/etc. created the Supernal with the Watchtowers (known and unknown) which filter and &quot;stabilize&quot; the surrounding Abyssal chaos into their own Supernal Realms. This created safe* magic, at the cost of the Exarchs being able to use them to more directly impose their will over the world. The Exarchs don't want people to Awaken, because the more there are, the less stable the system becomes (see: Paradox). All spells are imposing Abyssal Unreality upon the Real World, with the only difference being some are sanctioned and rendered less chaotic.<br /> <br /> This is inspired by, and similar to, the Secrets of Shangri-la in the Mage Chronicler's Guide.<br /> <hr /><br /> Another idea is to play with Mage Sight and Gnosis. Make Mage Sight basically always on with Gnosis as it's Opacity. Effort can be spent to Focus on it (like currently with Active Mage Sight), but as Gnosis climbs, it intrudes more and more into a Mage's normal perceptions. At Gnosis 5, its overlapping a Mage's senses at 50%, making separating the two annoying, but hardly impossible. But at Gnosis 9-10? They might not even be able to perceive reality as anything other than collections of symbols. That would, I think, be alienating from humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:44:48-07:00","id":978349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973872#post973872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue the Seers are a more mature antagonist anyway. Or a more pessimistic one: people don't need to be manipulated by archmages like Tychoides to do evil. They just need to be given a good steak</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another part for the horror for me. And not because I didn't know before, but seeing it so present in mage reinforced my observations in real-life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:48:30-07:00","id":978350,"title":"","content":"On a different note, I'm seeing (and have seen) misgendering on this thread, but the person being misgendered hasn't corrected it, and I don't want to name them , in case it's purposeful. So all I'll say is, to anyone using gendered pronouns, if you are not absolutely certain what someone's pronouns are, don't assume &quot;he&quot;. Don't assume it's &quot;she&quot; either, but there are pronoun issues on this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:57:24-07:00","id":978356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978350#post978350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different note, I'm seeing (and have seen) misgendering on this thread, but the person being misgendered hasn't corrected it, and I don't want to name them , in case it's purposeful. So all I'll say is, to anyone using gendered pronouns, if you are not absolutely certain what someone's pronouns are, don't assume &amp;quot;he&amp;quot;. Don't assume it's &amp;quot;she&amp;quot; either, but there are pronoun issues on this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>So then why point it out if the person being &quot;misgendered&quot; doesn't see the need to do so? If it's such a big deal why not throw the preferred pronouns in their sig? What is this tumblr?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:58:40-07:00","id":978358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978356#post978356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So then why point it out if the person being &quot;misgendered&quot; doesn't see the need to do so? If it's such a big deal why not throw the preferred pronouns in their sig? What is this tumblr?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not engaging you, just adding you to the ignore list, as I will to the person below who claimed this is some sort of on-high attempt when I didn't even name the person doing the misgendering and kept my message respectful =). SOCIAL JUSTICE BARDS UNITE no but I'm bored by this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 09-29-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:04:29-07:00","id":978362,"title":"","content":"Comming back to the original question and ignoring, that there has been a history of planting these questions and ignoring the productive advice for it I would like to add the following:<br /> <br /> Gecko you should be more specific on what you actually want to change. Mostly if you want mechanical changes or philosophical changes.<br /> <br /> The mechanics of Mage:tA are in my opinion well suited for what you want. If you like, you can probably tweek them here and there, like you suggested for stronger paradox, but I think these are minor problems and should probably be discussed in separat thread.<br /> <br /> For the philosophical differences about if Mage is actually a horror game or not, I strongly suggest to read &quot;The Night Watch&quot; books from Sergei Lukyanenko. While also intresting in the depiction of magic and overlapping different worlds, I think the greatest contribution of the books is the constant struggle between having near ultimate power, but still beeing utterly unable to change the world for something good with it. Mages too are not almighty superheroes. They are constraint by morals and by politics and if you don't submit at least partially to those, you aren't free, you are most likely dead. Anyway, read the books, they are far better, than anything I could argue here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:06:34-07:00","id":978365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978211#post978211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I'm getting half of the people saying that what I want is a radical departure and the other half saying it's already there.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few reasons for that. One is that people aren't looking at this thread in a vacuum, they are taking it within the context of all the things you've said about Mage and how it would be better off as a standalone superhero game, divorced from the Chronicles of Darkness. Most of what you are actually asking for in this thread is either already delivered by Mage, or could be accomplished with some very simple house rules and setting tweaks, but people can't just ignore the context this thread exists in. The other reason is that you seem to be trying to get something Mage already delivers, by way of making significant changes to its setting and mechanics. Some people respond to that by focusing on the themes you claim to want to play up, saying, &quot;woah dude, slow down, you can achieve the feel you're looking for without having to hack the game to pieces&quot;, and others respond by focusing on your proposed changes, saying, &quot;if you don't think you can enjoy Mage without hacking it to pieces, you might want to just accept that Mage is not your kind of game.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978211#post978211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, it's kind of dispiriting to hear that from Dave about the technocracy. Thankfully, M20 committed itself fully to making the central conflict as grey as most of the players seem to prefer. And I understand that the OP devs and mods have a bit of a chip against Genius, but I really don't think you can dismiss Kyle's remarkably insightful critiques and commentary that easily. I'm trying to be open minded, and I can see what people like about Awakening. And I know what it's like to be defensive over a personal creation. But I still think that the dismissively some have for Genius, is, well...a lot like my own initial dismissal of and vitriol towards Mage. The reason for my recent spurt of posts in the thread was because I tried to re-evaluate it, and really wanted to explore its possibilities (even though its lead developer once told me that I would die and no one would remember me).</div> </div> </div> </div>People who don't like Genius &quot;dismiss&quot; it because they aren't interested in the game that it is. When people who aren't fans of Genius try to re-evaluate it like you're trying to re-evaluate Mage, you end up with Sean's diatribe. And what do you know, Genius fans told him that the changes he proposed would make the game not Genius, just like people are telling you that the changes you want to make to Mage would make it not Mage. It's ok for you to not like Mage. It's ok for others to not like Genius.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978211#post978211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Dave, I'm still up to talk any time. Over the course of this thread, I realized I was falling back into defensive asshole mode again. I know what that place is like, it's not a good place.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to stop this. It's incredibly condescending and does not come off as the least bit genuine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978211#post978211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to wag my finger at everyone and say &amp;quot;oh, why couldn't we jus have had a productive discussion about house rules?&amp;quot; but I admit that if I wanted that I really should have approached it better.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you acknowledge it doesn't mean anything if you don't change your behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978211#post978211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am still up to talk about how to ramp up and emphasize the horror and monstrosity of Mage, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are serious in wanting to do that, I would recommend trying to do so without insulting Mage as-written, comparing it to Genius, making a show of apologizing for previous comments, or attempting to have a Heart-to-heart with Dave. Because that's the only way you'll ever get a productive discussion about it, given the context the conversation will exist in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:11:18-07:00","id":978366,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3093_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3093\" data-vbnamecard=\"3093\">hm8453a</a> There was this funny rule of internet that everyone is male unless stated otherwise. It's not harmful for me to be misgendered, I just correct people who did this. I would also like to ask you to stop defending people(in this case also me) to put yourself in a superior position.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n1tFbZ5kaY8\" target=\"_blank\">Here </a>is a funny and relevant yt clip. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:12:25-07:00","id":978367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978362#post978362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are constraint by morals and by politics and if you don't submit at least partially to those, you aren't free, you are most likely dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I agree with this. I personally prioritize the introspective horror of mage in my games--&quot;what does it say about me that I so freely x, y, z,&quot; and so on. But I think my disconnect with Gecko's claims is that I see plenty in the book I could use for more extrospective and/or overt horror. I'm not saying the following is your issue, Gecko, but I think a lot of people (myself when I started out) think they have to use everything in the book. And I think most games, like DnD from what I remember, are designed so that you ought to, but CofD isn't like that. Obviously, in any game (including DnD), you can do whatever the fuck you want, but in CofD, you're encouraged to. If you don't think the Seers are scary, I agree with the posters saying to scrap them and create a new enemy or use Banishers.<br /> <br /> Fun fact, I don't think I've even told Dave this--I have never, ever run a Mage game where the Seers were the main villains. Usually, my main villains are other Pentacle mages with contrasting goals, and it's a game of sabotage with ultimate power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 09-29-2016, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:21:19-07:00","id":978374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978366#post978366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3093_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3093\" data-vbnamecard=\"3093\">hm8453a</a> There was this funny rule of internet that everyone is male unless stated otherwise. It's not harmful for me to be misgendered, I just correct people who did this. I would also like to ask you to stop defending people(in this case also me) to put yourself in a superior position.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n1tFbZ5kaY8\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a funny and relevant yt clip. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And people are surprised and offended when internet communities are accused of being hostile towards women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-29-2016, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:23:20-07:00","id":978376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978374#post978374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And people are surprised and offended when internet communities are accused of being hostile towards women.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't even read past the first five words, I just put him on the ignore list =).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"a