div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978376#post978376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't even read past the first five words, I just put him on the ignore list =).</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's misgendering now? Do they know I'm a guy? Maybe I'm not. I'm offended","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:29:08-07:00","id":978382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978367#post978367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally prioritize the introspective horror of mage in my games--&quot;what does it say about me that I so freely x, y, z,&quot; and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one, if not the most important theme for me, too. It's basically corruption through power. A Mage has to constantly struggle and question his motives, if he doesn't want to develope into a complete psychopath and if he is already at the level of &quot;killing that seer is no big deal&quot;, he lost already. And as it was suggested in this thread: if players don't want to ask themselfs these questions, they should probably not play Mage.<br /> Fun fact: Vampire is exactly not the game for me because of this. Sadly all Vampire players I know, always play it like &quot;I am the God of Darkness, rule over humanity and the masquerade is useless&quot;. So a kind of dark supervillan game, which I think it is absolutely not meant to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:36:15-07:00","id":978389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978380#post978380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who's misgendering now? Do they know I'm a guy? Maybe I'm not. I'm offended</div> </div> </div> </div>As some wise person said: &quot;There is always somebody trying to extinguish the trash can, while the house behind him is burning.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:40:09-07:00","id":978392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978389#post978389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As some wise person said: &quot;There is always somebody trying to extinguish the trash can, while the house behind him is burning.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I also love the conflation of harm and offense.<br /> <br /> I don't care if someone's offended. Literally at all. If you're offended, that's on you (not you as in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11939\" data-vbnamecard=\"11939\">HardcoreHannes</a>, you as in proverbial second person you). Perpetuating harm through speech is something else.<br /> <br /> But I'll just remind my students of that, have to go soon anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:44:12-07:00","id":978395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978382#post978382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun fact: Vampire is exactly not the game for me because of this. Sadly all Vampire players I know, always play it like &quot;I am the God of Darkness, rule over humanity and the masquerade is useless&quot;. So a kind of dark supervillan game, which I think it is absolutely not meant to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back to this, true story, I played a mind mage named Serra in a crossover game once, and one of our other players was a Daeva whose first characterization was &quot;I want to rape Serra&quot; because he wanted to be able to Dominate (with both a capital and a lowercase) a mind mage. A power thing.<br /> <br /> Nothing came of it, and that's the end of the story.<br /> <br /> But I love the game myself. I WISH for players who can actually play it with nuance. Then I'll run it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:55:07-07:00","id":978399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978380#post978380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who's misgendering now? Do they know I'm a guy? Maybe I'm not. I'm offended</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a personal problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who don't like Genius &quot;dismiss&quot; it because they aren't interested in the game that it is. When people who aren't fans of Genius try to re-evaluate it like you're trying to re-evaluate Mage, you end up with Sean's diatribe. And what do you know, Genius fans told him that the changes he proposed would make the game not Genius, just like people are telling you that the changes you want to make to Mage would make it not Mage. It's ok for you to not like Mage. It's ok for others to not like Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had some Genius fans actually really like the changes I suggested, so it's broader than that, but yes. In fact, that was part of the point.<br /> <br /> I've had a few people explain to me that I just don't get Genius, and while some of them have been just as dismissive of my reading so far as I have been of them, it's entirely possible I don't. And I'm cool with that-honestly, if the Genius review continues, it's because people have asked me to continue with it. I'm content with personally not liking Genius and having that be that. I don't need to get the game, and I don't need the game to tailor itself to me. It is enough that I don't like it and I can move on to things I do.<br /> <br /> I feel, as a pertinent relation, I should talk about how I did not like Requiem at one point in time(anyone here remember those rants?). I'll ponder it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-29-2016, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:00:15-07:00","id":978403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978395#post978395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Back to this, true story, I played a mind mage named Serra in a crossover game once, and one of our other players was a Daeva whose first characterization was &amp;quot;I want to rape Serra&amp;quot; because he wanted to be able to Dominate (with both a capital and a lowercase) a mind mage. A power thing.<br /> <br /> Nothing came of it, and that's the end of the story.<br /> <br /> But I love the game myself. I WISH for players who can actually play it with nuance. Then I'll run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if you're ever looking, I would love it if you'd keep me in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:07:46-07:00","id":978412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978403#post978403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, if you're ever looking, I would love it if you'd keep me in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much! I'm flattered you'd be interested in playing with me.<br /> <br /> (Side-note,we actually are looking for players for a Mage game right now, but I don't want to talk about it here, I feel like we're derailing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:09:15-07:00","id":978414,"title":"","content":"Not attempting to serve as a moderator, but could we please drop the personal discussions and get back on track, discussing possible hacks to emphasise (as in, above and beyond what's already in the setting/system) the ambiguity and horror in Mage?<br /> <br /> My personal suggestion, born of 20+ sessions where the highest Paradox dice pool was 6, before mitigation (also, it had a +4 bonus because they were targetting an Abyssal entity directly):<br /> <br /> Paradox is a new Advantage, consisting of a rating (0-to-10) and a pool (0-to-10), like Willpower is. Casting any spell within your safe Reach (read: that wouldn't risk a Paradox roll) adds a Paradox point. Casting a spell above your safe Reach adds all Paradox points as a bonus to the Paradox dicepool, and resets it (so if you have 6 Paradox points and risk a Paradox roll, the roll gets +6 and your points go back to 0). Your base Paradox dicepool is equal to your Paradox Dots (the rating) or the base pool derived from your Gnosis, whichever's highest, and whenever you get 10 Paradox Points, they go back to 0 and you gain another Paradox Dot. Also, once you have any Paradox Dots, all spells risk a Paradox pool equal to the Dots, even if they're within your safe Reach.<br /> The only way to get rid of Paradox Dots might be taking Resistant Aggravated damage, on a 1-per-1 basis, with a Paradox Condition that would persist for as long as the damage does.<br /> <br /> This makes it so that no matter how careful you are, sooner or later, something awful will happen. It's still manageable, if you can handle absorbing the Paradox within your own pattern, but that comes with its own problems.<br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:10:33-07:00","id":978415,"title":"","content":"You have successfully reinvented Mage: the Ascension's Paradox system, circa 1997.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:12:40-07:00","id":978416,"title":"","content":"Not that that's a *bad* thing. We had reasons for avoiding building paradox in Awakening, but if it works, go for it. Maybe try making the extra paradox for previous paradox rolls in a scene apply to everyone, not individuals. Might have a similar effect without fiddly tracking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:14:28-07:00","id":978419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978414#post978414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not attempting to serve as a moderator, but could we please drop the personal discussions and get back on track, discussing possible hacks to emphasise (as in, above and beyond what's already in the setting/system) the ambiguity and horror in Mage?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I said myself in the post above yours that we were derailing. Not sure what more you want.<br /> <br /> I wrote a post several paragraphs long that Gecko hasn't responded to yet trying to help her emphasize the horror she's looking for. Again, not sure what more you want. I can't make her respond, and I don't see a need to lecture about what I can summarize in several paragraphs. When it's responded to, I'll be able to contribute to the conversation again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:43:53-07:00","id":978433,"title":"","content":"I can't speak for others but for the sake of addressing a latter post or two. Posting that I do not understand the premise upon which the opening statement of the thread is based upon is not an indictment of that statement. It's simply a declaration, along side an explanation of why I feel that horror has never been an element, whether you mean internal or external horror, I've found lacking in Mage the Awakening. If anything I would want more input from the OP or anyone else with a similar position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:01:25-07:00","id":978659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978414#post978414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not attempting to serve as a moderator, but could we please drop the personal discussions and get back on track, discussing possible hacks to emphasise (as in, above and beyond what's already in the setting/system) the ambiguity and horror in Mage?<br /> <br /> My personal suggestion, born of 20+ sessions where the highest Paradox dice pool was 6, before mitigation (also, it had a +4 bonus because they were targetting an Abyssal entity directly):<br /> <br /> Paradox is a new Advantage, consisting of a rating (0-to-10) and a pool (0-to-10), like Willpower is. Casting any spell within your safe Reach (read: that wouldn't risk a Paradox roll) adds a Paradox point. Casting a spell above your safe Reach adds all Paradox points as a bonus to the Paradox dicepool, and resets it (so if you have 6 Paradox points and risk a Paradox roll, the roll gets +6 and your points go back to 0). Your base Paradox dicepool is equal to your Paradox Dots (the rating) or the base pool derived from your Gnosis, whichever's highest, and whenever you get 10 Paradox Points, they go back to 0 and you gain another Paradox Dot. Also, once you have any Paradox Dots, all spells risk a Paradox pool equal to the Dots, even if they're within your safe Reach.<br /> The only way to get rid of Paradox Dots might be taking Resistant Aggravated damage, on a 1-per-1 basis, with a Paradox Condition that would persist for as long as the damage does.<br /> <br /> This makes it so that no matter how careful you are, sooner or later, something awful will happen. It's still manageable, if you can handle absorbing the Paradox within your own pattern, but that comes with its own problems.<br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>To address Dave's &quot;fiddly&quot; (quite legitimate) critique, you might consider simplifying this into a couple or a few categories that you can represent with Conditions. A progressive set of Paradoxical flaws could work. <br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, let's say, by way of example, four levels: Normal, Running Hot, Burdened, Scourged<br /> You get the first by attempting but failing to contain a paradox sufficiently poorly. You might upgrade on any exceptional Paradox success.<br /> <br /> If each level imposes an increased penalty to safe Reach but with a bonus to spellcasting, it would make casting increasingly prone to slipping out of control. In fact, it could improve the probability of the casting, just with similar boosts to the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> Since Paradox now targets others in 2e, this also happens to help magnify the horror of mages, per the original topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T02:49:23-07:00","id":978935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978433#post978433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak for others but for the sake of addressing a latter post or two. Posting that I do not understand the premise upon which the opening statement of the thread is based upon is not an indictment of that statement. It's simply a declaration, along side an explanation of why I feel that horror has never been an element, whether you mean internal or external horror, I've found lacking in Mage the Awakening. If anything I would want more input from the OP or anyone else with a similar position.</div> </div> </div> </div>Posting my own perspective here: Unlike other splats, Mages have choices. A Mage has a choice on whether he'll blindly follow his Obsessions into the rabbit hole. A Mage can decide never to overreach. In fact, with the exception of the Long-Term Nimbus (which has no mechanics attached to it besides &quot;Your ST should make something up&quot;), a Mage can decide to live as a Sleeper.<br /> And again, personally? I think the occasional &quot;saint&quot; does wonder to highlight the depths some Mages fall to, so I like the system as-is. It works, it does what it's supposed to. It's just neat.<br /> But then, I get to the table. Now, I know my players, and they're enjoying the story I'm presenting them -- it's definitely a Mage story, but it isn't a horror story. Why? Because Mage is all carrot and no stick, and my players are allergic to carrots. Seriously, after 20 sessions, not once was a Paradox voluntarily released, actions that could cause Wisdom loss have been avoided like the plague (even after reminding them it's a good source of Arcane Beats), and so on. If it wasn't for the external horror I bring to the story (Lovecraftian entities and time travel, mostly), there would be no horror whatsoever.<br /> So I understand why Gecko made this thread. I believe that, for some tables, the system needs more teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T03:52:18-07:00","id":978942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978338#post978338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the conversation has been something like:<br /> -&quot;I need help highlighting this aspect of the game&quot;<br /> -&quot;The mechanics already do that, nothing needs to be changed&quot;<br /> Repeated ad nauseum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this, the issue is that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> doesnt explain why the game as written fails to highlight those aspects to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T04:18:32-07:00","id":978945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978935#post978935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actions that could cause Wisdom loss have been avoided like the plague (even after reminding them it's a good source of Arcane Beats), and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like you need to push your players more if that's what you want. If you're going to let them simply dodge making moral decisions, there's not much the system can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:46:31-07:00","id":978963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978935#post978935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Mage is all carrot and no stick, and my players are allergic to carrots. Seriously, after 20 sessions, not once was a Paradox voluntarily released, actions that could cause Wisdom loss have been avoided like the plague (even after reminding them it's a good source of Arcane Beats), and so on. If it wasn't for the external horror I bring to the story (Lovecraftian entities and time travel, mostly), there would be no horror whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. My players never extend their Reach above their limit, never follow their obsessions if it causes them trouble, ask for help when something seems too big for them, etc... I'm living the exact same problem as Justin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:50:31-07:00","id":978968,"title":"","content":"That sucks, I've got a player who hasn't cast a spell yet without risking at least a chance die of Paradox and is being a complete asshole to everyone who gets in the way of his Obsessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:09:07-07:00","id":978971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978935#post978935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then, I get to the table. Now, I know my players, and they're enjoying the story I'm presenting them -- it's definitely a Mage story, but it isn't a horror story. Why? Because Mage is all carrot and no stick, and my players are allergic to carrots. Seriously, after 20 sessions, not once was a Paradox voluntarily released, actions that could cause Wisdom loss have been avoided like the plague (even after reminding them it's a good source of Arcane Beats), and so on. If it wasn't for the external horror I bring to the story (Lovecraftian entities and time travel, mostly), there would be no horror whatsoever.<br /> So I understand why Gecko made this thread. I believe that, for some tables, the system needs more teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same in my older, once-1E-team, now playing on 2E rules. But hey, they are lead by Guardian Obrimos, ex-Gauardian Arrow Moros and ex-Gaurdian Mysterium Mastigos - they have more than enough reason to be safe with magic ( three other players are more like support ). Still, when I put against them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895970-\u200b-2e-mystery-yellow-sign-hallows-network-corruption-and-abyssal-astral-realm?p=963000#post963000\">King in Yellow</a> that have risen automatic Paradox Dicepool, it become <i>really</i> interesting as they fought tooth and claw with me to <i>not relase</i> Paradox, burning for all Mana they have and taking Resistant Bashing damages. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Tomorrow we will look over Free Council 'astronomical' Scelasti cabal, I'm really interested how they will react on that...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, my new-mages-at-Apprentice levels are starting to get Reaches after few sessions and dwell in to questionable Obsessions... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978963#post978963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. My players never extend their Reach above their limit, never follow their obsessions if it causes them trouble, ask for help when something seems too big for them, etc... I'm living the exact same problem as Justin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rise your game as ST - MAKE them to use those resources or worse will happen. 'You <i>need</i> those extra Mana to defeat this spirit creature attacking your sister ' 'This Abyssal creature will not stop until he kill it!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-30-2016, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:17:32-07:00","id":978973,"title":"","content":"The game assumes that the people playing the game are playing because they <i>want</i> to play to the themes of the game. If they don't, well maybe they aren't that interested in that aspect of the game so whatevs, as long as everyone is having fun. If you really want them to go along with it, I guess you could slap them full of penalties every time they decide not to, but I'm not sure how much the people you play with would enjoy that.<br /> <br /> I also have a player who essentially blows himself (and everyone around him) up with Paradox every session, and he seems to enjoy it quite a lot. His Guardian cabalmate tries his best to put as much of a leash on it as he can, but hes usually running around playing cleanup more than anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-30-2016, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:25:45-07:00","id":978975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978945#post978945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like you need to push your players more if that's what you want. If you're going to let them simply dodge making moral decisions, there's not much the system can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they're being pushed, alright. There have been consequences for their decision to stick to the Wise path. This leads to an interesting story in and of itself, but their rationale is solid: It wasn't their fault. Yes, they could have stopped bad things from happening, but they believe the consequences for interfering could have been *worse*.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:31:18-07:00","id":978979,"title":"","content":"Have the consequences for failure been so personal that the possibility of the alternative being 'worse' is acceptable to them because while it might be worse in the long run, at least they managed to protect [insert important person/thing].<br /> <br /> So it stops being, well people died, but the alternative could've been worse, to, I might have accidentally summoned an abyssal horror into the world, but at least I saved my family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:50:11-07:00","id":978985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978973#post978973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game assumes that the people playing the game are playing because they <i>want</i> to play to the themes of the game. If they don't, well maybe they aren't that interested in that aspect of the game so whatevs, as long as everyone is having fun. If you really want them to go along with it, I guess you could slap them full of penalties every time they decide not to, but I'm not sure how much the people you play with would enjoy that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean, but people have the same problem across the other lines, for instance people playing vampires who never want to lose starting Humanity and so forth. Sometimes things aren't incentivized enough, but sometimes it's just the players and the Storyteller might need an extra hand in incentivizing their players.<br /> <br /> For people who have had this problem, would something like only being able to raise Arcana and Gnosis through Arcane Exp help? And it seems like if the players can always ask for help, you could get past that by making things of imminent concern, or at least limit that option to characters who have Merits that let them ask for help, complete with drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also have a player who essentially blows himself (and everyone around him) up with Paradox every session, and he seems to enjoy it quite a lot. His Guardian cabalmate tries his best to put as much of a leash on it as he can, but hes usually running around playing cleanup more than anything. </div> </div> </div>Does anyone else have this? I'm starting up a game and I'm curious to see which way things go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:06:16-07:00","id":978994,"title":"","content":"I feel like someone that careless with their Paradoxes would get - at best - a stern warning from the local Epopt. At worst, the Interfector may drop by for tea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:14:56-07:00","id":978997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978935#post978935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Posting my own perspective here: Unlike other splats, Mages have choices. A Mage has a choice on whether he'll blindly follow his Obsessions into the rabbit hole. A Mage can decide never to overreach. In fact, with the exception of the Long-Term Nimbus (which has no mechanics attached to it besides &quot;Your ST should make something up&quot;), a Mage can decide to live as a Sleeper.<br /> And again, personally? I think the occasional &quot;saint&quot; does wonder to highlight the depths some Mages fall to, so I like the system as-is. It works, it does what it's supposed to. It's just neat.<br /> But then, I get to the table. Now, I know my players, and they're enjoying the story I'm presenting them -- it's definitely a Mage story, but it isn't a horror story. Why? Because Mage is all carrot and no stick, and my players are allergic to carrots. Seriously, after 20 sessions, not once was a Paradox voluntarily released, actions that could cause Wisdom loss have been avoided like the plague (even after reminding them it's a good source of Arcane Beats), and so on. If it wasn't for the external horror I bring to the story (Lovecraftian entities and time travel, mostly), there would be no horror whatsoever.<br /> So I understand why Gecko made this thread. I believe that, for some tables, the system needs more teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont see a problem with this. You said it yourself, your players are having fun, so why force things just to make mechanic that your players are clearly not interested in engagin relevant. The mechanics should serve the fun of the players no viceversa and sometimes the mechanics serve the fun of the players by getting out of the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:44:48-07:00","id":979012,"title":"","content":"Gecko, this is a review (of first edition, but nevertheless) by Matthew Dawkins where he admits that when he first read Mage, he didn't enjoy it because he didn't think it was horror. He explains how he moved from that, and maybe you'll relate, so I wanted to share it here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nk-yc8Bxrlk\" data-code=\"Nk-yc8Bxrlk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Nk-yc8Bxrlk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:04:18-07:00","id":979129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=978997#post978997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont see a problem with this. You said it yourself, your players are having fun, so why force things just to make mechanic that your players are clearly not interested in engagin relevant. The mechanics should serve the fun of the players no viceversa and sometimes the mechanics serve the fun of the players by getting out of the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not interacting with the mechanics because they don't need to (paraphrasing, btw). We're all having fun, yes, but it's not a <i>horror story</i>.<br /> <br /> Take Requiem. No matter what you do, sooner or later you're going to lose Humanity. Sooner or later, you're going to Frenzy. Neither of these are mechanics my players avoid, and are considered fun. Why doesn't Mage have something similar?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Mage <i>needs</i> these mechanics to be a horror game. I'm just saying some tables <i>could use</i> some new mechanics to emphasise those &quot;Oh gods, what have I done&quot; moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:14:23-07:00","id":979133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979129#post979129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not interacting with the mechanics because they don't need to (paraphrasing, btw).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they are. Avoiding it is still interacting with it. It still shapes their behaviour.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the horror is from what you choose to do. If your players are always fine with the choices you give them, that's not something the system can fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:37:00-07:00","id":979147,"title":"","content":"Mage is about the evils you choose to commit, not the ones forced onto you. If your players choose to play boy scouts, they've pretty much decided on the type of character they want to play. If they wanted to play someone conflicted or morally compromised they wouldn't actively avoid all attempts to bring that to the forefront like the plague.<br /> <br /> If you want them to face situations where they have to break moral codes and lose Wisdom, put them in situations where they <i>have</i> to make the hard choices. Lose-lose situations exist, as do situations where there's only a choice between two evils, and it's up to the player to decide which evil they consider the lesser of the two. Put them in a situation that forces them to go beyond safe boundaries or lose something they feel they absolutely must save above everything else, even if that something has to be their own lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:44:47-07:00","id":979152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979147#post979147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage is about the evils you choose to commit, not the ones forced onto you. If your players choose to play boy scouts, they've pretty much decided on the type of character they want to play. If they wanted to play someone conflicted or morally compromised they wouldn't actively avoid all attempts to bring that to the forefront like the plague.<br /> <br /> If you want them to face situations where they have to break moral codes and lose Wisdom, put them in situations where they <i>have</i> to make the hard choices. Lose-lose situations exist, as do situations where there's only a choice between two evils, and it's up to the player to decide which evil they consider the lesser of the two. Put them in a situation that forces them to go beyond safe boundaries or lose something they feel they absolutely must save above everything else, even if that something has to be their own lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here is the crux of this thread. At the end of the day it's about how responsible or not a mage wants to be with the power they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:54:54-07:00","id":979153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979129#post979129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not interacting with the mechanics because they don't need to (paraphrasing, btw). We're all having fun, yes, but it's not a <i>horror story</i>.<br /> <br /> Take Requiem. No matter what you do, sooner or later you're going to lose Humanity. Sooner or later, you're going to Frenzy. Neither of these are mechanics my players avoid, and are considered fun. Why doesn't Mage have something similar?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Mage <i>needs</i> these mechanics to be a horror game. I'm just saying some tables <i>could use</i> some new mechanics to emphasise those &quot;Oh gods, what have I done&quot; moments.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whys of the thing is another matter, yes.<br /> <br /> There is a separation between the mechanic of Frenzy and the mechanic of humanity. The oh god what have i done moments are difficult in mage as written because mage doesn't have a &quot;i take control of your PC moment&quot; like the others (vampire`s frenzy and Werewolf`s death rage) the one it has is the DM enforcing dickish twisting of your magic ala monkey paw or, the bleedout your love one suffer because of low wisdom.<br /> <br /> As humanity comparison to Wisdom comes from players accepting humanity more than wisdom. Wisdom has its problems which comes from being an objective morality so whether it works with the themes or not depends on whether you (as a player/DM) agree with the games interpretation of hubris or not. If you agree with it, them its all pink tinted shades like this little gem here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I absolutely disagree. I think the Wisdom system is 100% in-character and doing its job. In this case, the Wisdom system is making the players think again about what they're about to do and ask if it's really the right choice, even if for the wrong reasons. </div> </div> </div>Then everything work fine, nothing to change and anyone disagreeing obviously doesn't GET the game. *eye roll*<br /> <br /> However if you dont agree with the wisdom system then its feel arbitrary.<br /> <br /> Example i think by the description of wisdom, that being the responsible use of magic power, then mundane killing should either not be a sin (because its not magic) or be in higher grade than say &quot;change the timeline&quot;, &quot;read/modify minds&quot; or &quot;create life&quot;. Killing is always wrong says the objective morality of wod, i think killing is wrong depending on the context.<br /> <br /> Because morality or in this case wisdom is relative to each of us but the game gives us an objective definition of it when you dont agree with it, as player no PC, it cause 2 kinds of problems. Either you fight it, say instead of<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Wisdom system is making the players think again about what they're about to do and ask if it's really the right choice, even if for the wrong reasons. </div> </div> </div>They think &quot;how can i off this guy without getting screwed by the arbitrary morality system&quot; or on the other extreme is your situation, players just dont do the things that are a nono and use the system just like the alternative morality paths of vampire the masquerade, the famous &quot;path of what i was going to do anyway&quot;.<br /> All of that couple with the regression of wisdom to the carrot and the stick extremes. Having low wisdom, as far i could find, is ALWAYS bad so there is little temptation of power there. Even Werewolf got the good idea to add some advantages to having high end spectrum of morality (To those than dont play werewolf, forsaken morality is about reaching the perfect balance at 5 with 1 and 10 being the equivalent of wisdom 1 or integrity 1). So as player unless the DM force the situation, &quot;commit a wisdom sin or you gonna lose&quot; and gives you no way out them there is little player incentive to have low wisdom.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately im preparing a Forsaken campaign and dont have time to devote to this but an idea i had is using Resonance from Mage the ascension revised instead of Wisdom because to me it was the better morality system i seen in WoD.<br /> <br /> The basic idea was that depending on how you use your magic and what acts you committed you gain points in one of 3 resonances (Entropic, dynamic and static) and it would &quot;color&quot; your magic as you get more.<br /> <br /> Example, we had a verbena who kill all his enemies in messy brutal ways as the game continue he gained more entropic resonance (pain) which meant all his spell would cause searing pain, the player like that because it help his character to kill better until her try to heal someone with magic and realize that his healing also causer mind shattering pain.<br /> <br /> And thats the beauty of it, because is not an objectively &quot;bad thing&quot; but instead it was a show that action have consequence both good and bad. The game wasn't saying &quot;what you were doing is BAD&quot; but instead &quot;you got even better at what you were already doing at the expense of other things......so what does it say about you (pc) that your magic is tainted with pain?&quot; and thats what a morality system should do, not punishing you because of what it perceives at bad but showing you that choices opens some doors and close others.<br /> <br /> Honestly the system of resonance is interesting to explore in mage awakening as resonance was greatly expanded from the 3 categories of ascension and it fits better with the inverse paradigm of awakening as in ascension you start with a paradigm and supposedly, as you raise in power you discard it until you just blink and magic happens. While Awakening you start blinking and doing magic and as your raise in power you get more trappings of a paradigm (More yantras, a legacy, praxies) and getting a resonance that affects all your spells would fit nicely on that.<br /> <br /> My original idea was to make nimbus more mutable and instead of affecting the people near you, it would affect your magic. Thats my suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-30-2016, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:15:04-07:00","id":979163,"title":"","content":"Well, since we are on the subject, I really do hope we at some point get an official optional Wisdom track at some point in the future. I'd love to have Wisdom that actually measured how precise and prepared you were when casting magic (and when performing mundane acts at higher breakpoints since I want mundane acts to matter but still not hold the weight that magic does) rather than the weird halfway point we have now. I mean it probably won't happen because it's easy enough to houserule already, but it is something I'd love to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:27:57-07:00","id":979168,"title":"","content":"Could we please drop the &quot;you're just not getting it&quot; thing? It's needlessly condescending, at best. Instead, could everyone please assume everyone &quot;gets it&quot; and focus on ideas for hacks to pump the horror in Mage up to eleven?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979153#post979153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately im preparing a Forsaken campaign and dont have time to devote to this but an idea i had is using Resonance from Mage the ascension revised instead of Wisdom because to me it was the better morality system i seen in WoD.<br /> <br /> The basic idea was that depending on how you use your magic and what acts you committed you gain points in one of 3 resonances (Entropic, dynamic and static) and it would &quot;color&quot; your magic as you get more.<br /> <br /> Example, we had a verbena who kill all his enemies in messy brutal ways as the game continue he gained more entropic resonance (pain) which meant all his spell would cause searing pain, the player like that because it help his character to kill better until her try to heal someone with magic and realize that his healing also causer mind shattering pain.<br /> <br /> And thats the beauty of it, because is not an objectively &quot;bad thing&quot; but instead it was a show that action have consequence both good and bad. The game wasn't saying &quot;what you were doing is BAD&quot; but instead &quot;you got even better at what you were already doing at the expense of other things......so what does it say about you (pc) that your magic is tainted with pain?&quot; and thats what a morality system should do, not punishing you because of what it perceives at bad but showing you that choices opens some doors and close others.<br /> <br /> Honestly the system of resonance is interesting to explore in mage awakening as resonance was greatly expanded from the 3 categories of ascension and it fits better with the inverse paradigm of awakening as in ascension you start with a paradigm and supposedly, as you raise in power you discard it until you just blink and magic happens. While Awakening you start blinking and doing magic and as your raise in power you get more trappings of a paradigm (More yantras, a legacy, praxies) and getting a resonance that affects all your spells would fit nicely on that.<br /> <br /> My original idea was to make nimbus more mutable and instead of affecting the people near you, it would affect your magic. Thats my suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really interesting. I'd love to see a polished version of this, when you have the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:38:22-07:00","id":979173,"title":"","content":"It doesn't need to happen if you actually took the book up on its invitation to modify the AoH on the Wisdom scale however you want. It's annoying to see the complaint that Wisdom is objective morality or doesn't meet certain standards again and again when it's as divorced from morality and as customizable as you want. The book gave easily recognizable (By being holdovers from 1e) examples so you could gauge where you want your customized AoH to fall. Complaining after you were given an adequate tool in your box that the devs didn't also use it to build you a birdhouse is just plain lazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:56:43-07:00","id":979179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979173#post979173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't need to happen if you actually took the book up on its invitation to modify the AoH on the Wisdom scale however you want. It's annoying to see the complaint that Wisdom is objective morality or doesn't meet certain standards again and again when it's as divorced from morality and as customizable as you want. The book gave easily recognizable (By being holdovers from 1e) examples so you could gauge where you want your customized AoH to fall. Complaining after you were given an adequate tool in your box that the devs didn't also use it to build you a birdhouse is just plain lazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, then how about more on that subject, because it's a common enough complaint that apparently the section on Wisdom doesn't convey that very clearly, or give any example as to what extent it was meant to be taken. This comes up often enough and from enough different sources that it's obviously a bit of a problem. The flexibility of the Wisdom chart is mentioned like once in a single sentence, with no examples given of how it might be changed and for what reasons. The way it is written comes off as more like 'here, these are the rules. Like everything else in the game you can houserule it if you want.' Yes, I know it doesn't explicitly say that, but that's how it comes off to a lot of people. <br /> <br /> Yes, I know there's a limit to how much word count can be spent on things, but this is a really important sticking point that needed a lot more emphasis that it was given. I'll admit I forgot that the chart was supposed to be a guideline but that's because it's so utterly forgettable. It wasn't in the past, and the change, which is and should be pretty huge, is more of a briefly touched upon side note than anything. I cant remember if Signs was supposed to include anything about Wisdom or not, but I really hopes it does, because it really feels like something needs to expand on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:27:47-07:00","id":979197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979173#post979173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't need to happen if you actually took the book up on its invitation to modify the AoH on the Wisdom scale however you want. It's annoying to see the complaint that Wisdom is objective morality or doesn't meet certain standards again and again when it's as divorced from morality and as customizable as you want. The book gave easily recognizable (By being holdovers from 1e) examples so you could gauge where you want your customized AoH to fall. Complaining after you were given an adequate tool in your box that the devs didn't also use it to build you a birdhouse is just plain lazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are missing my point, im not saying that the sins of wisdom are wrong and other escale would be better. But the fact that having low wisdom is ALWAYS bad is my problem.<br /> <br /> Any scale of wisdom would run on the same problem I pointed out, as soon as the player or dm disagree with it. You obviously like the system and its scale so its not a problem to you and thus you fall on the first category of reader i said on my post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-30-2016, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:48:05-07:00","id":979212,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> There's also at least one other line about how what's Wise for one Mage might not be for another. Anyway, if the given AoH are just examples why would you need another list of counter-examples?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> Low Wisdom being bad isn't the part of your post I was addressing, but your statement that it has a fixed objective morality. Low Wisdom being bad, eh, I don't see a strong argument for it. There are advantages to low and downsides as well and the same goes for high. Nitpicking over the mechanics we do or don't like isn't what I'm doing here though, so you don't like it, that's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:10:12-07:00","id":979226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979212#post979212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> Low Wisdom being bad isn't the part of your post I was addressing, but your statement that it has a fixed objective morality. Low Wisdom being bad, eh, I don't see a strong argument for it. There are advantages to low and downsides as well and the same goes for high. Nitpicking over the mechanics we do or don't like isn't what I'm doing here though, so you don't like it, that's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are not adressing the point of my post, then you are just nickpicking a semantics. You just latching on any little element you can to just &quot;probe&quot; that the argument is wrong because 1 single element of it doesnt fit your definitions. Look obviously you think the game is perfect and cant be improve them why do you keep posting in a thread about someone trying to change the game, just to say &quot;everything works as intended&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979173#post979173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's annoying to see the complaint that Wisdom is objective morality or doesn't meet certain standards again and again when it's as divorced from morality and as customizable as you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is so annoying to you to read about people not liking certain mechanic then why dont you stop reading the thread all about not liking certain mechanic? Because obviously the customizable as you want lie* is not enough for some.<br /> <br /> *and yes, it is a lie because there are other example of the book of act that are morality sins no matter what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-30-2016, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:19:38-07:00","id":979232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979212#post979212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> There's also at least one other line about how what's Wise for one Mage might not be for another. Anyway, if the given AoH are just examples why would you need another list of counter-examples?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> Low Wisdom being bad isn't the part of your post I was addressing, but your statement that it has a fixed objective morality. Low Wisdom being bad, eh, I don't see a strong argument for it. There are advantages to low and downsides as well and the same goes for high. Nitpicking over the mechanics we do or don't like isn't what I'm doing here though, so you don't like it, that's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>To emphasize that the list isn't set in stone, and to show that certain things (lets take harming others with magic for example) aren't always acts of hubris. I feel it needs to do a better job demonstrating when and <i>why</i> something is an AoH and when and why it wouldn't be in another situation or for another person. Simply put, it needs a bit more clarity in how it is supposed to work in play, and examples are a great way of showing that. <br /> <br /> Yes, it can be changed, but what determines that change, how far can it be taken, and what sort of individual do we need to be talking about to necessitate such a change? Also, if Wisdom is explicitly supposed to be a measure of &quot;a mage\u2019s ability to judge the value of when, where, why, and how to use magic.&quot;, why can mundane actions be sins against Wisdom? Wisdom could benefit quite a bit from a more word count being devoted to it <i>somewhere</i>. Whether it be in Signs, another book later on, or a dev post officially going into greater detail on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:48:48-07:00","id":979243,"title":"","content":"I can agree that it would have been nice if they had been able to go into more detail on Wisdom, but I also think there's enough there to work with.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> I am allowed to address things in your posts that are not correct in the hope that you will then revise your position to one that's factually correct. This will lead to a stronger overall position for your arguments. You're also misunderstanding me, and placing words in my mouth. I never claimed the system was perfect (I've got a few bones to pick with how spell casting works). If you don't like it that's fine, but please dislike it for the actual faults it possesses instead of your made up ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:53:51-07:00","id":979247,"title":"","content":"What advantages are there to Low Wisdom? I'm working my way through things and all I know so far is that you have a weaker Nimbus. I suppose that could be an advantage if you use the Nimbus contamination rules. Maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:59:49-07:00","id":979252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979247#post979247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What advantages are there to Low Wisdom? I'm working my way through things and all I know so far is that you have a weaker Nimbus. I suppose that could be an advantage if you use the Nimbus contamination rules. Maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>The duration of Paradox Conditions gets shorter at lower Wisdom tiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:09:27-07:00","id":979256,"title":"","content":"To answer the question of why mundane actions can be Acts of Hubris when Wisdom is supposed to measure one's control over their magic is that Wisdom and Acts of Hubris are two different things. Acts of Hubris are what <i>cause</i> a Mage to lose her ability to control her magic, just as traumatic experiences are what cause humans to lose spiritual health and PTSD triggers are what cause Changelings to lose their ability to discern reality from Faerie. An argument could be made that Acts of Hubris are based on a moral code, and I would probably agree with it. Your mileage may vary on whether or not that is a problem for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:42:37-07:00","id":979270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979243#post979243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> I am allowed to address things in your posts that are not correct in the hope that you will then revise your position to one that's factually correct. This will lead to a stronger overall position for your arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>If i say that morality-like scales (be wisdom, in this case) are bad regardless of the scale of sin then how is relevant to point out that one can configure said scale however i want?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979243#post979243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're also misunderstanding me, and placing words in my mouth. I never claimed the system was perfect (I've got a few bones to pick with how spell casting works). If you don't like it that's fine, but please dislike it for the actual faults it possesses instead of your made up ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Action speak louder than words. The fact that everytime anyone post any kind of problem they have with the system and you defend it with basically nickpicking their argument on semantic alone or just waving your hand saying it doesnt bother you while contributing nothing make its clear that you are not interested in discussing, just spinning whatever nickpick you can find to fuel blind fanatism. Adding you to ignore list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-30-2016, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:45:37-07:00","id":979271,"title":"","content":"See, you're making the claim again that Wisdom is a morality scale, but because it's customizable you can remove any &quot;moral&quot; elements. So you can't actually make the claim that it's a morality scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:58:19-07:00","id":979275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979271#post979271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, you're making the claim again that Wisdom is a morality scale, but because it's customizable you can remove any &amp;quot;moral&amp;quot; elements. So you can't actually make the claim that it's a morality scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not <i>technically</i> Oberoni fallacy, but it's treading awfully close. The fact that the Wisdom rules give you permission to change the Acts of Hubris doesn't actually change the fact that the example Acts of Hubris are violations of a moral code. A moral code with distinct tints of blue and orange, but a moral code nonetheless. Wisdom itself is not inherently a morality scale because you're free to change the Acts of Hubris, but practically speaking that doesn't do anything to <i>help</i> people who take issue with the sample Acts of Hubris, as they still have to do exactly as much work to divorce AoH from morality as they would have to if the line saying they're just examples hadn't been there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:22:45-07:00","id":979287,"title":"","content":"Withdrawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Misread/posted. 09-30-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:29:44-07:00","id":979292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979275#post979275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not <i>technically</i> Oberoni fallacy, but it's treading awfully close. The fact that the Wisdom rules give you permission to change the Acts of Hubris doesn't actually change the fact that the example Acts of Hubris are violations of a moral code. A moral code with distinct tints of blue and orange, but a moral code nonetheless. Wisdom itself is not inherently a morality scale because you're free to change the Acts of Hubris, but practically speaking that doesn't do anything to <i>help</i> people who take issue with the sample Acts of Hubris, as they still have to do exactly as much work to divorce AoH from morality as they would have to if the line saying they're just examples hadn't been there.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, they have to do some work, but in my opinion it basically comes down to rewriting a bit of fluff more than needing to say the mechanic itself is no good. Fair assessment though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:56:46-07:00","id":979303,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with owning the idea that Wisdom is a morality scale of a sort (a behavior code, at the very least, and one rooted in a certain kind of ethical principle, even if it's largely about made-up magic things). Almost all of the NWoD/CoD games have as a central feature that they're about people in danger of losing their grip in one way or another (on ethics, on their ability to make rational judgments, on their perception of reality, etc). That's their thing. Demon and Beast tweak it a bit, but Cover, for instance, still ends up being a set of recommended and proscribed behaviors, it's just more individual than a general sense of ethics.<br /> <br /> And I'm fine with that. It's appropriate to the genre and it's a time-tested way to build story conflicts into the game mechanics.<br /> <br /> I guess I don't get where the prescriptive &quot;morality scales are bad!&quot; thing comes from - if nothing else, it seems pointlessly limiting - but, you know, whatever. I do think that if someone doesn't want to engage with the mechanic that specifically plugs in to that kind of story - not tweak it, but straight up go &quot;nope&quot; because it's automatically bad because of Reasons - then I don't really have a whole lot to offer for their complaint about where the horror is supposed to come from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:01:49-07:00","id":979305,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely sure the digression into Wisdom had anything to do with horror, but this thread has kind of just started meandering anyway since in the minds of most the matter seems to be fairly settled and the OP hasn't said one way or the other if any of it has been helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:12:12-07:00","id":979309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979256#post979256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To answer the question of why mundane actions can be Acts of Hubris when Wisdom is supposed to measure one's control over their magic is that Wisdom and Acts of Hubris are two different things. Acts of Hubris are what <i>cause</i> a Mage to lose her ability to control her magic, just as traumatic experiences are what cause humans to lose spiritual health and PTSD triggers are what cause Changelings to lose their ability to discern reality from Faerie. An argument could be made that Acts of Hubris are based on a moral code, and I would probably agree with it. Your mileage may vary on whether or not that is a problem for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>So AoH can lower Wisdom even if it has absolutely no barring on how Wise your actual ability to judge when to cast magic is? Then why even say that Wisdom is a measure of that if it isn't really true? Wisdom <i>isn't </i>a measure of your ability to judge proper magic use, because it is quite possible to be able to perfectly judge magic use, have every spell you've ever cast be objectively Wise (at least as objective as you can get), and still end up at Wisdom 0. The only thing it is clearly a measure of is how many AoH rolls you've failed. I can't even say how many times you've committed an AoH because it can swing pretty hard both ways with lucky/unlucky rolls. And AoH, as you've admitted, are arguably mostly based on a morality scale, which means Wisdom itself is mostly based on a morality scale, with little to do with a mages ability to judge when/how to wisely use magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-30-2016, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:34:07-07:00","id":979321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979309#post979309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So AoH can lower Wisdom even if it has absolutely no barring on how Wise your actual ability to judge when to cast magic is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Just like a Breaking Point can lower a human's Integrity even if it has absolutely no bearing on the character's spititual health and a Trigger can lower a Changeling's Clarity even if it has absolutely no bearing on the Changeling's Perceptive acuity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979309#post979309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why even say that Wisdom is a measure of that if it isn't really true?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is true, because having low Wisdom makes your magic harder to control. Just like Integrity is a measure of spiritual health because having low Integrity makes it harder to resist the spiritual harm done by witnessing magic, and Clarity is a measure of Perception because high clarity gives you bonuses to Perception rolls and low Clarity gives you penalties to Perception rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979309#post979309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wisdom <i>isn't </i>a measure of your ability to judge proper magic use, because it is quite possible to be able to perfectly judge magic use, have every spell you've ever cast be objectively Wise (at least as objective as you can get), and still end up at Wisdom 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct, it isn't a measure of your ability to judge proper magic use, it's a measure of how much control you have over your magic. Losing Wisdom means losing a degree of control over your magic, as reflected by the increased range of your long-term nimbus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979309#post979309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing it is clearly a measure of is how many AoH rolls you've failed. I can't even say how many times you've committed an AoH because it can swing pretty hard both ways with lucky/unlucky rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I say it doesn't measure adherence to the moral code that AoH are derived from. Violating that moral code is what causes you to lose control over your magic, and control over your magic is the thing Wisdom represents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979309#post979309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And AoH, as you've admitted, are arguably mostly based on a morality scale, which means Wisdom itself is mostly based on a morality scale, with little to do with a mages ability to judge when/how to wisely use magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>AoH are based on a morality scale, yes. Wisdom is not AoH. AoH can make you lose Wisdom, but they are not Wisdom <i>per se</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-30-2016, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:44:57-07:00","id":979326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979321#post979321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Just like a Breaking Point can lower a human's Integrity even if it has absolutely no bearing on the character's spititual health and a Trigger can lower a Changeling's Clarity even if it has absolutely no bearing on the Changeling's Perceptive acuity.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is true, because having low Wisdom makes your magic harder to control. Just like Integrity is a measure of spiritual health because having low Integrity makes it harder to resist the spiritual harm done by witnessing magic, and Clarity is a measure of Perception because high clarity gives you bonuses to Perception rolls and low Clarity gives you penalties to Perception rolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's correct, it isn't a measure of your ability to judge proper magic use, it's a measure of how much control you have over your magic. Losing Wisdom means losing a degree of control over your magic, as reflected by the increased range of your long-term nimbus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is why I say it doesn't measure adherence to the moral code that AoH are derived from. Violating that moral code is what causes you to lose control over your magic, and control over your magic is the thing Wisdom represents.<br /> <br /> <br /> AoH are based on a morality scale, yes. Wisdom is not AoH. AoH can make you lose Wisdom, but they are not Wisdom <i>per se</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book says: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wisdom is a mage\u2019s ability to judge the value of when, where, why, and how to use magic. </div> </div> </div>Yet that clearly isn't the case as your ability to judge the when, wheres, whys, and hows of using magic aren't dependent on Wisdom at all. I'd agree that Wisdom measures your ability to control magic insofar as having no Wisdom means you can't, but those are clearly two completely different things, both of which are said to be what Wisdom is while one clearly isn't by the mechanics of the Advantage itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-30-2016, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:52:16-07:00","id":979331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979326#post979326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says: <br /> <br /> Yet that clearly isn't the case as your ability to judge the when, wheres, whys, and hows of using magic aren't dependent on Wisdom at all. I'd agree that Wisdom measures your ability to control magic insofar as having no Wisdom means you can't, but those are clearly two completely different things, both of which are said to be what Wisdom is while one clearly isn't by the mechanics of the Advantage itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your point is that the sentence you quoted is not reflected in the mechanics, I agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T17:02:11-07:00","id":979335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979331#post979331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your point is that the sentence you quoted is not reflected in the mechanics, I agree with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we're in agreement. Wisdom says it is two things while it only really takes into account one of them when determining how it functions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T17:07:42-07:00","id":979337,"title":"","content":"Anyway, going back to an earlier discussion, one of the things I really like about Mage is that they're <i>tempted</i>, not cursed or damned. The fact that players can avoid Paradox and Wisdom loss with careful play is, to me, a feature rather than a bug. &quot;But horror!&quot; The thing is, I don't believe that predestined failure encompasses the totality of horror, and the game still takes place in a horror cosmos and cautious players are still actively engaging with the system by constantly having to be vigilant about Paradox and Acts of Hubris. The game is putting them in the position of constantly introspecting on their own desires and choices and the likely consequences - and I think that's the point.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though, I just feel like it's bad GM praxis to &quot;solve&quot; this &quot;problem&quot; by constantly engineering no-win situations where a cackling madman is like &quot;Hitler and Milli Vanilli are coming back and you can only stop one! CHOOSE WISELY, FOOLS AHAHAHHAHA!&quot; I think a GM/ST/referee/whateveryouwannacallit's job is to present a situation at least somewhat &quot;fairly&quot; - which is to say, without some kind of adversarial stance - and allow them to attempt to resolve it however they like, and if they manage to outthink you, tell them &quot;GG&quot; and move on. If their actions have an unhappy outcome that makes sense within the fiction, few people will complain (especially if you made it clear that it was a possibility), but everyone will notice the instant you start violating the narrative integrity of your own setting just to crank up the difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","user":"jacobkosh","date":". 09-30-2016, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T17:16:05-07:00","id":979341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979303#post979303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I don't get where the prescriptive &quot;morality scales are bad!&quot; thing comes from - if nothing else, it seems pointlessly limiting - but, you know, whatever. I do think that if someone doesn't want to engage with the mechanic that specifically plugs in to that kind of story - not tweak it, but straight up go &quot;nope&quot; because it's automatically bad because of Reasons - then I don't really have a whole lot to offer for their complaint about where the horror is supposed to come from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, i am gonna concede that maybe there is a tweak that make morality scale work. I have seen it fall flat on the first edition of forsaken, mage, changeling, hunter, blue book, mage 2e and Masquerade revised. However forsaken 2nd sounds good on paper and i will be testing next, week and i haven played, nor will be, demon so maybe it can work.<br /> <br /> And as i said is not that wisdom system fails completely, it works so long as everyone buys into its definitions. Thats why some people defend it to death and some others hate it or just leaves them cold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-30-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T18:04:10-07:00","id":979375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979335#post979335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then we're in agreement. Wisdom says it is two things while it only really takes into account one of them when determining how it functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't have phrased it that way, but yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T19:42:47-07:00","id":979434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979341#post979341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as i said is not that wisdom system fails completely, it works so long as everyone buys into its definitions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which you define, so problem solved there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:11:12-07:00","id":979580,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Wisdom is defined by the book. Just because you <i>can</i> change something with house rulings doesn't mean that the book itself doesn't already cover and define that thing. Just because the book gives you permission to change it (also known as Rule 0 in broader tabletop culture) doesn't mean there isn't a problem if you feel it <i>needs</i> changed (if it wasn't broken, it wouldn't need fixed; this is the essence of the Oberon Fallacy mentioned earlier).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979337#post979337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, going back to an earlier discussion, one of the things I really like about Mage is that they're <i>tempted</i>, not cursed or damned. The fact that players can avoid Paradox and Wisdom loss with careful play is, to me, a feature rather than a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having played Mage 2e a while, this is where Mage 2e falls really flat for me.<br /> <br /> There is no temptation.<br /> <br /> For Paradox in particular: If you decide to Release Paradox, a single success means your spell doesn't happen (at best) making it about equal to flat-out failing, or the spell gets twisted and does the opposite of what you want, or some other variant. That's even worse than just failing. If you're really lucky, your spell will happen as you wanted, but with horrible side-effects that cannot easily be remedied. Releasing at all can be an Act of Hubris, too, further adding to the extreme cost of Releasing.<br /> <br /> So Releasing Paradox isn't a temptation because the cost is far too high than anything you could possibly get out of doing it.<br /> <br /> Containing can be better or worse. There's been some debate over RAI/RAW for how it works.<br /> <br /> In either case, Resistant Bashing damage is only really a concern if you're in the middle of a hostile situation. Bashing heals too quickly to be a factor otherwise.<br /> <br /> The issue comes from the Paradox Conditions, which admittedly can also happen with Releasing.<br /> <br /> Either you can Scour the Condition away instantly, meaning the only cost to Containing is a single point of Lethal damage if you fail, or you have to wait for the Condition to lapse first. I've heard people justify both sides. Personally, given they each have &quot;scour it away&quot; as one of their Resolution options, I lean towards the first.<br /> <br /> In the first case, there's still no temptation. You could fail with ten Paradox successes and your only cost is 1 lethal damage. So long as you're failing to Contain Paradox less often than once every two days, there's really no reason not to.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, the second case is not a temptation for the same reason Releasing isn't. The price is too steep to ever justify. The average character is stuck with all their spells for the rest of the session causing further paradox or summoning Abyssal Entities, which is even worse than Releasing.<br /> <br /> Depending on how your ST runs things, Paradox is either a non-issue or too steep a gamble to ever partake in. Which I suspect is why people are saying their players either won't touch it with a 20' pole or they're going whole-hog with it.<br /> <br /> Either way, it isn't a temptation if it's either a non-option or a total non-consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:50:18-07:00","id":979592,"title":"","content":"I just run with Paradox not taking penalties to spellcasting. It's mages conscience to decide if he want to spread Abyss a bit further, instead of modifying his spells...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-01-2016, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:15:17-07:00","id":979618,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> I wasn't talking about changing Wisdom but the AoH of which the ones in the book are just examples not hard and fast rules. Please read more closely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:01:05-07:00","id":979739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=979580#post979580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on how your ST runs things, Paradox is either a non-issue or too steep a gamble to ever partake in. Which I suspect is why people are saying their players either won't touch it with a 20' pole or they're going whole-hog with it.<br /> <br /> Either way, it isn't a temptation if it's either a non-option or a total non-consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a big thing when it comes to Paradox. How your ST handles it is pretty paramount to how willing a player is going to be when it comes to releasing/containing it. Generally when I, or when a friend of mine who ST's for me, run it Paradox is quite often beneficial to the casting mage. At the very least it's made interesting. Sure, there's the occasional one that really comes back to bite you in the ass, but more often than not it isn't used as a 'your spell just fails' mechanic.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if the ST punishes his players with literally the worst possible thing he can think of every time they'll just stop risking it. If you don't tempt them into wanting to take chances they'll just play it safe forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:22:08-07:00","id":980004,"title":"","content":"I think I've been pretty clear about what I'm looking for, but I'd be happy to clarify anything. In particular, the main focus is making Mages feel inherently monstrous, because that's what I see as the core of the setting, especially minor templates. I don't like &quot;but they could do awful things so they're monsters&quot;, because that applies to any game where your character has superpowers. What differentiates ChroD from other settings for me is that it's about exploring horror archetypes. If I wanted to just be someone with superpowers, I'd play something else. <br /> <br /> I'll stop with the heart to heart attempts, but they're completely genuine. I'm not trying to manipulate anyone. I know that when I was in rage mode, attempts to reach out to me seemed disingenuous, so I won't keep trying. <br /> <br /> There's inevitably going to be a lot of Genius in this project, since I love it it dearly and think it has a lot of incredible ideas, and it pretty much captures what I'm going for. <br /> <br /> One of my favorite parts of Genius, for example, was the &quot;you were a scientist, but you can never do actual science again&quot;. It's one of the most effective personal horror scenarios I've seen in, well, anything. It's scary in a way that few other things are. The sense of having a beautiful vision but being unable to bring it into reality is something that I'd really like to bring in, that I think would be very effective in Mage, but I'm having a lot of trouble reconciling it with the whole &quot;now you're one of the special elite who knows the secret truths of reality, unlike those dumb sheeple&quot; thing. That's what mad scientists think they are, but the thing that makes them monstrous is that it isn't true. Again, that's something I've been very clear about wanting to emphasize. I'll try to be more diplomatic about Mage, but it's kind of hard to talk about it without insulting it in some way when I'm trying to fix what genuinely seem like problems to me. I love Geist, for example, but I don't object to the homebrew threads focused on &quot;fixing&quot; it, because I can totally recognize that there are things about it that you can definitely make a case for being problems. There's a difference between kinds of homebrew- this kind, and the Geist fixes, are about correcting perceived faults, which is different from those which are about adding content or making adjustments that aren't made to remedy problems. So, making a homebrew Legacy for Mage or a homebrew Key for Geist or a Dark Era can be done without implying that there are problems with the original, but something like this really can't. I understand that I've been a dick about this in the past, and I'm trying to do better, but there's not really a way to ask &quot;how do I make mages feel more monstrous&quot; without implying that the game as it is makes them insufficiently monstrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:48:42-07:00","id":980017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;but they could do awful things so they're monsters&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I read your whole post, three times but these words strike out to me most. I agree, like you, that merely having Powers (Capital 'P') means a being could or could not be villianous just like regular people and different levels of armament/authority in real life That phrase you use strikes out at me with a context different than I believe your tone meant it.<br /> <br /> What one significant line between which beings are monstrous and which are not, is the compunction/hesitation it feels towards acting monstrously. When I read &quot;but they could do awful things so they're monsters&quot; my mind put an astricks with the disclaimer: What it really should say is &quot;but they can do awful things because they lack the sane and reasonable compunction not to, so they are monsters&quot; and I was reminded of Legacy soul crafting and how that seeming does a psychic surgery on your very being, a type of spiritual lobtomy that makes you a sociopath concerning anything you crafted yourself to be capable of.<br /> <br /> In my house rules I emphasis <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801749#post801749\">this aspect of horror with this Hack</a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:01:10-07:00","id":980022,"title":"","content":"If you think Mage lacks the beautiful vision that can never be I'd like to point you to the apparent futility of fighting the Abyss, the Exarchs, the Lie, etc. Mages have cosmic principles keeping them from achieving their grandest ideals and it would not be hard to make the argument that the Orders have managed to delude themselves into thinking that they can achieve what the Sleepers can't despite the millenia of history saying otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:50:17-07:00","id":980040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I've been pretty clear about what I'm looking for, but I'd be happy to clarify anything. In particular, the main focus is making Mages feel inherently monstrous, because that's what I see as the core of the setting, especially minor templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like &amp;quot;but they could do awful things so they're monsters&amp;quot;, because that applies to any game where your character has superpowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less &quot;they could do awful things&quot; and more &quot;their entire existence is constant temptation to do awful things in pursuit of their irresistible Obsessions.&quot; But, if that doesn't do it for you, that's fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What differentiates ChroD from other settings for me is that it's about exploring horror archetypes. If I wanted to just be someone with superpowers, I'd play something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree, but you are welcome to that opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll stop with the heart to heart attempts, but they're completely genuine. I'm not trying to manipulate anyone. I know that when I was in rage mode, attempts to reach out to me seemed disingenuous, so I won't keep trying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's inevitably going to be a lot of Genius in this project, since I love it it dearly and think it has a lot of incredible ideas, and it pretty much captures what I'm going for. <br /> <br /> One of my favorite parts of Genius, for example, was the &amp;quot;you were a scientist, but you can never do actual science again&amp;quot;. It's one of the most effective personal horror scenarios I've seen in, well, anything. It's scary in a way that few other things are. The sense of having a beautiful vision but being unable to bring it into reality is something that I'd really like to bring in, that I think would be very effective in Mage,</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Have fun with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I'm having a lot of trouble reconciling it with the whole &amp;quot;now you're one of the special elite who knows the secret truths of reality, unlike those dumb sheeple&amp;quot; thing. That's what mad scientists think they are, but the thing that makes them monstrous is that it isn't true.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what mages think too, and it's not true of them either. I'm surprised if you feel that's such a big part of what makes Genius horrifying to you that you have such trouble finding horror in Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, that's something I've been very clear about wanting to emphasize. I'll try to be more diplomatic about Mage, but it's kind of hard to talk about it without insulting it in some way when I'm trying to fix what genuinely seem like problems to me. I love Geist, for example, but I don't object to the homebrew threads focused on &amp;quot;fixing&amp;quot; it, because I can totally recognize that there are things about it that you can definitely make a case for being problems. There's a difference between kinds of homebrew- this kind, and the Geist fixes, are about correcting perceived faults, which is different from those which are about adding content or making adjustments that aren't made to remedy problems. So, making a homebrew Legacy for Mage or a homebrew Key for Geist or a Dark Era can be done without implying that there are problems with the original, but something like this really can't. I understand that I've been a dick about this in the past, and I'm trying to do better, but there's not really a way to ask &amp;quot;how do I make mages feel more monstrous&amp;quot; without implying that the game as it is makes them insufficiently monstrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>The key to not being insulting to the game you are hacking is to focus on personal preference. When in doubt, use &quot;I statements.&quot; &quot;I have a problem with X&quot; instead of &quot;X is a problem with the game.&quot; &quot;I want to change X&quot; instead of &quot;X needs to be changed.&quot; Avoid suggesting that the game is broken. &quot;Hacking&quot; instead of &quot;Fixing&quot;. Mage isn't unplayable, you just don't like the way it plays. And that's ok. And changing it so you can play it in a way that you do like is ok. It only becomes not ok when you claim that what you like is objectively better than what other people like, or that other people are wrong for liking Mage as-written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:51:17-07:00","id":980041,"title":"","content":"See, that comes back to the answer that what I'm looking for is already present, and I acknowledge that. What I'm looking for is how to frame things so that it seems possible and even likely that the Orders are delusional and the &quot;Lie&quot; and the &quot;Abyss&quot; are safety mechanisms that keep reality from cracking open.<br /> <br /> I guess also I kind of feel that &quot;able to force delusions into reality&quot; is a better way to handle the archetype of the Mage in a horror setting than &quot;knows secret truths about the universe&quot;. But again, that is kind of personal preference. The whole idea of fighting against reality itself is what draws me to the mad scientist archetype, and the doomed and dangerous nature of doing it is what makes them compelling monsters to explore. <br /> <br /> You say that &quot;mages realize the secret truths the sheeple don't&quot; isn't true in the game. What's your evidence? Where does it say this or imply it? Sure, you're free to interpret mages as being delusional, but the game as written primarily supports the &quot;mages see secret truths about the nature of reality that normal people don't&quot; interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-01-2016, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:34:06-07:00","id":980067,"title":"","content":"As has been explained before that's because the books of any given line are written from a pro-X splat perspective. <br /> <br /> Also, since the game actually handles most of these things already it's incumbent on the ST to provide stories that develop, delve into, and exemplify any intended themes. The devs can't make a better ST out of anyone no matter how many books they write, it still takes practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:45:31-07:00","id":980075,"title":"","content":"Promethean, Mummy, Changeling, and presumably Deviant beg to differ. Even Vampire isn't shy about pointing out why it sucks to be a vampire. Each Clan write up even has a &quot;why we fear ourselves&quot; section. <br /> <br /> And are you implying that the devs expect a good ST to interpret that Mages are delusional and run their games accordingly despite a lack of support for that idea? I don't think that's what you're implying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:58:14-07:00","id":980083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980041#post980041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, that comes back to the answer that what I'm looking for is already present, and I acknowledge that. What I'm looking for is how to frame things so that it seems possible and even likely that the Orders are delusional and the &quot;Lie&quot; and the &quot;Abyss&quot; are safety mechanisms that keep reality from cracking open.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... that's a 100% plausible interpretation of the setting as-written. All it takes to make it the objective truth is the ST saying so. So, put that in your ST notes, and when designing your chronicle, be sure that the mysteries you present to your players indicte those truths when looked at with a critical eye.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980041#post980041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess also I kind of feel that &quot;able to force delusions into reality&quot; is a better way to handle the archetype of the Mage in a horror setting than &quot;knows secret truths about the universe&quot;. But again, that is kind of personal preference. The whole idea of fighting against reality itself is what draws me to the mad scientist archetype, and the doomed and dangerous nature of doing it is what makes them compelling monsters to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, &quot;Magic is Mages forcing their delusions onto reality&quot; is a completely plausible interpretation of Awakening's metaphysics. &quot;Knowing secret truths about the universe&quot; is a Mage's interpretation of their own powers. Nothing says their interpretation is actually right, and there are very good reasons to believe they're not. Fighting against reality itself is one of Mage's major themes (even if it's not one I would choose to focus on if I were to run it). It just seems like what you need is a setting doccument more than extensive hacks. Not to say you shouldn't hack the rules to emphasize those themes if you want to, just that those changes aren't strictly necessary in order to play to those themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980041#post980041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that &quot;mages realize the secret truths the sheeple don't&quot; isn't true in the game. What's your evidence? Where does it say this or imply it? Sure, you're free to interpret mages as being delusional, but the game as written primarily supports the &quot;mages see secret truths about the nature of reality that normal people don't&quot; interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game is written from a Mage's perspective, since Mages are the protagonists. They are, however, meant to be anti-aspirational protagonists, which we know from word-of-developer and from the fact that it's a Chronicles of Darkness game. For an example of Mages being delusional, look no further than the Atlantis myth. Mage society collectively buys into a story they know for a fact is at best only symbolically true, and at worst outright fiction. The truth is, no such place ever existed. The aspects of reality they call &quot;The Lie&quot; have always been part of reality. The supernal symbols they blame for the existence of those parts of reality have always been a part of the Supernal. The Abyss has always separated the phenomenal from the Supernal. Magic has always been intrinsically harmful to the human soul. Mages have a story that conveniently explains why these facts are only true of <i>this version of reality</i>, which overwrote a previous version of reality that just-so-happened to be an idyllic utopia by Mage standards until those <i>badwrong</i> Supernal symbols (which used to be mages, don't you know) snuck into the Supernal where they didn't belong and ruined everything so hard it applied retroactively. Now, that story <i>could</i> be true. The young earth creationist explaination for dinosaur fossils <i>could</i> be true too, if you're willing to swallow the pill that the universe operated under different rules back then (admittedly an easier pill to swallow when you know for a fact that the rules of the universe are malleable, but still...) But Occam's Razor would tend to suggest Mages are fooling themselves.<br /> <br /> Personally, I favor an interpretation that says the myth contains a grain of truth, but has been massively distorted to suit a narrative that casts mages in a better light. If you prefer an interpretation that says they're totally wrong, that's just as valid within the setting as-written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-02-2016, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:07:58-07:00","id":980090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980075#post980075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean, Mummy, Changeling, and presumably Deviant beg to differ. Even Vampire isn't shy about pointing out why it sucks to be a vampire. Each Clan write up even has a &quot;why we fear ourselves&quot; section.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Mage comes right out and says that the Atlantis myth is a lie Mages tell themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980075#post980075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And are you implying that the devs expect a good ST to interpret that Mages are delusional and run their games accordingly despite a lack of support for that idea? I don't think that's what you're implying.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no. The devs leave grand cosmological truths like that open to ST interpretation, as part of the toolbox. If you want to run your games according to the interpretation that mages are delusional, the book supports you in that. If you want to run your games according to the interpretation that Mages are the only ones enlightened enough to see the real truth about reality, the book supports you in that too. If you want to run different chronicles according to a totally different interpretation of your own devising, the book supports you in that. The default assumption is that it's a mystery, which due to the nature of Mages, the PCs are likely to seek to investigate. What answers they find is one of the places the horror can be revealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-02-2016, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:36:19-07:00","id":980106,"title":"","content":"That last post wasn't directed at you, BTW, it was directed at someone else, especially the thing about &quot;expecting STs to see through the setting&quot;. <br /> <br /> So, let's get back to tacks. I'm looking for advice on hacking the setting and running the game to support the &quot;delusional&quot; interpretation. What would be the best ways to do that narratively and mechanically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:41:20-07:00","id":980134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980075#post980075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean, Mummy, Changeling, and presumably Deviant beg to differ. Even Vampire isn't shy about pointing out why it sucks to be a vampire. Each Clan write up even has a &quot;why we fear ourselves&quot; section.<br /> <br /> And are you implying that the devs expect a good ST to interpret that Mages are delusional and run their games accordingly despite a lack of support for that idea? I don't think that's what you're implying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're correct, that's not what I'm implying. What I'm saying is that an ST who is trying to improve (I try not to make a distinction between a good and bad ST, I prefer to think that one -is- an ST on a continuum to greater facility as an ST at any given time) will be able to read through a text and arrive at an interpretation(s) of it that suit the needs of the story they want to craft. This can be facilitated by asking others who ST the same game how to achieve those ends. If we have a disagreement I don't expect you to change your opinion, but that doesn't mean I will stop stating mine when I think I have an answer.<br /> <br /> For instance, the delusional interpretation can be played up via Mage Sight, the text for that straight up calls it hallucinations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-02-2016, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T01:23:11-07:00","id":980154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980106#post980106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's get back to tacks. I'm looking for advice on hacking the setting and running the game to support the &quot;delusional&quot; interpretation. What would be the best ways to do that narratively and mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at what Mysteries <i>are</i> \u2014 most of them revolve around specific experiments and peculiarities rather than profound little-t truths about the way the world works and the reward for pursuing them is an experiential understanding that feeds into the wordless knowledge of how to twist the world to your bidding.<br /> <br /> Even conventional Awakened metaphysics only posits that the Supernal is the way the world <i>should</i> work without the interference of the Abyss, because the secret laws that mages learn are so esoteric and removed from phenomenal reality as experienced by humanity at large that there is functionally no difference between their being The Way The World Really Works and their instead being Stuff We've Put In The Hallucinogenic Magic Pile That The Hallucinogenic Magic Pile Yielded Forth Due To All The Stuff We Put In The Hallucinogenic Magic Pile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T05:04:56-07:00","id":980193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980106#post980106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That last post wasn't directed at you, BTW, it was directed at someone else, especially the thing about &quot;expecting STs to see through the setting&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, let's get back to tacks. I'm looking for advice on hacking the setting and running the game to support the &quot;delusional&quot; interpretation. What would be the best ways to do that narratively and mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said it before and I'll say it again, incase my advice to you became lost.<br /> Play up wisdom breaking points, play up the Abyss, Play up the moments when reality groans because these guys are putting so much stress upon it that it is about to give in, and let them start the game hunting down a mage who went Wisdom 0, who walks down the street and magic pours out of him his dillusions are ripping apart reality randomly. Flowers bloom, cat howl, fires start at random lights get brighter darkness gets stronger things are randomly platonically formed even people who are performing their jobs. So a salesman suddenly becomes a perfected salesman, a cellphone becomes a perfected cellphone. Lashes of all the arcana randomly rip at reality tearing away at everything everyone holds their sanity down with. And you have to up and murder this guy. Then when your done, all the sleeper witnesses, and destroy any traces he left in his path. It all has to be covered up for the safety of the Sheep.<br /> <br /> Then let them feel good about loosing wisdom. Give them an Arcane Experience or let them have a free dot of an arcanum that isn't their inferior if its their first time loosing that dot. Let them feel that gaining power comes faster and easier the more they let go of what's holding them back.<br /> <br /> Play up Paradox and give them every reason to reach. Give them things that are able to resist magic So they need to reach, reach, reach, reach, and make sure that the +1 paradox for casting a spell infront of sleepers is cumulative. Paradox is Mages Perils of the Warp. When you unleash it have it mean something. If you have a copy of Death Watch, Only War, or Dark Heresy you can borrow do so, that will give you a great bunch of Ideas for Abyssal effects. Let them feel fear as they see what they have wrought. Also I think I pointed out giving an extra boost to the Sacrament Yantra when you offer up a living sleeper (willing or otherwise doesn't matter) to encourage that sort of thing is always helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T11:38:28-07:00","id":980358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my favorite parts of Genius, for example, was the &quot;you were a scientist, but you can never do actual science again&quot;. It's one of the most effective personal horror scenarios I've seen in, well, anything. It's scary in a way that few other things are. The sense of having a beautiful vision but being unable to bring it into reality is something that I'd really like to bring in, that I think would be very effective in Mage, but I'm having a lot of trouble reconciling it with the whole &quot;now you're one of the special elite who knows the secret truths of reality, unlike those dumb sheeple&quot; thing. That's what mad scientists think they are, but the thing that makes them monstrous is that it isn't true. Again, that's something I've been very clear about wanting to emphasize. I'll try to be more diplomatic about Mage, but it's kind of hard to talk about it without insulting it in some way when I'm trying to fix what genuinely seem like problems to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the sleeping curse, there's your nimbus clinging to everything you hold dear, there's the fact that for every miracle that you're capable of, such as curing cancer instantly and painlessly, you simply can't go around playing lay-on-hands-Jesus-Christ.<br /> <br /> To take each in context: You simply can't relate to the sleeping masses, who unbeknown to them are pawns to a multitude of horrifying schemes, from vampiric overlords brainwashing people without their knowledge, to spirits urging violence and death to gorge on the aftermath, to an artificial God using them as cogs in it's endless experiments. You've seen all of that, can you take action? How do you do that without extremely traumatizing those around you? Who do you confide in?<br /> <br /> Your loved ones, your coworkers, your job, your previous life before you awakened should be put aside, not because chasing the mysteries is inherently enticing enough, but because there's little recourse to do that before your nimbus draws attention to them, by very much the same things you're now able to see.<br /> <br /> The spirits which you can clearly see and distinguish now prefer to urge your kids, not because they can sense your nimbus, but because whatever essence they derive from it simply <i>tastes better.</i><br /> <br /> The close encounter with your possible demise, the thing that triggered your involuntary denial of a fixed, fallen reality and made your fate all but apparent to you, to it's gruesome yet delayed end now finds a way to entangle those whom you care about. Can you afford to watch how they suffer accidents after accident like a parody of Final Destination movies? What does it takes to change anyone's fate?<br /> <br /> And when you can change your or anyone's else fate, should you? Can you foresee what your changes will bring? Destiny doesn't takes lightly to those who try to bull-fight it for long.<br /> <br /> Again, your issue isn't a lack of avenues for mage to be horrific, but a lack of imagination for using those themes in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 10-02-2016, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:30:24-07:00","id":980526,"title":"","content":"Off the top of anyone's heads, what would be the major things that would need to be changed to update the Gifted Scientists from the MCG to 2e rules?<br /> <br /> Here are some other goals:<br /> - Establish a clear link between power and monstrosity. Gaining Gnosis inevitably distances you from humanity and has lots of nasty effects.<br /> - Use this to balance Mages. Mages should be able to choose between being human and being powerful. They shouldn't be able to get both. <br /> - A better system of limits and sacrifices. Every Mage should have personal limits on their powers, and doing major effects should require sacrifice of some sort. Unknown Armies is a great example. <br /> - Actually, &quot;how can I make Mage more like Unknown Armies&quot; is pretty much a good question in itself. <br /> <br /> An idea that would cover a lot of those would be to give Mages Bans and Banes when they gain Gnosis or lose Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T20:39:42-07:00","id":980553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980526#post980526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off the top of anyone's heads, what would be the major things that would need to be changed to update the Gifted Scientists from the MCG to 2e rules?<br /> <br /> Here are some other goals:<br /> - Establish a clear link between power and monstrosity. Gaining Gnosis inevitably distances you from humanity and has lots of nasty effects.<br /> - Use this to balance Mages. Mages should be able to choose between being human and being powerful. They shouldn't be able to get both.<br /> - A better system of limits and sacrifices. Every Mage should have personal limits on their powers, and doing major effects should require sacrifice of some sort. Unknown Armies is a great example.<br /> - Actually, &quot;how can I make Mage more like Unknown Armies&quot; is pretty much a good question in itself.<br /> <br /> An idea that would cover a lot of those would be to give Mages Bans and Banes when they gain Gnosis or lose Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been toying with stuff way more than I ought to as my own Mage game winds down, but it's kinda voluminous, so I'll share an easy-to-adapt tidbit regarding your first request:<br /> <br /> So, my players found it a bit tricky to keep track of Virtue/Vice <i>and</i> Aspirations <i>and</i> Obsessions. As a way of emphasizing the way mages lose their connection to their humanity as they raise their Gnosis, every normal person in my game has five Motives - one Virtue, one Vice, one Long-Term Aspiration, and two Short-Term Aspirations. Each Obsession a mage has replaces one of those five slots - chosen at the time Gnosis increases. At Gnosis 1 most mages are just going to ditch one of those Short-Term Aspirations, but what do you do when you get your second Obsession at Gnosis 3? Or your third at Gnosis 6. By Gnosis 9, you'll have four Obsessions crowding out all but one of your remaining Motives. Do you retain the capability to feel good about living up to your high ideals (Virtue)? Do you cling to your guilty pleasures (Vice)? Do you continue to pursue major life goals (Long-Term Aspiration)? Or do you hang onto your ability to derive satisfaction from small accomplishments (Short-Term Aspiration)? And what of those mages who convince themselves at Gnosis 1 that they would rather cut out the &quot;sinful&quot; part of themselves (Vice)?<br /> <br /> In consequence, as a mage's Gnosis increases, she becomes more and more a creature of her Obsessions.<br /> <br /> Raising Gnosis makes it harder to advance mundane traits Even if you're not playing for Beats, there is always that moment every other Gnosis bump where the player needs to think about what part of his character's human motivations to cut out forever - which serves as a reminder to the <i>player</i> that his character is losing something even as she gains more occult power. It's a subtle loss of humanity compared to Bans and Banes, but it has the advantage of being easy to implement. As an added bonus, it reduces the mechanical complexity of tracking Obsessions on top of the five mundane Motives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 10-02-2016, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:05:04-07:00","id":980619,"title":"","content":"That's pretty damn cool, and if there's more to your hacks I'd love to here it. Voluminous is good, I'm loving it so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:08:55-07:00","id":980620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980553#post980553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an awesome hack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:14:49-07:00","id":980648,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a>, I just use for my Gifted to work as Mage Template with my <i>Instrumentalist</i> Condition - it works really good. If you want to diverse more Gifted from Mages, just make them Pathless, add specific Instruments ( Yantras ) and let them be easier to pass their Wonders/Inventions under Dissonance. All that you need, really. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Instrumentalist </b><b>( Persistent, Awakened only )</b><br /> You character, even if technically mage, does not see that her miracles are coming from her. Whatever if she is die hard scientists, seeing her magic as advanced technology, or dedicated priest, believing they are granted by her patrons \u2013 she cannot 'cast' any spell without utilizing appropriate Yantras. She cannot force herself to acknowledge that Supernal power comes from her and by this, is slave to tools and ceremonies. When character tries to cast without at least one Yantra in accordance with its worldview, spell is automatic Dramatic Failure \u2013 resolve it\u2019s effects on character and environment in accordance.<br /> It\u2019s very popular affliction in Nameless mages or some parts of Free Council. What\u2019s even more disturbing, large parts of Banishers are under it.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Specific background. Wisdom loss.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Confrontation with reality of being mage. Dramatic Failure on spellcasting roll ( choose player and ST combined )<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> Character gives a 'tribute' for higher force or analyze the 'scientific basis' of his miracles (Arcane). Character undermines the Truth about the origins of magic in other sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:01:05-07:00","id":980716,"title":"","content":"Another slightly more complicated one that might not quite match the math of the final game (I started my chronicle by adapting an early version of the rules because we were so eager to playtest it): The choice isn't to contain or release Paradox. Rather, a mage can either Contain or <i>Control</i> it.<br /> <br /> Containing deals one <i>lethal</i> damage for each Paradox die. Each success on the Wisdom roll downgrades one level of lethal to bashing or reduces bashing damage by one. This makes it much more difficult to contain more than a couple Paradox. (worth noting that we stripped out the increase to Paradox due to higher Gnosis, so like I said, the math might not work here).<br /> <br /> Controlling means pitting your spellcasting successes against the successes on the Paradox roll. If you score <i>more</i> successes than the Paradox dice, the spell works perfectly, as you have successfully maintained control over it. A large number of Paradox successes (5+) can still cause Anomalies and even Manifestations, but your spell is fine. If you score successes <i>equal</i> to the Paradox successes, the spell still happens as you envisioned, but it is considered relinquished unsafely (what mages in my world call a Lesser Havoc). If the Paradox successes exceed your spellcasting roll, usually nothing happens (spell factors get dropped to 0), but sometimes you end up with a Major Havoc - basically the &quot;spell gets warped by the Abyss&quot; effect we see in the Core.<br /> <br /> (Again, I'm not confident on the math, as our houseruled version doesn't increase Paradox based on Gnosis, the Paradox roll for Control is two dice per Reach beyond the mage's safe Grasp, and our spellcasting pools tend to be larger because spell factors don't reduce the spellcasting dice pool.)<br /> <br /> Also, Anomalies come in two flavors - Personal and Environmental. Environmental Anomalies are what you see in the Core. Personal Anomalies seek out a nearby &quot;innocent bystander&quot; (a Sleeper witness, if available, or a Sleepwalker or other minor template if there are no Sleeper witnesses). That victim suffers in some way related to the Arcanum of the spell - turned to stone, given a Destiny that turns her into a serial killer, etc. In the case of big Anomalies, the transformation is permanent or fatal - or else affects multiple victims.<br /> <br /> (We ditched Sleepers worsening Paradox - which I don't recommend unless you want to rewrite the setting, which relies pretty heavily on Quiescence being a thing - and this hack makes it so it's still a bad idea to cast magic in the presence of Sleeper witnesses in our game, but it's much more of a moral hazard, as killing an innocent person with a Personal Anomaly is a severe Wisdom sin).<br /> <br /> Our goal was to make it so that Containing a Paradox was safe for the environment but probably guaranteed to suck for you, while Controlling a Paradox was probably perfectly safe (&quot;my spellcasting pool is much bigger than the Paradox pool&quot;) but the sheer number of times a mage makes spellcasting rolls means that statistically improbable events will eventually happen. The idea is to encourage the <i>player</i> to participate in the hubris of his character - run the calculations and decide whether he's willing to risk a Greater Havoc. Granted, we added a <i>lot</i> of new Reach effects to the spell list, so the other side of it is to make it totally worth an extra Reach or two to do something awesome that you should not be doing at your dot rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 10-03-2016, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:00:53-07:00","id":980922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980716#post980716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reach beyond the mage's safe Grasp</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god... Why didn't Mage use &quot;Grasp&quot; instead of &quot;free Reach&quot; to refer to the number of times you can Reach without adding Paradox dice... That makes <i>so much sense</i> I'm retrospectively shocked no one thought of or suggested it during development (or if someone did, that they didn't go with the suggestion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:17:29-07:00","id":981089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980922#post980922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god... Why didn't Mage use &quot;Grasp&quot; instead of &quot;free Reach&quot; to refer to the number of times you can Reach without adding Paradox dice... That makes <i>so much sense</i> I'm retrospectively shocked no one thought of or suggested it during development (or if someone did, that they didn't go with the suggestion).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember exactly when one of my players coined the term Grasp, but it didn't make it into the file my playtest group sent to Dave. But I agree that it's a useful shorthand for the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T16:45:36-07:00","id":981102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980041#post980041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess also I kind of feel that &quot;able to force delusions into reality&quot; is a better way to handle the archetype of the Mage in a horror setting than &quot;knows secret truths about the universe&quot;. But again, that is kind of personal preference. The whole idea of fighting against reality itself is what draws me to the mad scientist archetype, and the doomed and dangerous nature of doing it is what makes them compelling monsters to explore.<br /> <br /> You say that &quot;mages realize the secret truths the sheeple don't&quot; isn't true in the game. What's your evidence? Where does it say this or imply it? Sure, you're free to interpret mages as being delusional, but the game as written primarily supports the &quot;mages see secret truths about the nature of reality that normal people don't&quot; interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>My best friend and I debate this idea all the time. We take turns championing &quot;Mages <i>ARE</i> just another type of Intrusion (like all the supernatural beings), and the Supernal is just a section of the Abyss.&quot;<br /> <br /> The idea that supernatural powers work by something &quot;beyond nature&quot; and the world would have been a sane, safe, and consistent place save the intervention of what could be classified as alien forces redefining it (Tell me the Uratha Sundering and Mage Atlantis allegories isn't a tale of an Abyssal Intrusion going apocalyptic in the scope of world reshaping.) Especially given what is written in Genius implying about Intrusions being a source of that template, and the Abyss is about infinite possibility and nothingness yearning to be expressed and/or destroy all that is expressed. Everything about the Abyss is True, and everything about the Abyss is a Lie.<br /> <br /> Scary thought, this mishmash of crazy is supported by the many worlds interpretation of string theory and understanding the <a href=\"https://youtu.be/JkxieS-6WuA\" target=\"_blank\">tenth</a> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/ySBaYMESb8o\" target=\"_blank\">dimension</a>. Every possibility exists even universes with laws antithetical to our own and (if leakage between universes <i>is</i> possible, it may or may not be) different sets of universes leaking into each other. The world where Chronicles of Darkness seems to be an example of this type of leakage.That leaves the question, what kind of universe is the one we are actually in, and if universe leakage through is possible is our universe one of the ones subject to that? -cough<a href=\"https://www.ted.com/talks/brian_greene_why_is_our_universe_fine_tuned_for_life?language=en\" target=\"_blank\">-Ia! Ia! Cthulhu Fhtagn!</a>-cough- The Abyss would be an infinite set of radically intermingled universes leaking into others near its edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-04-2016, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T04:55:32-07:00","id":981387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973285#post973285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A. &quot;Mad scientist&quot; is one of my two favorite horror archetypes (the other being &quot;Frankensteinian galvanic chimera&quot;, the ChroD depiction of which is sadly also dragged down by HFY and mortality porn and is something else I'm working on).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand why you think <b>Promethean</b>'s themes are dragged down when those themes - their desire to be human since they're so inhuman - is what you think all the splats should have as their horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973278#post973278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be more specific, I prefer for it to be that power itself is monstrous, not just what people do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can sympathize with this. I pieced together a short <b>GURPS</b> bout where the characters were witches in Salem who traded their souls to various demons for infernal magic.<br /> <br /> To help with that, and maybe other qualms you have, you might look towards first edition's Mage Chronicler's Guide. There's a campaign seed where all magic is Abyssal or something like that in there. Also, I know a lot of people have mentioned playing Banishers but maybe you'd also be interested in running a game of Scelesti, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:41:33-07:00","id":981400,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to get into another argument about Promethean here, but let's just say that part of what chafes me is that Promethean is so singularly focused on that one goal. And just because I want it to be a game about being a monster doesn't mean I don't think the characters should never be able to come to terms with being a monster. <br /> <br /> And I'm not really interested in playing Banishers or Scelesti. I mean, I would be, but it doesn't help with this problem. Being Bad Wrong Scary Mages doesn't really solve the &quot;mages aren't monstrous enough&quot; issue if there are Good Reasonable Mages Who Are Right running around too. I'd rather change things/emphasis so that all mages are essentially unstable human dynamite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:44:00-07:00","id":981401,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.<br /> <br /> I forgot to mention that someone posted on this forum a homebrew Abyss/Paradox Arcanum. That might interest you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:09:46-07:00","id":981446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981400#post981400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to get into another argument about Promethean here, but let's just say that part of what chafes me is that Promethean is so singularly focused on that one goal. And just because I want it to be a game about being a monster doesn't mean I don't think the characters should never be able to come to terms with being a monster.<br /> <br /> And I'm not really interested in playing Banishers or Scelesti. I mean, I would be, but it doesn't help with this problem. Being Bad Wrong Scary Mages doesn't really solve the &quot;mages aren't monstrous enough&quot; issue if there are Good Reasonable Mages Who Are Right running around too. I'd rather change things/emphasis so that all mages are essentially unstable human dynamite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the presence of Good Reasonable Vampires Who Are Right or Good Reasonable Demons Who Are Right make Vampires or Demons less monstrous? Making all characters of a certain type irredeemably evil (or Bad Wrong Scary) sounds like the opposite of horror. Or fun. Or interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:59:33-07:00","id":981534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981446#post981446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the presence of Good Reasonable Vampires Who Are Right or Good Reasonable Demons Who Are Right make Vampires or Demons less monstrous? Making all characters of a certain type irredeemably evil (or Bad Wrong Scary) sounds like the opposite of horror. Or fun. Or interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you are referring to <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DarknessInducedAudienceApathy\" target=\"_blank\">Darkness Induced Audience Apathy</a>.This a very real phenomenon, and should be avoided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's inevitably going to be a lot of Genius in this project, since I love it it dearly and think it has a lot of incredible ideas, and it pretty much captures what I'm going for.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite parts of Genius, for example...</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to guess, one thing that Mage is missing which Genius has is that Transgression to make progress towards what would be the equivalent of Mage Obsessions is hard wired (via game mechanics)into the game. Make doing horrible things (Atrocities as defined by in my Homebrew, if you're interested in my conversion of the vampire hack to be universally applicable for supernaturals) required to ultimately resolve one of the steps needed to master the ultimate secret of the Obsession. Then you'd have a game where Mages would need to by definition struggle against their urge to completely resolve their Obsession to remain moral; This is much like a &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981446#post981446\">Good Reasonable Vampires Who Are Right or Good Reasonable Demons Who Are Right</a>&quot; whom must fight their natures. This transmutes an implied 'fluff' possible to a 'mechanical' definite. The struggle that is meaningful is what makes stories really good in my opinion, and making the struggle against Obsession a moral struggle adds meaning, and horror, in my opinion. Very Victor Frankenstein and Doctor Jekyll style horror. Mandating that an internal struggle take place and that struggle has mechanics as real as combat doesn't mandate everyone be a &quot;monster&quot;, but does add a monstrous tone to the whole template when compared to mere humans.<br /> <br /> I am a fan that 2 Edition has been taking fluff concepts like Changelings being hunted to be dragged back to Arcadia and freeholds provide protection, or that Vampire is about Personal Horror thus they must care about things outside themselves in their Touchstones, or Werewolves are Predators so they must Hunt.<br /> <br /> I think defining Obsessions as things that require actions no sane/Wise person would do, possibly even Atrocious, darkens the setting in the way you'd like. Really safe, sane, healthy, and Wise things shouldn't be counted as Obsessions anyway, since the connotation of the word and concepts don't mix. Making that explicit with a game system is a logical next step.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=980004#post980004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;how do I make mages feel more monstrous&quot; without implying that the game as it is makes them insufficiently monstrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not perceived your social trespass, of which you seem to be responding to its rebuke, but in general I'd say you've stated your case well and need only acknowledge the strengths of those debating with you as well as their faults to speak fairly. I would say that about most debates/conversations though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-04-2016, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:37:03-07:00","id":981565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981446#post981446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the presence of Good Reasonable Vampires Who Are Right or Good Reasonable Demons Who Are Right make Vampires or Demons less monstrous? Making all characters of a certain type irredeemably evil (or Bad Wrong Scary) sounds like the opposite of horror. Or fun. Or interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I was saying, try again. If you'd been paying more attention, you'd pick up that &quot;monstrous&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; aren't the same thing, and your analogy doesn't work at all, because all vampires and demons, even the relatively &quot;good&quot; ones, are monstrous to some degree. I want all mages to be inherently monstrous to a degree, not just certain Bad Wrong Types. And, I actually think that there's nothing wrong with a premise where the characters are all to some degree Bad Wrong Scary, and have to cope with it and make the most of it. I have said repeatedly how much I dislike the &quot;they're monsters because they could do terrible things&quot; argument. The problem isn't that &quot;good wizards vs evil wizards&quot; doesn't have the potential to be scary, it's that it's not a personal horror setting about being a monster/horror archetype. It's Harry Potter. There's nothing wrong with that, but I've said repeatedly that it's not what I'm looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:41:03-07:00","id":981571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981565#post981565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not what I was saying, try again. If you'd been paying more attention, you'd pick up that &quot;monstrous&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; aren't the same thing, and your analogy doesn't work at all, because all vampires and demons, even the relatively &quot;good&quot; ones, are monstrous to some degree. I want all mages to be inherently monstrous to a degree, not just certain Bad Wrong Types. And, I actually think that there's nothing wrong with a premise where the characters are all to some degree Bad Wrong Scary, and have to cope with it and make the most of it. I have said repeatedly how much I dislike the &quot;they're monsters because they could do terrible things&quot; argument. The problem isn't that &quot;good wizards vs evil wizards&quot; doesn't have the potential to be scary, it's that it's not a personal horror setting about being a monster/horror archetype. It's Harry Potter. There's nothing wrong with that, but I've said repeatedly that it's not what I'm looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you think that Mage as written is Harry Potter then I'm just going to ignore everything you have to say about Mage in the future. And bow out of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:46:00-07:00","id":981574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981571#post981571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, if you think that Mage as written is Harry Potter then I'm just going to ignore everything you have to say about Mage in the future. And bow out of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, it's still a more generous interpretation of it than yours was of my post. &quot;Stories with good guys and bad guys can still be scary if the bad guys are really evil&quot; seems to be what you were saying, and I was pointing out that, true as that may be, it doesn't solve my problem. <br /> <br /> And part of my problem is that the Awakened are a lot closer to being Harry Potter wizards than they are to embodying a recognizable horror archetype. Dungeons and Dragons isn't a personal horror game, even though you can put scary things in it and play characters who are monstrous. <br /> <br /> And here's the thing: you're not reading my post or the source material very well if you can call the Covenants or most Demons good, reasonable, and right. You didn't address the point about inherent monstrosity at all. Demons, no matter how virtuous and well-intentioned they are, are still terribly glorious inhuman automatons who will almost inevitably have to do morally dubious things in order to survive. I'm saying I want to focus on bringing that into Mage. If you think that that makes the game less interesting, maybe ChroD isn't the setting for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-04-2016, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:10:37-07:00","id":981595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981574#post981574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you think that that makes the game less interesting, maybe ChroD isn't the setting for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how you think you own the setting or are some kind of Savior we have all been crying out for.<br /> <br /> Unless this is some weird meta performance art where you are trying to show how a mages obsession can lead to the path of hubris and being ostracized. In which case bravo.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 10-04-2016, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:01:38-07:00","id":981712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981574#post981574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think that that makes the game less interesting, maybe ChroD isn't the setting for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what, I've been trying to avoid getting into these discussions for a long time, but oh buy this one hurt a little to read.<br /> <br /> Why the actual <i>fuck</i> should Chronicles of Darkness not be the setting for them because they prefer to play in a different way than you do? You've been prattling on about your homebrew settings and how they are <i>soooo</i> superior to the canon setting in a fucktonne of threads, and the suggestions you have gotten may have been rather hostile sometimes, but at least people didn't go &quot;maybe ChroD isn't the setting for you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe this annoyed a little bit more because I agree with them actually. I can't see the horror in vampire, neither can I really get the horror in Demon, I play those because I think they're fun, not because of the horror. But I can totally grasp the horror in Mage and I actually find that the concepts that are at work in Mage are the ones that scare me the absolute most of all the games (bar Mummy, because I fucking love Mummy).<br /> <br /> So before you go prancing about how Mage is more like Harry Potter than any kind of horror game, then please consider that this is <i>the exact reason everyone responds to you with hostility</i>. Because you keep talking shit about games we enjoy and play and pour a lot of energy into, and this annoys people a lot, and then you derail threads with long discussions about how Promethean or Mage or whatever new thing that has grapped your fancy this month is a shitty game and is weighed down by specific themes which annoys people even more.<br /> <br /> I mean, I won't criticize you for hacking, given that I've held a game where Promethean actually was about becoming posthuman step by step and transcending mortal limitations, hell I'll even share my notes with you when I'm done updating them to Second Edition, but until then.<br /> <br /> Please, <i>please</i> consider what you say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:11:32-07:00","id":981715,"title":"","content":"This whole..thing seems to have its roots in the gulf between people who spend a lot of time talking about and theorycrafting RPGs to fit a set of narrow, prescriptive definitions (of horror, of ethical ambiguity, etc) versus people who actually play RPGs with human beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:33:42-07:00","id":981734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981715#post981715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole..thing seems to have its roots in the gulf between people who spend a lot of time talking about and theorycrafting RPGs to fit a set of narrow, prescriptive definitions (of horror, of ethical ambiguity, etc) versus people who actually play RPGs with human beings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll admit that I've spent infinitely more time theorycrafting than I've spent playing games.<br /> <br /> I'm just tired of the attitude that there is anything objectively wrong with Mage as written, because Mage is a perfectly functional and well-written game.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can disagree with it on a lot of points, and I do have my disagreements as well, but I don't shout them open for <i>everyone to hear and see so they can know how much I dislike feature X or feature Y</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:13:25-07:00","id":981765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981715#post981715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole..thing seems to have its roots in the gulf between people who spend a lot of time talking about and theorycrafting RPGs to fit a set of narrow, prescriptive definitions (of horror, of ethical ambiguity, etc) versus people who actually play RPGs with human beings.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole..thing seems to have its roots in the gulf between people who spend a lot of time talking about and theorycrafting RPGs to fit a narrow narrative of how the game always &quot;works&quot; while people not thinking the same are &quot;not getting it&quot; versus people who actually play RPGs with human beings and encounter flaws in their game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There i fix that for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981734#post981734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit that I've spent infinitely more time theorycrafting than I've spent playing games.<br /> <br /> I'm just tired of the attitude that there is anything objectively wrong with Mage as written, because Mage is a perfectly functional and well-written game.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you say you that you dont play much and basically armchair DM but follow that with saying that the game, you admit dont play much more, is perfectly functional and well written game? Isnt that incredible contradictory? Dont get me wrong on paper the game seems perfectly fine but paper is the magical element that makes almost anything works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981734#post981734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, you can disagree with it on a lot of points, and I do have my disagreements as well, but I don't shout them open for <i>everyone to hear and see so they can know how much I dislike feature X or feature Y</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why are you in a forum discussing the game then? I mean, if you want to discuss ONLY how good and perfect the game is then you should avoid threads about houserules or ones with titles with negative adjectives. Or join a specific forum that only positive things can be posted and anything negative is censored. This is the kind of places where we should &quot;scream&quot; (not using caps on though) how much we dislike freature X or Y. Thats how we got a second edition btw. Look at Werewolf, people complain about ghost child and devs took it into account and remove them on 2nd.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981400#post981400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm not really interested in playing Banishers or Scelesti. I mean, I would be, but it doesn't help with this problem. Being Bad Wrong Scary Mages doesn't really solve the &quot;mages aren't monstrous enough&quot; issue if there are Good Reasonable Mages Who Are Right running around too. I'd rather change things/emphasis so that all mages are essentially unstable human dynamite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but what about if you hack it so every mage is a banisher on the mechanical sense? Meaning integrity instead of wisdom, wouldnt that make mage inherently monster to themselves?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=973285#post973285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds good. As for the last point, it's because:<br /> <br /> A. &quot;Mad scientist&quot; is one of my two favorite horror archetypes (the other being &quot;Frankensteinian galvanic chimera&quot;, the ChroD depiction of which is sadly also dragged down by HFY and mortality porn and is something else I'm working on).</div> </div> </div> </div>What the hell is mortality porn? I have never played promethean but still, thats a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-04-2016, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:18:19-07:00","id":981771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981712#post981712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but at least people didn't go &amp;quot;maybe ChroD isn't the setting for you.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, a lot of us did tell Gecko &quot;maybe Awakening isn't the game for you&quot;. Which I frankly don't understand why there's so much backlash for this sentiment. It's not meant to be telling the recipient that they aren't allowed to play if they don't enjoy the game in the right way, it's meant as an earnest suggestion that if you seriously dislike the core concepts of the game, it seems like the more intuitive solution would be not to play it.<br /> <br /> Of course, the more we talk about this, the more I become convinced that Gecko <i>does</i> like the core concepts of Mage, but is missing the forest for the trees. If some house rules help her see the forest, then I'm all for helping her with that. But I also want to make sure she doesn't clearcut the whole thing just to get all the trees out of the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:23:54-07:00","id":981775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981765#post981765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the hell is mortality porn? I have never played promethean but still, thats a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Morality porn is Gecko's uncharitable shorthand for everything she dislikes about Promethean. Essentially, she dislikes humanism and since some of the Onyx Path developers are vocal humanists and humanism is a stated theme of Promethean, she tries to marginalize that theme by giving it a stupid sounding label.<br /> <br /> The grain of truth within the label is that Promethean does assume humanity is a desireable state (welcome to CofD, what else is new.) The protagonists' endgame goal is to achieve humanity and second edition has a antagonist group, alchemists, who are humans seeking to transcend humanity, by means which happen to require harming or killing Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-04-2016, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:34:00-07:00","id":981784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981765#post981765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There i fix that for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's set aside the fact that you don't &quot;theorycraft&quot; a game to work as-written and instead cut straight to the operative point:<br /> <br /> Gecko plays with human beings so little that the Changeling 2e game I'm currently running is a direct result of me and two of her other prospective players getting fed up with her spending six months making no progress on setting up the bizarro hybrid 1.5e game she assembled a group for, particularly after it became clear she was more invested in performing thread-necromancy on these very forums for the sake of arguing with Promethean writers than actually working with the players to develop a setting based on their characters like she had said she was going to do.<br /> <br /> One of those players was present for the previous time she let a proposed game die on the vine in this manner. For contrast, we managed to cobble together the basics of a plot and setting and PCs within about two months and spent the remaining time until July tweaking the specifics and refining concepts and meshing schedule, and in the three months since beginning we've done substantial work developing and refocusing the setting and characters.<br /> <br /> Gecko has established herself fairly directly as not having an experiential basis for her issues with any of the games, and for this reason it is ill-advised to try and claim affinity with her just because both of you complain about the games as-written. It's possible (and in fact relatively simple) to voice a concern about the material without burning bridges and making a tremendous goddamn mess of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:42:17-07:00","id":981789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981765#post981765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you say you that you dont play much and basically armchair DM but follow that with saying that the game, you admit dont play much more, is perfectly functional and well written game? Isnt that incredible contradictory? Dont get me wrong on paper the game seems perfectly fine but paper is the magical element that makes almost anything works.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't have an opportunity to play much because I work as a lawyer and have a very, very packed schedule and thus I literally can't play that much and must naturally spend more time considering it than I do playing it. But I do play, I've literally ran the same game of Ascension since <i>1999 </i>dude.<br /> <br /> And I disagree with you, that it looks perfectly fine on paper, I think a lot of the game looks <i>horrible</i> on paper but works great in an actual game (Exhibit A: The entire Time Arcanum.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981765#post981765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why are you in a forum discussing the game then? I mean, if you want to discuss ONLY how good and perfect the game is then you should avoid threads about houserules or ones with titles with negative adjectives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to discuss how awesome a game is. In fact I could spend hours harping on about how <i>fucking shit</i> I think some games are, but I won't because they waste everyone's time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981765#post981765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or join a specific forum that only positive things can be posted and anything negative is censored. This is the kind of places where we should &quot;scream&quot; (not using caps on though) how much we dislike freature X or Y.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I see a difference between screaming at the top of your lungs about how shitty a feature is or how shitty <i>you think</i> a feature is.<br /> <br /> And that &quot;only positive things&quot; remark is almost mildly insulting as it implies that I cannot <i>take</i> looking at criticism of a game I like. This is, in fact wrong, if I couldn't take the criticism, I would have gone back to the DarkFrame thread and homebrewed instead of finding myself in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:51:47-07:00","id":981796,"title":"","content":"I'm not against humanism, I'm against specific aspects of Promethean and against fiction that boils down to &quot;oh my god isn't immortality awful&quot;. That's what mortality porn means. Harry Potter and Highlander are other examples of it. Humanism is a real world philosophy that doesn't really go into immortality, but I primarily agree with what it does deal with. Promethean has very little to do with humanism as a philosophy, and mostly uses it as a shorthand for &quot;if you don't want your character to become human you're PLAYING WRONG&quot;. But &quot;mortality porn&quot; specifically is a very valuable term to describe the bizarre aversion many scifi and fantasy authors have to the concept. Dinosaur Comics has a brilliant strip about this, where T-Rex, my personal hero, basically says that humans tell all these stories about how immortality would be awful because we aren't immortal, and we want to reassure ourselves that we aren't missing anything. I think that's very true in a philosophical and historical sense- humanity has developed a deep and enduring Stockholm syndrome with death and mortality, because it's been inescapable. That becomes a problem, however, now that we're finally reaching an era in which those two might be overcome. <br /> <br /> I'd like to apologize for my comment about &quot;maybe ChroD isn't for you&quot;, because it was unfair. Bigdamnhero's incredibly uncharitable misreading of my post as &quot;everyone should be irredeemably evil&quot; really kind of hit a nerve. <br /> <br /> And that aside, I do think people should be able to play any way they want, but I think systems and settings are set up to facilitate certain kinds of playing, and people playing them should be aware of that. My issue with Mage is that it doesn't do as well capturing the sort of atmosphere and stories that I want out of ChroD. <br /> <br /> Also, speaking of uncharitability: &quot;people who agree with me have friends and social lives but people who disagree with me are shut-ins with no friends&quot;. If you have a gripe with the mechanical implications of my suggestions and their potential impact on the game's playability, by all means use the knowledge you have gained from all the time you've spent Playing With Actual People to tell me when I'm doing something that could make the game unplayable. Are you saying that I'm making the game too depressing and dark for people to enjoy? Plenty of people love Wraith, Changeling, Promethean, and Mummy, and those are all quite a bit darker than I'll probably ever make Mage. Are you saying that mechanics that emphasize the inhumanity of the protagonists hinder its ability to be played and enjoyed? Vampire, Changeling, and Unknown Armies all have important mechanics that measure how divided you are from humanity, and all of those mechanics seem to work quite well for those games. As an aside, if you're ever wondering what I'm going for, I'm asking myself &quot;how do I make this more like Unknown Armies?&quot;. As much as I love playing Unknown Armies, I would still love to having something like that with ChroD's higher power level and and setting. <br /> <br /> Okay, I admit it. I don't really get to play tabletop RPGs much due to numerous personal issues. My primary interest in tabletop RPGs is in setting and philosophy. I'm sorry about that. The primary point of this hack is philosophical and setting based. I'm sorry if you don't think that's a good idea, or that's not how you engage with tabletop games. I'm sorry I'm not approaching this from an &quot;experiential&quot; perspective, but a &quot;I read the book and learned about the setting and I would like to change some parts of it&quot; perspective. Satchel, I didn't know that was you. I'm sorry that I wasn't able to pull off the campaign. Can we...can we get over it? I'm sorry. I was new to things and I promised something I didn't end up delivering. But here's a fun idea! Let's not dredge up irrelevant personal things to argue that people we don't like are antisocial shutins! All of the shit I've been involved in, and I've never dredged up stuff people did from years ago to point at it and say &quot;See! See! Look! This person is a stupid dumb nerd!&quot; You're explicitly telling people that they shouldn't agree with me or support me because apparently I'm some sort of socially-broken, nonfunctional monster. <br /> <br /> Charlaquin, clearcutting in this case would primarily mean removing existing elements that already emphasize the instability and monstrosity of Mage. Which would you consider those to be, and do you think my changes risk breaking them? Things like Obsession and Paradox fill those rolls, and I'm proposing emphasizing both of them and making them even nastier, so that's sort of like planting even more trees? Metaphors are hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-04-2016, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:54:11-07:00","id":981797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981784#post981784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's set aside the fact that you don't &quot;theorycraft&quot; a game to work as-written and instead cut straight to the operative point:</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally i see a fair amount of people just saying the games (in general not just this one or onyxpath one) always work with lots of hanwaving for any concerns other people raise to the point i doubt many of those people game with real people and instead only with fanatism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981784#post981784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gecko has established herself fairly directly as not having an experiential basis for her issues with any of the games, and for this reason it is ill-advised to try and claim affinity with her just because both of you complain about the games as-written. It's possible (and in fact relatively simple) to voice a concern about the material without burning bridges and making a tremendous goddamn mess of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>This i dont know really, dont check the promethean forum nor i care much about the reputation of gecko of what games he run. But you are right actually, i was gonna said that ManusDomine wasnt complaining about geckos manners but that he was going about how he hated people complain on a forum`s game about said game. And while his comment is incredibly hypocritical before that he did post a call on his manners of posting. So yeah, point taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:58:08-07:00","id":981800,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a> default assumption seems to be that if you disagree with them then you must love the game and think it's perfect and hate any negative feedback because of your rabid fan status. You have my condolences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:06:34-07:00","id":981804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981789#post981789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I see a difference between screaming at the top of your lungs about how shitty a feature is or how shitty <i>you think</i> a feature is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this is another matter entirely. Yes there is a less inflamatory way to express that. Like i said i miss when you call on Gecko`s ways of expressing his point and wrote from that. Apologies.<br /> <br /> And no @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\">Mrmdubois</a></b>, that status if just for you. You work very very hard for it and you gain it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-04-2016, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:11:17-07:00","id":981808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981796#post981796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue with Mage is that it doesn't do as well capturing the sort of atmosphere and stories ChroD is meant for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage was the third nWoD game, in design before the first edition nWoD corebook was written.<br /> <br /> Your statement is factually incorrect. CofD is <i>exactly</i> meant for the atmosphere and stories of Mage. Also those of Vampire and Werewolf. Everything else came later.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:13:16-07:00","id":981810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981796#post981796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin, clearcutting in this case would primarily mean removing existing elements that already emphasize the instability and monstrosity of Mage. Which would you consider those to be, and do you think my changes risk breaking them? Things like Obsession and Paradox fill those rolls, and I'm proposing emphasizing both of them and making them even nastier, so that's sort of like planting even more trees? Metaphors are hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must ask again, what would be insufficient for your hack/homebrew to make all mages banisher mechanically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:13:22-07:00","id":981811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981808#post981808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage was the third nWoD game, in design before the first edition nWoD corebook was written.<br /> <br /> Your statement is factually incorrect. CofD is <i>exactly</i> meant for the atmosphere and stories of Mage. Also those of Vampire and Werewolf. Everything else came later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken. I edited that sentence to make it less...bad, because you're right. I can't adjudicate what ChroD is &quot;meant for&quot;, I can only say what I would like it to focus on and what I think it would be best at focusing on.<br /> <br /> And making all Mages Banishers could be interesting, but I do find them interesting antagonists, and you'd kind of lose that by making them the default. Also, as I've said, the more I change, the harder it is for me to use the existing material. If I didn't care about that, I'd just make an entirely new game. But I'm trying to do something that makes it as easy as possible for me to use the existing setting and material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:15:52-07:00","id":981812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981796#post981796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But here's a fun idea! Let's not dredge up irrelevant personal things to argue that people we don't like are antisocial shutins!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to attribute whatever meaning you like to my response to LRS's implicit claim that people who have an issue with the games as-written all hold those views due to personally encountering them in actual play scenarios, but it would be fantastic if you didn't stoop to actually putting words in my mouth.<br /> <br /> The realities of wordcount and nontechnical language mean there are a number of things in RPGs that are conceivably potentially a problem on paper but simply don't come up in execution due to the games being played and arbitrated by groups of ostensibly-cooperative human individuals rather than the hypothetical constructs of one person's nightmare scenario divorced from a collective narrative context.<br /> <br /> \u200bWithout experience in the former scenarios it is substantially easier to fall into the pitfalls on which the latter feed, regardless of how dull or vibrant your social life is or how often or little you go outside. There is no call to manufacture insults to inject into that observation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:19:47-07:00","id":981815,"title":"","content":"&quot;Don't agree with or support this person because they let me down and don't know what they're talking about is&quot; is pretty insulting to begin with. Also, &quot;one person's nightmare scenario&quot;. And I never thought that was what LRS was saying. It was a response to someone literally saying &quot;the only people who would agree with gecko are people who never actually play tabletop games with people&quot;. LRS was saying that they know people who have similar complaints and who have played the game with people. <br /> <br /> And I will reiterate the question I asked in response to the initial &quot;playing games with actual people&quot; jab: what parts of my proposed changes would make the game harder or clunkier to play? What problems do you foresee in gameplay? How could these be addressed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:25:10-07:00","id":981818,"title":"","content":"I'm going to leave the discussion of mortality and trans/humanism be because it's an argument that will never lead to anything productive and tends to end in locked threads and suspensions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981796#post981796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> issue with Mage is that it doesn't do as well capturing the sort of atmosphere and stories ChroD is meant for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's where you're running into friction with people, Gecko. This comment right here presumes that you know what sort of atmosphere and stories ChroD is &quot;meant for&quot; better than the people who actually make ChroD. Mage the Awakening is a story ChroD is meant for, as evidenced by the fact that it's a canon ChroD game. Genius the Transgression (for example) is not, as evidenced by the fact that Onyx Path and White Wolf before it have never expressed any interest in canonizing it, or created a game with similar themes. Suggesting that a ChroD game doesn't fit what ChroD is &quot;meant for&quot; implicitly asserts that your perspective on ChroD is superior to that of its developers. If you don't want to get pushback on these sorts of things, what you should say is that it doesn't do as well capturing the sort of atmosphere and stories <i>you want to use ChroD for</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981796#post981796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin, clearcutting in this case would primarily mean removing existing elements that already emphasize the instability and monstrosity of Mage. Which would you consider those to be, and do you think my changes risk breaking them? Things like Obsession and Paradox fill those rolls, and I'm proposing emphasizing both of them and making them even nastier, so that's sort of like planting even more trees? Metaphors are hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, way back in the first few pages of the thread I made some suggestions for house rules to emphasize aspects of the game that fit in with the themes you want to underline. I think making Paradox harsher would definitely help you, as would adding a bit more of a stick incentive to Obsessions to go along with the carrot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:28:40-07:00","id":981821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981811#post981811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And making all Mages Banishers could be interesting, but I do find them interesting antagonists, and you'd kind of lose that by making them the default. Also, as I've said, the more I change, the harder it is for me to use the existing material. If I didn't care about that, I'd just make an entirely new game. But I'm trying to do something that makes it as easy as possible for me to use the existing setting and material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you are kind in a crossroad here because <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981815#post981815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I will reiterate the question I asked in response to the initial &quot;playing games with actual people&quot; jab: what parts of my proposed changes would make the game harder or clunkier to play? What problems do you foresee in gameplay? How could these be addressed?</div> </div> </div> </div>This runs counter to the above objective of making your hacks as compatible with existing material. If you wanna change the way the antagonist (the seers) or the protagonist faction (&quot;normal&quot; mages) work you gonna have to stick in other &quot;factions&quot; territory a little. If you make mages inherently mounstrous and meshing Genius you will be force to convert new material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:30:09-07:00","id":981824,"title":"","content":"I apologized for that and clarified what I should have said. Though...Demon and Deviant do have a lot of themes in common with Genius. I'm not saying that was deliberate, but I am saying that clearly OP had some interest in telling some of the kinds of stories that Genius tells. And I maintain that Genius would have been a better fit for ChroD, at least as I see it. I'll try to be more diplomatic, but when I disagree with the decisions of the devs, that's because I genuinely believe that their approach wasn't the best one. <br /> <br /> Both of those things are excellent suggestions. The mention of cutting down trees kind of threw me, though, because it sounded like you were warning me about potentially removing parts of the game that help emphasize what I'm going for.<br /> <br /> I'm converting new material and changing things, but what I'm proposing would be massively less disruptive and more compatible than making all Mages Banishers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:30:50-07:00","id":981825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981734#post981734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll admit that I've spent infinitely more time theorycrafting than I've spent playing games.<br /> <br /> I'm just tired of the attitude that there is anything objectively wrong with Mage as written, because Mage is a perfectly functional and well-written game.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can disagree with it on a lot of points, and I do have my disagreements as well, but I don't shout them open for <i>everyone to hear and see so they can know how much I dislike feature X or feature Y</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no, I'm with you - I love Mage, and I love it for all the things Gecko says are problems. I love that it's a game about power and responsibility, about the difficulty of wise choice-making even with good information and good aims, rather than a game of passively sitting there while the GM fiats you to death. I love that players have agency to engage, or not engage, with Hubris and Wisdom loss as they will, and can tell stories about people fighting to hold on to their humanity, people gleefully letting it go to become something else, or people who find some kind of separate peace in between.<br /> <br /> And this is what all the people I've played with have liked, too! They love the freedom of the Arcana, how the game rewards lateral thinking and creative play. At the end of the first session of my newest chronicle, one player, who was new both to Mage and the CoD, saw how another player overcame an obstacle and turned to me, eyes wide. &quot;Wait a minute,&quot; he said, &quot;it's like we can do <i>anything?&quot;</i> I grinned back.<br /> <br /> Every World of Darkness game has, along with horror, some kind of basic elemental appeal to it - a selling point, a reason to play. Yeah, vampires are cursed creatures who suck blood, but they're also sexy and cool and transgressive. They get to do all the stuff teenage you wished you could do. OG Werewolf let you play ultraviolent biker terrorists fucking up the Man. New Demon is like, hey kids, want to be Arnie in Terminator 2 mixed with a Doom cyberdemon and also, for the more RP-inclined, you can trick people into unwise bargains? Even in a mortals game, you can be a brave mystery-solving cop or a crusading journalist or a wily thief.<br /> <br /> These games give you cool shit to do because they're games and they're meant to be played. And this is the element that is missing from so many gaming discussions online, which so often get sidetracked by white room situations, prescriptive definitions (&quot;um excuse me sir this TVTropes link defines horror as blahblahblah&quot;), and the eternal question of how to enforce a certain outcome.<br /> <br /> And I feel like this has been missing since page one. The motivations here seem to be entirely to do with making Mage more exactly like (how the OP perceives) the other CoD games, which...why? Why am I, a hypothetical player sitting down to play a game, supposed to care about someone's sense of persnickety cross-game-line correctitude? That's not a bullet point! Or when Gecko says they don't want even the possibility of positive, helpful mages, and that it's a game about 'delusion' - what kind of appeal is that supposed to hold? &quot;Okay, guys, this game is called Mage, but in my superior version, you play powerless mentally ill people who are constantly subject to GM fiat! Are you scared yet? This is horror!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","user":"jacobkosh","date":". 10-04-2016, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:37:23-07:00","id":981829,"title":"","content":"Okay, guys, this game is called Mage, but in my superior version, you play powerless mentally ill people who are constantly subject to GM fiat! Are you scared yet? This is horror!&quot; That's funny, you pretty much just described Unknown Armies, which is one of the most critically acclaimed RPGs of all time. Do you think Kagematsu is a bad game because you can't play a cyborg in it? To do you think My Life With Master is a bad game because it assumes all the masters are going to be evil? You don't like games about delusion? I'm assuming you're not a fan of Changeling or Don't Rest Your Head, then. <br /> <br /> Saying that I want a game where the GM fiats players to death or where it's impossible to be a helpful Mage is incredibly uncharitable, and if you're that determined to represent what I want in the worst possible way, I'm not sure why you're posting here. I don't particularly care that you find my proposed changes uninteresting or too depressing. No one's making you play them. Gecko's Dream Game or Gecko's Awakening both have plenty of power fantasy material and player empowerment. <br /> <br /> So being able to &quot;do anything&quot; appeals to you and your players. That's fine! I personally think it's much more interesting when the players have limits on their powers that they have to work around, especially in a horror setting. All the coolest &quot;wait, he did what?&quot; moments from fiction that I've seen happened because the characters had limits on what they could do, and I've always felt that Awakening doesn't have nearly as much potential for that as I'd like. I don't want to play a character who can do anything. If you want to, that's fine.<br /> <br /> &quot;stories about people fighting to hold on to their humanity, people gleefully letting it go to become something else, or people who find some kind of separate peace in between.&quot; great! That's what I want to do too! If you think my proposed changes would make that harder to achieve, by all means tell me what I should be doing differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-04-2016, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:41:22-07:00","id":981831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here're some more:<br /> \u2022 Many Mages deliberately try to avoid gaining power, because gaining power inevitably removes the Mage more and more from humanity. Obsessions get stronger, Bans and Banes develop, and ultimately the Mage risks becoming an utterly inhuman Archmaster.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The factions now have more of a resemblance to the Covenants in Vampire- they primarily exist to help Mages justify and survive their cursed state.<br /> <br /> \u2022 More pessimistic Mages prefer the terms &quot;Hollow&quot; or &quot;Open&quot; to &quot;Awakened&quot;, because they more accurately describe what happens. A Mage blows a hole in his soul and desperately fills it with chunks of occult symbols, grabbing onto a watchtower to survive having their mind cast into primordial chaos. The &quot;hollow&quot; nature of Mages is why they're so sensitive to the occult and potent with it: they have &quot;open space&quot; with which to connect directly with the supernatural. Obsessions play into this, too: every Mage feels a deep and aching pain, as if they are missing something precious, and Obsessions are an attempt to fill that hole.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would have to rewrite all the order books or better put make them incompatible with your hack fluffy wise. As the way mage society work in a way is for them to gain more power. And the third point would make banishers redundant or at least ideologically correct. If all mage thinks this banisher status as &quot;heretic murderers&quot; is downgraded to &quot;just murderers&quot; and even then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 The Nimbus grows more powerful as a Mage gains in power as a representation of their growing distance from humanity, acting similarly to the Wake from Leviathan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will recomend resonance rules in, of all places, Las vegas source book for mage ascension page 122. Its has rules for a more &quot;proactive&quot; nimbus that is similar to this. Fair warning as many things from ascension is dependent of DM fiat extremely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=971791#post971791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 It's quite hard to effect powerful supernatural creatures, and some are immune to direct uses of magic entirely. Creativity and problem-solving are key.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> has mention a discarted rule for this somewhere while making mage. I think it was that supernaturals should roll resolve+composue+sup advantage because it would be made them extremely difficult for them to be affected.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:44:16-07:00","id":981837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981829#post981829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and let me guess- that player's name was Albert Einsten, and after he said it everyone on the bus clapped?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to get on people's case about things that they didn't say, it does not help your case to then go on to near-literally say &quot;I bet the example you just outlined wasn't as cool as this thing I care about, and it probably also didn't even happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> Particularly when you went out of your way to <i>edit that second part into your post.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:48:51-07:00","id":981840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981837#post981837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to get on people's case about things that they didn't say, it does not help your case to then go on to near-literally say &amp;quot;I bet the example you just outlined wasn't as cool as this thing I care about, and it probably also didn't even happen.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Particularly when you went out of your way to <i>edit that second part into your post.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Noted and removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:49:40-07:00","id":981841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981829#post981829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you're that determined to represent what I want in the worst possible way, I'm not sure why you're posting here.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lack of self-awareness here is staggering. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:53:44-07:00","id":981844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981841#post981841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The lack of self-awareness here is staggering. </div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about that. I'm just getting kind of frustrated, because after all the fights and arguments, I decided to try to take an honest look at Mage and set aside all the prejudice I had built up against it. I found a lot of stuff that was potentially interesting, so I made an attempt to do something constructive, and like Mage, and find a way to enjoy it and get involved with it, and...well, it turned into people calling me an antisocial shutin. <br /> <br /> I've made it clear what I want. I've made it clear why I want it. I'm sorry if my preferences and opinions differ from yours. I'm trying to be more civil, and accepting, but it's hard when I can't even start a project without constantly having to defend it. If I've mischaracterized anyone's arguments or problems or objections, please tell me and I will acknowledge and apologize for it. Point me to where I've misrepresented things or people in the worst possible way, which I've certainly done, and I will apologize for it and edit the posts in question. <br /> <br /> If there's anything I've said or posted that you object to or want me to edit, just tell me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-04-2016, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:03:49-07:00","id":981853,"title":"","content":"At least for me it seems like you have a tendency to discount any opinion that doesn't align specifically with yours. You got a lot of responders (I'd like to think I'm included) who pointed out various ways to achieve your goals either by using the existing rules or hacking together new ones and there was some debate about whether or not Mage did or didn't address the kind of horror you wanted. Your response to that was to post multiple times that there were two sides and that you couldn't pick one to be on, and basically set yourself up as some kind of arbiter in a pointless and frankly non-existent conflict before you came along in the first place. It's no small wonder you got punched in the face for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:05:22-07:00","id":981856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981844#post981844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...well, it turned into people calling me an antisocial shutin.</div> </div> </div> </div>People can and do have social lives and activity cycles outside the sphere of how they engage with roleplaying games.<br /> <br /> This aspect of human existence is independent from the fact that having experience playing in and running roleplaying games makes it significantly easier to see how those games are supposed to work in execution instead of from a purely hypothetical perspective as a reader and/or homebrewer.<br /> <br /> Nobody called you antisocial. Nobody called you a shutin. Neither of these things are a prerequisite for not having managed to both assemble an interested gaming group and actually run a few sessions of a roleplaying game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:08:54-07:00","id":981858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981853#post981853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least for me it seems like you have a tendency to discount any opinion that doesn't align specifically with yours. You got a lot of responders (I'd like to think I'm included) who pointed out various ways to achieve your goals either by using the existing rules or hacking together new ones and there was some debate about whether or not Mage did or didn't address the kind of horror you wanted. Your response to that was to post multiple times that there were two sides and that you couldn't pick one to be on, and basically set yourself up as some kind of arbiter in a pointless and frankly non-existent conflict before you came along in the first place. It's no small wonder you got punched in the face for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we not compare this to punching? It doesn't serve the purpose of de-escalating the conflict that's been worked up. <br /> <br /> I said I was getting mixed messages because I was. There were people telling me that what I wanted was already there, and there were people telling me that it was a radical change. That's not a misrepresentation, that's what was happening. I didn't say I couldn't pick a side and I didn't try to set myself up as an arbiter. I said that I was aware that the elements I wanted were already there in many ways and I just wanted help on emphasizing them. <br /> <br /> When people gave me suggestions, I thanked them and noted them. I've actually gotten some excellent feedback and ideas. When you've given me useful advice here or on other threads, I've noted it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:10:53-07:00","id":981860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981856#post981856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People can and do have social lives and activity cycles outside the sphere of how they engage with roleplaying games.<br /> <br /> This aspect of human existence is independent from the fact that having experience playing in and running roleplaying games makes it significantly easier to see how those games are supposed to work in execution instead of from a purely hypothetical perspective as a reader and/or homebrewer.<br /> <br /> Nobody called you antisocial. Nobody called you a shutin. Neither of these things are a prerequisite for not having managed to both assemble an interested gaming group and actually run a few sessions of a roleplaying game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that was an exaggeration of what people said and I'm sorry for it. &quot;You obviously haven't played with actual people&quot; is the kind of thing that's hard not to take as an insult. <br /> <br /> And, please acknowledge, when my lack of experience running tabletop roleplaying games was mentioned, I did not deny it, and I specifically asked those with more experience if they had any specific suggestions or examples regarding things I should be taking into consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:14:05-07:00","id":981864,"title":"","content":"Well, something else I've said multiple times is that you have to expect that different people will come up with different interpretations of any given text instead you just keep saying, &quot;Welp, there's two sides here, now I don't know what to do.&quot; Instead of accepting that fact of life and moving forward. Instead of banging your head on the wall of human nature you could attempt to synthesize the useful bits of information that you've gotten into something that works for you. You'd get a lot less flak because it would look more like you're paying attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:14:08-07:00","id":981866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981858#post981858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can we not compare this to punching? It doesn't serve the purpose of de-escalating the conflict that's been worked up. </div> </div> </div> </div>Getting rid of the &quot;fixing&quot; part of your sig might help, it's a little pretentious anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:18:32-07:00","id":981868,"title":"","content":"&quot;accepting that fact of life and moving forward. Instead of banging your head on the wall of human nature you could attempt to synthesize the useful bits of information that you've gotten into something that works for you&quot; Which is literally exactly what I've been doing, as I said. When I made the two sides comment, i acknowledged that both of them had a point, and that I wanted to keep moving forward based on that. I don't really see any headbanging here, since if you took a shot for every time on this thread I've asked some variation of &quot;so, does anyone have any suggestions or feedback?&quot; you'd get alcohol poisoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:21:45-07:00","id":981871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981565#post981565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, I actually think that there's nothing wrong with a premise where the characters are all to some degree Bad Wrong Scary, and have to cope with it and make the most of it. I have said repeatedly how much I dislike the &quot;they're monsters because they could do terrible things&quot; argument. The problem isn't that &quot;good wizards vs evil wizards&quot; doesn't have the potential to be scary, it's that it's not a personal horror setting about being a monster/horror archetype. It's Harry Potter. There's nothing wrong with that, but I've said repeatedly that it's not what I'm looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know in a previous post I said I understand how you might want Mages whose magic is evil, but how would you <i>game</i> with that? If it's so evil and monstrous then why do they cast spells? Like...just don't do it then.<br /> <br /> In my <b>GURPS</b> game, where the magic the PCs used was from an evil source, it was <i>their choice</i> to bargain away their souls. Otherwise what motivates them to cast spells? Because they feel pressured to in a situation that's got out of hand? Isn't that what RAW <b>Mage the Awakening</b> promotes?<br /> <br /> Vampires don't have a choice; they <i>need</i> to drink blood. Werewolves don't have a choice; they <i>need</i> to hunt. If Mages drew power from an evil source, as you imply you want, couldn't they just avoid their horror story by not casting spells? Where's the game in that?<br /> <br /> I'm all for helping you, but people did earlier in the thread and I'm not sure what else you're still looking for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981595#post981595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how you think you own the setting or are some kind of Savior we have all been crying out for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how fair this is when the whole thread has been telling OP that <b>Mage</b> isn't for them.<br /> <br /> Gecko's social graces aside, we all proclaim that <b>CofD</b> is a great toolbox setting but then we all hem and haw when someone wants to use the toolbox and tweak it to something more their taste. I'm not trying to be disingenuous to the other posters in the thread, as yall tried to give advice too, I'm just lamenting what the thread turned into","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:25:19-07:00","id":981875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971461-emphasizing-ambiguity-and-horror-gecko-s-currently-unnamed-awakening?p=981868#post981868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;accepting that fact of life and moving forward. Instead of banging your head on the wall of human nature you could attempt to synthesize the useful bits of information that you've gotten into something that works for you&amp;quot; Which is literally exactly what I've been doing, as I said. When I made the two sides comment, i acknowledged that both of them had a point, and that I wanted to keep moving forward based on that. I don't really see any headbanging here, since if you took a shot for every time on this thread I've asked some variation of &amp;quot;so, does anyone have any suggestions or feedback?&amp;quot; you'd get alcohol poisoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but when brush aside the advice you didn't want to hear and then turn around to ask for more advice.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:27:54-07:00","id":981876,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Alright, folks, this thread has long since stopped being about discussing house rules and started being about carrying out personal arguments. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a>, if you still want help brewing house rules to emphasize certain themes and mood in Mage, you can start a new thread about it. But, I am going to <i>strongly</i> recommend that you frame it in terms of bringing the game more in line with <i>your personal preferences</i>, not with &quot;archetypal horror monsters&quot; or anything to do with what you perceive to be the overall themes of ChroD. Regardless of if you believe your critiques of Mage are &quot;genuine problems&quot; or not, if you phrase it like that you are going to get pushback, and we're going to end up in this exact situation again. If you want people to participate in the discussion in good faith, you need to meet them halfway, and you need to respect that other people have different preferences and not present your own preferences as superior.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:28:53-07:00","id":981877,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> yes, you've asked for help multiple times, but seriously that two sides thing and how it confuses you has been the main point of at least three posts on various occasions. Simply acknowledging that both &quot;sides&quot; (I'm not as convinced as you that there are any sides on that topic) have a point is not actually making progress on using any of the input you've received.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}